{"type":"custom_message","customType":"pi-goal-context-epoch-v1","content":"{\"capabilityGuidance\":[\"Use the main session's currently selected PLAN / ORCHESTRATOR / YOLO mode and available tools. Do not assume unavailable capabilities. Goal evaluation itself cannot mutate through GoalJudge; GoalVerifier is read-only acceptance verification.\"],\"contextEpoch\":0,\"continuationInstruction\":\"Continue implementing the current immutable plan, then stop for GoalJudge and independent GoalVerifier evaluation.\",\"criteria\":[],\"cycle\":0,\"generation\":1,\"loopId\":\"7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866\",\"objective\":\"Implement the referenced plan.\",\"originalPlan\":{\"content\":\"# Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan\\n\\n## Objective\\n\\nClose the nine verified discrepancies remaining after `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`, then reconcile closeout evidence against one exact commit. Preserve county fail-closed behavior, explicit Copilot confirmation, durable audits, fixture honesty, product deferrals, and all existing checks.\\n\\n## Starting point\\n\\n- Audited commit: `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be`\\n- Read first:\\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\\n- Begin with `git status --short`; preserve all user changes.\\n- Never infer Cuyahoga from Ohio, weaken authorization/CAS/idempotency, fabricate provenance, disable hooks, or turn external deferrals into fake functionality.\\n\\n## Work unit 1 — Canonical legacy county reconciliation\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Introduce one canonical resolver/service for watchlist county coverage that receives the property and confirmed county-record provenance.\\n- Resolution order:\\n  1. explicit normalized county;\\n  2. verified confirmed county snapshot as a bounded migration signal;\\n  3. unknown.\\n- Explicit county conflicting with snapshot provenance must fail closed and surface a typed review state.\\n- Add an idempotent persistence/reconciliation operation for county-less legacy records. Do not swallow persistence failures or infer from state/address.\\n- Make property detail, `/api/coverage`, screening inputs, county mutation routes, worker selection, recorded-document routes, and task creation consume the same result.\\n- Apply the canonical coverage guard to recorded-document collection and search-polling reads. Unavailable properties must not expose stale county-specific results as current authoritative data.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Unit matrix: explicit Cuyahoga, planned, unsupported, unknown, legacy confirmed Cuyahoga, and explicit/provenance contradiction.\\n- Emulator integration: reconcile the same legacy property twice; assert stable persisted county and no duplicate tasks/events.\\n- Route contract tests proving property detail, coverage, screening, county records, and recorded documents agree.\\n- Zero-write assertions for unsupported and unknown mutation/enqueue paths.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nEvery surface returns one consistent county capability. No route selects Cuyahoga from state alone, and legacy reconciliation is durable and idempotent.\\n\\n## Work unit 2 — Complete provenance on feed and task surfaces\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Extend the shared provenance presentation contract rather than introducing component-local labels.\\n- Add typed source identity, provider mode, trust/status, confidence, and freshness/as-of fields to feed/task projections where the underlying domain record supplies them.\\n- Map dashboard feed cards and agent-task/property links through the shared contract.\\n- Render explicit unavailable values instead of inferring confidence or freshness.\\n- Preserve honest fixture/demo labels and bounded task language; task completion must not imply records clearance.\\n- If a feed/task has no record-derived source, label it as workflow/system activity rather than inventing provenance.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Table-driven presentation tests for fixture, live, cached, manual, modeled, system/workflow, stale, incomplete, and unavailable values.\\n- Component tests for feed cards and task rows covering source, mode, status, freshness, confidence percentage, and missing-value behavior.\\n- Regression tests preventing fixture links from appearing official and task success from appearing as clearance.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nEvery record-derived feed/task presentation communicates its source and trust limits; workflow-only events are explicitly distinguished from source-backed facts.\\n\\n## Work unit 3 — Make Copilot stale reclaim atomic and redact identifiers\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Replace read-then-unconditional-update reclaim in `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts` with a Firestore transaction/CAS.\\n- Compare execution state, lease timestamp/version, and attempt count before transitioning to `executing`.\\n- Exactly one concurrent caller may acquire an expired execution; losers re-read and return interrupted/replay without dispatch.\\n- Preserve terminal replay and fresh in-flight behavior.\\n- Stop persisting caller-controlled `targetId` and `idempotencyKey` verbatim. Store validated canonical identifiers or keyed hashes sufficient for traceability/idempotency.\\n- Version the execution schema if required and remain backward-compatible.\\n- Document crash boundaries where domain mutation and terminal audit transition cannot be atomic.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Emulator-backed concurrent reclaim test using a barrier: two post-grace confirmations, exactly one domain action and one audit lifecycle.\\n- Failure injection before claim, after claim/before dispatch, and after dispatch/before terminal audit write.\\n- Sequential replay, redaction, stale revision, cross-user, malformed proposal, and audit-unavailable tests.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nConcurrent retries cannot duplicate domain effects, and durable audit records contain only validated or irreversibly transformed identifiers.\\n\\n## Work unit 4 — Finish light-only theme enforcement\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Change `src/app/viewport.ts` to advertise only the approved light color scheme and light theme color.\\n- Remove the active `.dark` production token block and remaining launch-surface `dark:` variants.\\n- Ensure app layout/providers cannot reactivate system dark mode.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Extend regression tests to inspect viewport metadata, production CSS, layout providers, and launch-surface classes.\\n- Assert no dark media theme color, `light dark`, `.dark` token block, or active `dark:` utilities remain in scope.\\n- Browser-check with `prefers-color-scheme: dark`; the product must still render the approved light theme.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nRuntime metadata, CSS, providers, and rendered behavior consistently force the launch light theme.\\n\\n## Work unit 5 — Correct screening column semantics\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Align header and row order to `Property, County, Verdict, As of, Reason, Required checks, Action`.\\n- Preserve capability messaging and disabled-action explanations.\\n- Confirm responsive overflow, semantic associations, focus order, and mobile readability.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Component assertion matching each header to its rendered cell.\\n- Keyboard and mobile test for row selection and action focus order.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nEvery value appears under its correct heading across desktop and mobile.\\n\\n## Work unit 6 — Make local-stack model configuration deterministic\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Define a safe environment rule for `scripts/records-local-stack.sh`: exported variables take precedence; otherwise load only required local-model keys from `.env.local` without evaluating arbitrary shell syntax.\\n- Derive `/v1/models` from the normalized base URL and probe it when configured.\\n- Keep the probe optional for deterministic tests and never use `/health` or port 8090.\\n- Preserve process-owned shutdown behavior.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Shell tests for exported configuration, `.env.local` fallback, precedence, absent configuration, whitespace/quoted values, and malicious/non-model lines not being executed.\\n- Existing unrelated-worker preservation test must continue passing.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nDocumented `.env.local` configuration triggers the correct optional `/v1/models` probe without unsafe environment evaluation.\\n\\n## Work unit 7 — Repair API/runbook documentation and seed evidence\\n\\n### Implementation\\n\\n- Update `src/app/api/test-routes.md` to match actual non-live payload fields and reason unions.\\n- Remove stale claims that `searching` is a stored county-record status; explain that in-flight state comes from valid task/search records.\\n- Reconcile final report and closeout test totals, Prettier status, commands, and commit identity against newly executed evidence.\\n- Commit a reproducible seed-twice integration test that compares document IDs, counts, and representative normalized payload hashes against the Firestore emulator.\\n- Document exact unit, integration, E2E, formatting, route-crawl, seed, and optional local-9B commands.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- Run the seed twice against a reset emulator and assert identical results.\\n- Add documentation/schema contract tests for example response fields and statuses where practical.\\n- Smoke-check every documented safe local command.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nDocumentation matches executable behavior, and seed idempotency is reproducible from committed code.\\n\\n## Work unit 8 — Fill missing browser and integration evidence\\n\\nAdd focused evidence without replacing real behavior with mocks:\\n\\n- Browser test: streamed Copilot proposal card appears before reload and survives reload.\\n- Browser tests: confirmation Tab cycle, Escape behavior, and mobile layout.\\n- Emulator tests: screening create/retry unavailable states produce no run, task, event, action, or projection writes.\\n- Provenance tests for feed, tasks, owner requests/mail, and deep-dive summaries.\\n- Recorded-document read-route tests for unavailable and reconciled legacy county states.\\n- Omnibox accessible-name and Copilot-only behavior test.\\n- Concurrent Copilot reclaim integration test from Work unit 3.\\n\\nKeep live local-9B validation opt-in and serial. Deterministic suites remain network-free.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\n\\nEvery identified evidence gap has a committed automated test or a documented reproducible manual/live rehearsal where automation is inappropriate.\\n\\n## Work unit 9 — Verification and truthful closeout\\n\\nRun from a dependency-complete checkout at one exact commit:\\n\\n1. `git diff --check` and status review.\\n2. LSP diagnostics for every edited source file, including `src/app/globals.css`.\\n3. Type-check.\\n4. ESLint.\\n5. Prettier check, fixing all failures.\\n6. Complete unit suite with exact suite/test/skip counts.\\n7. Complete integration suite serially where required.\\n8. Focused Records Agent Playwright desktop and mobile suites.\\n9. Route crawl and interaction audit.\\n10. Seed-twice emulator verification.\\n11. County contradiction and unavailable zero-write rehearsal.\\n12. Concurrent Copilot reclaim rehearsal.\\n13. Local-stack `.env.local` probe and unrelated-worker preservation tests.\\n14. Optional serial local-9B `/v1/models`, validator, live chat, and streamed-proposal proof with `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`.\\n\\nUpdate both closeout reports with the same commit SHA, exact commands/exits/counts, skipped tests, environment limitations, and intentional deferrals. Never describe unavailable evidence as passed.\\n\\n## Execution order\\n\\n1. County resolver/reconciliation and recorded-document guards.\\n2. Copilot atomic reclaim/redaction.\\n3. Provenance feed/task rollout.\\n4. Theme, screening columns, and local-stack configuration in independent file-ownership lanes.\\n5. Documentation and seed evidence after contracts stabilize.\\n6. Missing browser/integration evidence.\\n7. Full verification and closeout.\\n\\nUse focused agents for independent units. Keep county reconciliation and Copilot transaction work in high-reasoning lanes. Require each implementer to report changed files, exact tests/results, assumptions, and residual risk. Independently verify actual diffs and results before accepting handoffs.\\n\\n## Definition of done\\n\\n- Legacy county records reconcile durably and every route reports the same fail-closed capability.\\n- Feed and task surfaces use the shared provenance contract or explicitly identify workflow-only activity.\\n- Concurrent stale Copilot retries dispatch exactly one action and audit inputs are safely transformed.\\n- Launch runtime is consistently light-only.\\n- Screening columns and focus order are semantically correct.\\n- `.env.local` model configuration triggers a safe optional `/v1/models` probe.\\n- API/runbook documentation and seed status claims match code.\\n- Seed-twice, zero-write, browser, mobile, provenance, and concurrent-reclaim evidence is committed and reproducible.\\n- Full verification passes at one recorded commit, reports agree on exact results, and no actionable audit discrepancy remains.\\n\",\"hash\":\"b1642915c461fd2e2b379dd15404f144542a94533bea65b33b1b9e0fd0a1637a\",\"path\":\"/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md\"},\"schemaVersion\":1,\"verifier\":{\"discrepancies\":[],\"requiredValidation\":[\"Re-run the focused checks required by the acceptance criteria.\"]}}","display":false,"details":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"goal-epoch-8cbf25dccb7474128440e859b673712aa65b8555e0cae0ac096bb839cd2f4a79","hash":"e7d5b00ccc0bbd13463d1416becacbbac41137882afb13091996af62ad22c1af"},"id":"9e7512f9","parentId":"3fd3e8f1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:04:01.913Z"}
