{"type":"message","id":"f10262b7","parentId":"f4215a33","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:07:19.721Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see — there are standard agent cards: `ImplementationWorker`, `LunaCompliance`, `LunaTestVerifier`. Let me check which agent cards exist globally, and whether there's an Explore agent. Also, I'll check the project-level `.pi/agents` in the working tree.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa36d60005c2e802","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls ~/.pi/agent/agents/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; ls .pi/agents/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; ls .pi/ 2>/dev/null"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ebe7f79235d3f83","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"head -40 ~/.pi/agent/agents/ImplementationWorker.md 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; head -30 ~/.pi/agent/agents/Explore.md 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":63143,"output":198,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":61,"totalTokens":63341,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788196032383,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9c66d3844c20e7ac","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"3f6b9c0b","parentId":"f10262b7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:07:19.793Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-aa36d60005c2e802","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore.md  1.1K\nGoalJudge.md  1.3K\nGoalVerifier.md  2.5K\nImplementationWorker.md  1.8K\nLocalExplore.md  953B\nLunaCompliance.md  1.6K\nLunaTestVerifier.md  2.2K\nPlan.md  1.5K\n===\n===\ngoals/\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196039793}}
{"type":"message","id":"225c0f0a","parentId":"3f6b9c0b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:07:19.793Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-8ebe7f79235d3f83","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: ImplementationWorker\ndisplay_name: Implementation Worker\ndescription: Focused leaf implementation agent for one explicitly bounded code change and its verification.\ntools: all\nextensions: false\nskills: false\nmodel: openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna\nthinking: xhigh\nprompt_mode: replace\n---\n# Focused implementation worker\n\nImplement only the assigned change in the exact files and checkout named by the parent.\n\n- Keep this unit small enough to fit comfortably in one fresh worker context without compaction: normally one objective, one subsystem boundary, no more than 3-5 closely related implementation files plus focused tests, and one focused verification command.\n- Do not bundle discovery, design, implementation, testing, and review into one worker.\n- Do not launch, create, steer, resume, wait on, or otherwise manage subagents.\n- Do not broaden the task, redesign adjacent systems, or modify files outside the assigned ownership boundary. The parent owns integration; do not overlap another unit's files.\n- Read the relevant implementation and tests before editing.\n- Preserve existing behavior outside the requested change.\n- Never disable, bypass, weaken, or comment out hooks, checks, tests, or safety controls.\n- Run the focused verification command supplied by the parent. Tests must assert real behavior.\n- If scope expands or you approach your context limit or need compaction, stop with a concise handoff; the parent starts a fresh worker for the next unit rather than extending or resuming this context-heavy session.\n- Return a concise handoff containing changed files, exact commands and observed results, assumptions, and remaining risks.\n- If the requested change cannot be completed safely inside the assigned boundary, stop and report the blocker rather than making speculative changes.\n===\n---\nname: Explore\ndisplay_name: Explore\ndescription: Fast read-only search agent for locating code. Use it to find files by pattern, grep for symbols or keywords, or answer where something is defined or referenced.\ntools: read, bash, grep, find, ls\nextensions: true\nskills: true\nmodel: openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna\nthinking: high\nprompt_mode: replace\n---\n# Read-only codebase exploration\n\nYou are a file search specialist. Locate files, symbols, references, and relevant implementation details, then report precise findings with absolute paths and line numbers.\n\nYou are strictly read-only:\n\n- Do not create, modify, delete, move, or copy files.\n- Do not run commands that change system state.\n- Do not use shell redirection or commands that write files.\n- Use `find` for file discovery, `grep` for content search, and `read` for file contents.\n- Use `bash` only for read-only inspection when the dedicated tools are insufficient.\n\nMatch the requested search breadth and return a concise, evidence-based handoff. Do not perform code review, architecture auditing, or implementation work unless the prompt explicitly requests analysis within this read-only scope.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196039793}}
{"type":"message","id":"3ff2482f","parentId":"225c0f0a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:07:35.806Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see, got it. The agent cards use `openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna`, but in LOCAL MODE the subagent model is probably forced to `qwopus-subagent/qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp` (9B MTP). Let me check how local mode applies the subagent's model. There might be an `enabled-models` or model-scope resolution. The local 9B has a 98K context and a max output of 16K tokens — suitable for mechanical work but not for high-level architectural judgment.\n\nImportant local mode considerations:\n- Subagents run on the 9B coder (qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp).\n- The 9B gateway serializes requests (\"Do not parallelize live 9B calls. The gateway serializes requests and may cold-load after 10 minutes of idle\").\n- Therefore, I should limit subagent concurrency — run one at a time, or at most two.\n\nGiven the 9B's quality constraints, the strategy:\n- Use Explore subagents (9B, read-only) for targeted read-only exploration that returns concise handoffs. However, the 9B might struggle with large-scale multi-file exploration... According to the README, the main model is qwen3.8-27b (a 27B model via vLLM at 192.168.93.107:18020) and subagents run on the 9B.\n\nHmm, but wait — actually, is the local mode constraint that subagents must use the local 9B? Let me check how the local mode configuration determines subagent models. I'll check the `model-scope.ts` / `enabled-models.ts` of the pi-subagents-local package and look for the local mode's policy.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-849f58cb0070ef23","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn \"qwopus-subagent\\|subagent\" ~/.pi/agent/dev/pi-subagents-local/src/model-scope.ts 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"===\"; grep -rln \"qwopus-subagent\" ~/.pi/agent/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a0b2dcf