- Since the 9B gateway serializes requests, run at most 1-2 subagents at a time.\n\nQuality risk: 9B coder for implementation. Mitigations: precise briefs, small scope, parent verification of diffs, running verification commands, parent re-implementation if the handoff is insufficient.\n\nLet me confirm the current HEAD matches the audited commit a9eeff9, then start exploration. Also confirm that the untracked file (the new plan) is the only change.\n\nLet me mark task 1 as in-progress and start exploration. I'll do the exploration in two batches:\n1. Explore agent for WU1 + WU3 (the architecture-heavy units: county resolver consumers, copilot-actions).\n2. Explore agent for WU2, WU4, WU5, WU6, WU7, WU8 (mechanical units).\n\nNo, better: run one at a time to avoid serialization contention, or maybe 2 at a time. Let me first launch the first Explore for the heavy units. But first, let me quickly check the repo layout myself (fast, read-only, cheap) to give the Explore agent precise file paths. Let me find the key files:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nLocal mode confirmed: I'm the 27B main model; subagents run on the local 9B gateway (serialized). Let me anchor on the repo layout, then dispatch focused exploration.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdb01864619357bf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git log --oneline -3 && echo \"===\" && ls src/lib/ | head -40 && echo \"===\" && ls scripts/ && echo \"===\" && ls src/app/ | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":67251,"output":821,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":710,"totalTokens":68072,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788196117284,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9693228249ed730a","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
