{"type":"message","id":"c1ca1d62","parentId":"03ca4173","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:11:48.687Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b60513df112e5be2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Shared helpers for the recorded-documents API routes.\n *\n * Same contract as the county-records routes: authenticated, the property\n * must be in the CALLER's own watchlist (resolved server-side), per-user\n * rate limited, no-store, force-dynamic.\n */\nimport { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport type { StoredCountyRecord } from '@/types/county-records';\nimport { requireWatchedProperty } from '../county-records/shared';\n\nconst NO_STORE = { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } as const;\n\nexport { NO_STORE };\n\nexport type WatchedPropertyAuth = {\n  user: { id: string };\n  property: import('@/types/records-dashboard').WatchlistItem;\n};\n\n/**\n * The canonical 409 for \"the county record changed since you looked at\n * it\" — the caller must reload the property (which re-renders the county\n * AND the recorded state) before retrying.\n */\nexport function countyRecordChangedResponse(\n  current: StoredCountyRecord\n): NextResponse {\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    { error: 'county_record_changed', state: current },\n    { status: 409, headers: NO_STORE }\n  );\n}\n\n/** 404 helper for an unknown search id (or another owner's search). */\nexport function searchNotFoundResponse(): NextResponse {\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    { error: 'Recorded search not found' },\n    { status: 404, headers: NO_STORE }\n  );\n}\n\n/**\n * Authentication wrapper for the recorded-documents routes. (The county\n * shared's `requireWatchedProperty` does the real work; this keeps the\n * routes from importing across feature trees directly.)\n */\nexport async function requireRecordedProperty(\n  request: NextRequest,\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n): Promise<WatchedPropertyAuth | NextResponse> {\n  const auth = await requireWatchedProperty(request, params);\n  return auth;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196308687}}
{"type":"message","id":"399dc5a2","parentId":"c1ca1d62","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:12:00.272Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: `GET .../recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]` (the polling read) has no coverage guard. If the property's coverage degrades after the search was enqueued (e.g., the county record changes to unsupported, or the property's county is changed/erased), this read will return the old search results as the current authoritative data. WU1 demands \"applying the canonical coverage guard to recorded document collection and search polling reads. Unavailable properties must not expose stale county-specific results as current authoritative data.\"\n\nAlso, the \"collection\" read — where is that? `recorded-documents/__tests__/` exists, but there's no route.ts in the recorded-documents directory itself? Wait, the listing showed this:\n\n```\nsrc/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents:\n__tests__/\nsearch/\nsearches/\n```\n\nThere's no route.ts at the recorded-documents root. The \"collection\" (list of recorded documents) is probably read via the deep-dive's property route, or via a dashboard feed/projection. Let me check where recorded documents are collected: `src/lib/recorded-documents/provider.ts`, and the firestore library. Also check the worker's search-polling behavior (the worker polls the provider and writes results). Let me read the recorded-documents firestore library and the worker.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-876b3552e3341920","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"wc -l src/lib/firestore/*.ts src/lib/recorded-documents/*.ts src/lib/agent-worker.ts; echo \"===\"; grep -n \"getRecordedSearchById\\|getLatestRecordedSearch\\|listRecorded\\|recordedDocuments\" src/lib/firestore/recorded-documents.ts | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":88920,"output":384,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWri