{"type":"message","id":"cbfee424","parentId":"d7fc94df","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:12:17.891Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bd100bce7867a221","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"  recordedScenario?: string;\n  /** Injectable for tests; defaults to the configured model (Task 7). */\n  draftText?: (input: OwnerDraftInput) => Promise<ParsedDraft>;\n}\n\ninterface TaskSuccess {\n  eventType: string;\n  record: StoredCountyRecord;\n}\n\nfunction scenarioOption(\n  ctx: WorkerContext\n): { scenario: FixtureScenario } | undefined {\n  return ctx.fixtureScenario ? { scenario: ctx.fixtureScenario } : undefined;\n}\n\n/**\n * Provider selection (M1): registry-driven and county-scoped. The county is\n * verified by `requireLiveCounty` BEFORE any provider call — an unknown or\n * uncovered county never reaches a provider (no address/state fallback).\n */\nfunction providerFor(\n  ctx: WorkerContext,\n  county: CountyIdentity\n): CountyRecordsProvider {\n  return ctx.provider ?? getCountyRecordsProvider(county);\n}\n\n/**\n * M1 run-time re-check: the property's canonical coverage must be `live`\n * NOW (the world may have changed since enqueue), and — when the task\n * input captured a county — it must still match. Fails closed with a\n * blocking error and ZERO county writes.\n */\nasync function requireLiveCounty(\n  item: WatchlistItem,\n  record: StoredCountyRecord | null,\n  expectedCounty: CountyIdentity | null | undefined\n): Promise<LiveCoverage> {\n  const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n    item.county ?? null,\n    record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n  );\n  if (coverage.status !== 'live') {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'unsupported_county',\n      notCoveredPayload(coverage).message\n    );\n  }\n  if (\n    expectedCounty &&\n    normalizeCountyCode(expectedCounty.code) !==\n      normalizeCountyCode(coverage.county.code)\n  ) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'county_changed',\n      'The property\\u2019s county changed since this work was queued. Reload and re-run it.'\n    );\n  }\n  return coverage;\n}\n\n/** Best-effort: persist the county on a legacy item once confirmed. */\nasync function backfillCountyBestEffort(\n  uid: string,\n  item: WatchlistItem,\n  county: CountyIdentity\n): Promise<void> {\n  if (item.county) return;\n  try {\n    await backfillWatchlistCounty(uid, item.id, county);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.warn(\n      `[agent-worker] county backfill failed (non-fatal): ${String(error)}`\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nfunction casOptionsFor(task: AgentTask) {\n  return {\n    actor: 'worker' as const,\n    taskRef: task.taskId,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Re-verify the property still belongs to the owner (identity check) and\n * return the current item (M1 run-time coverage re-checks consume it).\n */\nasync function requireWatchlistProperty(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string\n): Promise<WatchlistItem> {\n  const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n  if (!item) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'property_removed',\n      'The property is no longer in your watchlist; nothing to do.'\n    );\n  }\n  return item;\n}\n\n/**\n * county_resolve: parcel-index lookup + classification (+ auto-confirm on\n * an exact match). Mirrors the old synchronous route, but every write is\n * CAS-checked against the task's captured `expectedRevision` and a stale\n * world surfaces as CountyRecordChangedError (→ blocked, not retried).\n */\nasync function runCountyResolve(\n  task: AgentTask,\n  ctx: WorkerContext\n): Promise<TaskSuccess> {\n  // SAFETY: the county resolve route builds this exact shape at enqueue\n  // time (sanitized: address from the watchlist, no PII, bounded).\n  const input = task.input as unknown as CountyResolveInput;\n  if (!input.address || typeof input.address.state !== 'string') {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'invalid_input',\n      'This task is missing its address; re-run the resolution from the property page.'\n    );\n  }\n  const uid = task.ownerUid;\n  const propertyId = task.propertyId;\n  const item = await requireWatchlistProperty(uid, propertyId);\n  const address = input.address;\n\n  // M1 coverage gate: re-verify county capability at run time (the world\n  // may have changed since enqueue) and require the captured county to\n  // still match. Fails closed — no county writes, no provider call, no\n\n[796 more lines in file. Use offset=410 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196337891}}
{"type":"message","id":"80323935","parentId":"cbfee424","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:12:17.891Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a43aaac21dfbe1f5","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Recorded-document search persistence (Task 5).\n *\n * Search runs live at `users/{uid}/recordedDocumentSearches/{searchId}`.\n * The searchId is DETERMINISTIC — `rdsearch:{propertyId}:r{countyRevision}`\n * — so a repeat request for the same revision returns the existing run\n * (idempotent by construction) and a new county revision starts a new run.\n * Runs are CAS'd on `revision` exactly like the county records: a stale\n * writer can never clobber a newer state.\n *\n * Stored documents are NORMALIZED metadata only (see the types module) —\n * never raw source payloads.\n */\n\nimport { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport { countyRecordRef, normalizeStoredRecord } from './county-records';\nimport {\n  createTaskInTransaction,\n  findTaskByIdempotencyKeyInTransaction,\n  type EnqueueTaskInput,\n} from './agent-tasks';\nimport type { AgentTask } from '@/types/agent-tasks';\nimport type {\n  RecordedSearch,\n  RecordedIndexResult,\n  ProviderIndexOutcome,\n  RecordedSearchStatus,\n  RecordedIndexConfigSet,\n} from '@/types/recorded-documents';\nimport {\n  RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG,\n  getRecordedDocumentsMode,\n} from '@/lib/recorded-documents/config';\n\nconst COL = (uid: string) =>\n  getFirestoreDb()\n    .collection('users')\n    .doc(uid)\n    .collection('recordedDocumentSearches');\n\n/** Deterministic search id: scoped to the property + county revision. */\nexport function recordedSearchIdFor(\n  propertyId: string,\n  countyRecordRevision: number\n): string {\n  return `rdsearch:${propertyId}:r${countyRecordRevision}`;\n}\n\nexport class RecordedSearchError extends Error {\n  constructor(message: string) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = 'RecordedSearchError';\n  }\n}\n\n/** A CAS failure on a search run — carries the CURRENT run. */\nexport class RecordedSearchConflictError extends Error {\n  constructor(\n    message: string,\n    readonly current: RecordedSearch\n  ) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = 'RecordedSearchConflictError';\n  }\n}\n\n/* ── Reads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\nfunction parseSearch(\n  id: string,\n  data: Record<string, unknown> | null | undefined\n): RecordedSearch | null {\n  if (!data) return null;\n  const raw = data as Record<string, unknown>;\n  // SAFETY: indexes are only ever written by completeRecordedSearch, which\n  // maps provider outcomes into the exact RecordedIndexResult shape.\n  const indexResults = Array.isArray(raw.indexes)\n    ? (raw.indexes as unknown as RecordedIndexResult[])\n    : [];\n  return {\n    searchId: id,\n    propertyId: String(raw.propertyId ?? ''),\n    countyRecordRevision: Number(raw.countyRecordRevision ?? 0),\n    status: String(raw.status ?? 'queued') as RecordedSearchStatus,\n    mode: (raw.mode === 'live' ? 'live' : 'fixture') as RecordedSearch['mode'],\n    configVersion: Number(raw.configVersion ?? RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG.version),\n    startedAt: (raw.startedAt as string | null) ?? null,\n    completedAt: (raw.completedAt as string | null) ?? null,\n    indexes: indexResults,\n    documents: Array.isArray(raw.documents)\n      ? (raw.documents as RecordedSearch['documents'])\n      : [],\n    // SAFETY: manualNextSteps are only ever written by this module (strings).\n    manualNextSteps: Array.isArray(raw.manualNextSteps)\n      ? (raw.manualNextSteps as unknown as string[])\n      : [],\n    createdAt: String(raw.createdAt ?? raw.updatedAt ?? ''),\n    revision: Number(raw.revision ?? 0),\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * The LATEST search run for a property (most recent `createdAt`). Null when\n * the property has never been searched.\n */\nexport async function listLatestRecordedSearchesForOwner(\n  ownerUid: string\n): Promise<RecordedSearch[]> {\n  const snap = await COL(ownerUid).get();\n  const latestByProperty = new Map<string, RecordedSearch>();\n  for (const doc of snap.docs) {\n    const search = parseSearch(doc.id, doc.data());\n    if (!search) continue;\n    const current = latestByProperty.get(search.propertyId);\n    if (\n      !current ||\n      search.createdAt.localeCompare(current.createdAt) > 0 ||\n      (search.createdAt === current.createdAt &&\n        search.revision > current.revision)\n    ) {\n      latestByProperty.set(search.propertyId, search);\n    }\n  }\n  return [...latestByProperty.values()];\n}\n\nexport async function getLatestRecordedSearch(\n  ownerUid: string,\n  propertyId: string\n): Promise<RecordedSearch | null> {\n  const snap = await COL(ownerUid)\n    .where('propertyId', '==', propertyId)\n    .orderBy('createdAt', 'desc')\n    .limit(1)\n    .get();\n  if (snap.empty) return null;\n  return parseSearch(snap.docs[0].id, snap.docs[0].data());\n}\n\n/** Read one search by its (deterministic) id. */\nexport async function getRecordedSearchById(\n  ownerUid: string,\n  searchId: string\n): Promise<RecordedSearch | null> {\n  const doc = await COL(ownerUid).doc(searchId).get();\n  return parseSearch(doc.id, doc.data());\n}\n\n/* ── Completion rule ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n/**\n * The top-level completion rule (plan Task 5): `complete` only when EVERY\n * configured required index is `complete` or `not_applicable`. A required\n * index that is `blocked` or `failed` — or that the provider did not\n * report at all — makes the search `search_incomplete`. A run-level error\n * is `failed`. The completion denominator is the versioned config, never\n * the number of documents returned.\n */\nexport function computeTopLevelStatus(\n  outcomes: ProviderIndexOutcome[],\n  config: RecordedIndexConfigSet = RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG,\n  runError: string | null = null\n): RecordedSearchStatus {\n  if (runError) return 'failed';\n  const byId = new Map(outcomes.map((o) => [o.id, o]));\n  for (const cfg of config.indexes) {\n    if (!cfg.required) continue;\n    const outcome = byId.get(cfg.id);\n    if (\n      !outcome ||\n      (outcome.status !== 'complete' && outcome.status !== 'not_applicable')\n    ) {\n      return 'search_incomplete';\n    }\n  }\n  return 'complete';\n}\n\n/**\n * The top-level manual next steps: one per blocked/failed/unreported\n * index, plus the standing manual-review guidance when nothing else applies.\n */\nexport function computeManualNextSteps(\n  outcomes: ProviderIndexOutcome[],\n  config: RecordedIndexConfigSet = RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG\n): string[] {\n  const steps: string[] = [];\n  const byId = new Map(outcomes.map((o) => [o.id, o]));\n  for (const cfg of config.indexes) {\n    const outcome = byId.get(cfg.id);\n    if (!outcome) {\n      steps.push(\n        `${cfg.label}: the source did not report this index — review it manually.`\n      );\n    } else if (\n      (outcome.status === 'blocked' || outcome.status === 'failed') &&\n      outcome.manualNextStep\n    ) {\n      steps.push(`${cfg.label}: ${outcome.manualNextStep}`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (steps.length === 0) {\n    steps.push(\n      'Search the county recorder indices by parcel number and record the results manually.'\n    );\n  }\n  return steps;\n}\n\n/* ── Enqueue seam (routes) ─────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\nexport interface EnqueueRecordedSearchResult {\n  /** True when the county revision the caller saw is stale — no task. */\n  stale: boolean;\n  /** The current county record revision (0 when there is no record). */\n  countyRecordRevision: number;\n  /** True when this call created the search + task (false = existing). */\n  created: boolean;\n  /** The search run (existing or newly created; null when stale). */\n  search: RecordedSearch | null;\n  /** The enqueued (or existing) task; null when stale. */\n  task: AgentTask | null;\n}\n\n/**\n * ONE transaction: read the county record (transactionally), compare its\n * revision to the caller's `expectedRevision` (stale → nothing is created),\n * and, when current, create the deterministic search run (status `queued`)\n * + its idempotently-keyed task. A stale caller can never enqueue work for\n * superseded state — the same one-transaction contract the county seam uses.\n */\nexport async function enqueueRecordedSearchIfCurrent(\n  ownerUid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  expectedCountyRevision: number,\n  now: Date = new Date()\n): Promise<EnqueueRecordedSearchResult> {\n  const searchId = recordedSearchIdFor(propertyId, expectedCountyRevision);\n  const searchDoc = COL(ownerUid).doc(searchId);\n\n  return getFirestoreDb().runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n    // ── ALL READS first (Firestore transactions require read-before-write).\n    // Revision guard: the county record must match what the caller saw.\n    const countyDoc = await tx.get(countyRecordRef(ownerUid, propertyId));\n    const record = countyDoc.exists\n      ? normalizeStoredRecord(countyDoc.data())\n      : null;\n    const currentRev = record?.revision ?? 0;\n\n    // Idempotent search read (doc id == deterministic searchId).\n    const searchSnap = await tx.get(searchDoc);\n    // Idempotent task read (same key: the searchId).\n    const existingTask = await findTaskByIdempotencyKeyInTransaction(\n      tx,\n      ownerUid,\n      searchId\n    );\n\n    if (currentRev !== expectedCountyRevision) {\n      return {\n        stale: true,\n        countyRecordRevision: currentRev,\n        created: false,\n        search: searchSnap.exists\n          ? parseSearch(searchId, searchSnap.data())\n          : null,\n        task: existingTask,\n      };\n    }\n\n    const taskInput: EnqueueTaskInput = {\n      ownerUid,\n      kind: 'recorded_documents_search',\n      propertyId,\n      input: { expectedRevision: currentRev },\n      idempotencyKey: searchId,\n    };\n\n    // ── WRITES: the search run (if new) and the task (if new) commit together.\n    let search: RecordedSearch | null = null;\n    if (searchSnap.exists) {\n      search = parseSearch(searchId, searchSnap.data());\n    } else {\n      // The mode here is a PREDICTION of the active environment; the worker\n      // persisting its own provider's mode at start/completion is\n      // authoritative.\n      const mode = getRecordedDocumentsMode();\n      const createdAt = now.toISOString();\n      tx.set(\n        searchDoc,\n        {\n          propertyId,\n          countyRecordRevision: currentRev,\n          status: 'queued',\n          mode,\n          configVersion: RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG.version,\n          startedAt: null,\n          completedAt: null,\n          indexes: [] as unknown[],\n          documents: [] as unknown[],\n          manualNextSteps: [] as unknown[],\n          createdAt,\n          updatedAt: createdAt,\n          revision: 0,\n        },\n        { merge: true }\n      );\n      search = {\n        searchId,\n        propertyId,\n        countyRecordRevision: currentRev,\n        status: 'queued',\n        mode: getRecordedDocumentsMode(),\n        configVersion: RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG.version,\n        startedAt: null,\n        completedAt: null,\n        indexes: [],\n        documents: [],\n        manualNextSteps: [],\n        createdAt,\n        revision: 0,\n      };\n    }\n\n    const { task, created } = existingTask\n      ? { task: existingTask, created: false }\n      : createTaskInTransaction(tx, taskInput);\n\n    return {\n      stale: false,\n      countyRecordRevision: currentRev,\n      created,\n      search,\n      task,\n    };\n  });\n}\n\n/* ── Worker transitions ────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n/**\n * queued → running (or a RESTART after a lease expiry: running → running).\n * The restart keeps the same run (same deterministic id) and bumps the\n * revision — a crashed worker can never leave a run unrunnable.\n *\n * `mode` (optional): the mode of the provider about to run the search.\n * The enqueue-time value is only a PREDICTION (the worker process decides\n * the real mode); persisting it at start keeps the run's provenance label\n * honest before the long upstream call, and completion remains the\n * authoritative write.\n */\nexport async function startRecordedSearch(\n  ownerUid: string,\n  searchId: string,\n  now: Date = new Date(),\n  mode?: 'fixture' | 'live'\n): Promise<RecordedSearch> {\n  const searchDoc = COL(ownerUid).doc(searchId);\n  return getFirestoreDb().runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n    const existing = await tx.get(searchDoc);\n    if (!existing.exists) {\n      throw new RecordedSearchError(`recorded search not found: ${searchId}`);\n    }\n    const current = parseSearch(searchId, existing.data())!;\n    if (current.status !== 'queued' && current.status !== 'running') {\n      throw new RecordedSearchConflictError(\n        `recorded search is not startable (status: ${current.status})`,\n        current\n      );\n    }\n    const startedAt = now.toISOString();\n    tx.set(\n      searchDoc,\n      {\n        status: 'running',\n        mode: mode ?? current.mode,\n        startedAt,\n        updatedAt: startedAt,\n        revision: current.revision + 1,\n      },\n      { merge: true }\n    );\n    return {\n      ...current,\n      status: 'running',\n      mode: mode ?? current.mode,\n      startedAt,\n      revision: current.revision + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nexport interface CompleteRecordedSearchInput {\n  outcomes: ProviderIndexOutcome[];\n  /** Sanitized run-level error (→ status `failed`) — null otherwise. */\n  runError: string | null;\n  mode: 'fixture' | 'live';\n  /**\n   * Revision the caller observed when it started this run. The completion\n   * only applies if the document is still at that revision — a stale worker\n   * whose lease expired (and whose run was therefore restarted by a fresh\n   * claim) never overwrites the new worker's run (returns null instead).\n   */\n  expectedRevision: number;\n}\n\n/**\n * running → terminal. The top-level status comes from the required-index\n * completion rule (never from the document count). Stale-worker protection\n * is the revision CAS on `input.expectedRevision`: every transition bumps\n * the revision, so a completion that was re-claimed/restarted underneath\n * the caller sees a different revision and is refused (returns null — the\n * new worker owns the run and the task document).\n */\nexport async function completeRecordedSearch(\n  ownerUid: string,\n  searchId: string,\n  input: CompleteRecordedSearchInput,\n  now: Date = new Date()\n): Promise<RecordedSearch | null> {\n  const searchDoc = COL(ownerUid).doc(searchId);\n  return getFirestoreDb().runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n    const existing = await tx.get(searchDoc);\n    if (!existing.exists) {\n      throw new RecordedSearchError(`recorded search not found: ${searchId}`);\n    }\n    const current = parseSearch(searchId, existing.data())!;\n    if (current.revision !== input.expectedRevision) {\n      return null;\n    }\n    if (current.status !== 'running') {\n      throw new RecordedSearchConflictError(\n        `recorded search is not running (status: ${current.status})`,\n        current\n      );\n    }\n\n    const status = computeTopLevelStatus(\n      input.outcomes,\n      undefined,\n      input.runError\n    );\n    const indexes: RecordedIndexResult[] = input.outcomes.map((o) => ({\n      id: o.id,\n      label: o.label,\n      required: o.required,\n      status: o.status,\n      docCount: o.documents.length,\n      blockerReason: o.blockerReason,\n      manualNextStep: o.manualNextStep,\n      fetchedAt: o.fetchedAt,\n    }));\n    const documents = input.outcomes.flatMap((o) => o.documents);\n    const manualNextSteps =\n      status === 'complete'\n        ? []\n        : input.runError\n          ? [`The search failed: ${input.runError}. Run the manual review.`]\n          : computeManualNextSteps(input.outcomes);\n    const completedAt = now.toISOString();\n\n    tx.set(\n      searchDoc,\n      {\n        status,\n        mode: input.mode,\n        // The completion rule was just evaluated against the CURRENT config\n        // version — persist the version that actually produced the status\n        // (the enqueue-time value may predate a deploy).\n        configVersion: RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG.version,\n        startedAt: current.startedAt,\n        completedAt,\n        updatedAt: completedAt,\n        indexes,\n        documents,\n        manualNextSteps,\n        revision: current.revision + 1,\n      },\n      { merge: true }\n    );\n\n    return {\n      ...current,\n      status,\n      mode: input.mode,\n      configVersion: RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG.version,\n      startedAt: current.startedAt,\n      completedAt,\n      indexes,\n      documents,\n      manualNextSteps,\n      revision: current.revision + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196337891}}
{"type":"message","id":"b7f52571","parentId":"80323935","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:12:46.793Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great, now I've got a solid grasp of the recorded-documents subsystem. Key findings:\n\n1. **`backfillCountyBestEffort`** (agent-worker.ts) — exists, but it's *best-effort* (\"if the county is confirmed on a legacy item, persist it once\") — swallows failures with a `console.warn` and continues. WU1 says: \"Add an idempotent persistence/reconciliation operation for county-less legacy records. Persistence failures must not be swallowed.\" So what the plan is asking for is: a dedicated, idempotent reconciliation operation with failure surfacing — not best-effort. Also \"must not infer from state/address\" — the current backfill uses the confirmed record's county (fine, provenance-based).\n\n2. **Worker's `requireLiveCounty`** — uses the canonical resolver with provenance. Good.\n\n3. **Polling read route** (`searches/[searchId]/route.ts`) — no coverage guard. WU1 asks for the guard here: \"Unavailable properties must not expose stale county-specific results as the current authoritative data.\" What exactly does that mean in terms of implementation? When the property's coverage is no longer live (e.g. county changed to unsupported, or the record went unsupported), a poll against an old search should return a typed response indicating the results are stale / no longer authoritative — rather than the bare search JSON. I need to think carefully: the search run is a historical record (the run itself has mode/provenance). The concern: a property whose coverage has degraded (county changed to unsupported, or the record became unsupported) — the UI's polling read returns documents that look current.\n\nDesign decision (needs to be principled, not a hack): attach a `coverage` field (the current canonical coverage) to the search-polling response, so that when `coverage.status !== 'live'` the UI can render \"coverage changed — results no longer authoritative\" — or return a typed envelope: `{ search, coverage, stale: boolean }`. The response shape change needs to be backward-compatible with the UI polling. Let me check how the UI consumes this endpoint (deep-dive recorded documents section). Also, \"recorded document collection\" — the read for the collection of recorded documents — where is that? Probably the deep-dive property detail includes recorded documents via… let me check the property detail route — it returned `{ property, crexi, screening, coverage }` — no recorded documents. So the \"collection\" read is… the UI's `recorded-documents` section probably fetches `/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]` for the latest search. Or there might be a route under `recorded-documents/` root — no, no route.ts there. Let me check what the UI is fetching (search \"recorded-documents\" in the property deep-dive component).\n\nAlso need: `getCountyRecord` from firestore/county-records.ts (for the read path) — no problem.\n\nNext WU3: copilot-actions.ts (940 lines). This is the biggest file. Let me read it now — I need the full picture of the reclaim logic. Read it chunk by chunk, focusing on execution record lifecycle, reclaim, redaction, and where targetId/idempotencyKey are persisted.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9aad5fcc183f52ea","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":330,"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/copilot-actions.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":95519,"output":755,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":692,"totalTokens":96274,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788196337894,"responseId":"chatcmpl-920b6d459f59e097","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"362b5df5","parentId":"b7f52571","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:12:46.831Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9aad5fcc183f52ea","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Copilot action dispatcher (M3) — the ONLY server-side path that\n * executes a confirmed copilot proposal.\n *\n * Contract (design brief: \"no ambiguous clear, ever\" applies to actions\n * too):\n *\n *   - the allowlist is the allowlist: an action type that is not in\n *     COPILOT_ACTION_ALLOWLIST executes NOTHING (unknown types are\n *     rejected before any read or write, and proposal-only types —\n *     manual/offline work — have no server-side action at all);\n *   - the fingerprint binds the proposal the user actually saw: the\n *     confirm request must echo the sha256 of\n *     `${actionType}|${targetId}|${revision}|${summary}` exactly as\n *     computed by `proposalFingerprint` (the same function the\n *     `propose_action` tool stamps onto the streamed card). Any drift —\n *     a reworded summary, a swapped target — is `tampered` and executes\n *     NOTHING;\n *   - ownership, revision, and eligibility are re-checked SERVER-SIDE\n *     at execution time (the proposal payload is model-generated input\n *     and is never trusted);\n *   - a confirmed proposal invokes EXACTLY ONE authorized domain action\n *     through the same seam the dedicated endpoint uses (the county\n *     enqueue, cancelTask/retryTask, or the owner-request route\n *     handlers), each already idempotent/CAS-checked — a duplicate\n *     confirmation finds the world has moved and executes nothing;\n *   - every attempted confirmation gets a DURABLE, owner-scoped,\n *     redacted execution record (copilotActionExecutions), keyed by\n *     the proposal fingerprint, with explicit states: accepted →\n *     executing → succeeded/failed. The record is claimed BEFORE the\n *     domain action runs, so a persistence failure can never produce an\n *     unrecorded successful mutation; a terminal record is replayed on\n *     duplicate confirmations (one confirmation → one action, one\n *     lifecycle); a crash between accepted and succeeded leaves a\n *     non-terminal record that a later retry reclaims and reconciles\n *     (safe because every domain seam is idempotent/CAS-keyed).\n */\nimport { createHash } from 'crypto';\nimport { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport { z } from 'zod';\nimport {\n  getCountyRecord,\n  enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent,\n} from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';\nimport { getWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { cancelTask, retryTask } from '@/lib/firestore/agent-tasks';\nimport {\n  AgentTaskRevisionConflictError,\n  AgentTaskStateError,\n} from '@/types/agent-tasks';\nimport {\n  resolveCountyCoverage,\n  notCoveredPayload,\n} from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';\nimport { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport { getOwnerRequest } from '@/lib/firestore/owner-requests';\nimport { POST as draftOwnerRequest } from '@/app/api/properties/[id]/owner-requests/[requestId]/draft/route';\nimport { POST as sendOwnerRequest } from '@/app/api/properties/[id]/owner-requests/[requestId]/send/route';\nimport type { OwnerRequest } from '@/types/owner-requests';\nimport {\n  COPILOT_ACTION_ALLOWLIST as CANONICAL_ALLOWLIST,\n  COPILOT_PROPOSAL_ONLY as CANONICAL_PROPOSAL_ONLY,\n  COPILOT_ACTION_TYPES as CANONICAL_ACTION_TYPES,\n  type ExecutableCopilotAction as CanonicalExecutable,\n  canonicalProposalString,\n} from '@/lib/copilot-proposal';\n\n// The canonical action-type contract lives in copilot-proposal.ts\n// (isomorphic — the client stream parser and the tool schema source\n// the same lists). These re-exports keep the existing server-side\n// import surface stable.\nexport const COPILOT_ACTION_ALLOWLIST = CANONICAL_ALLOWLIST;\nexport const COPILOT_PROPOSAL_ONLY = CANONICAL_PROPOSAL_ONLY;\nexport const COPILOT_ACTION_TYPES = CANONICAL_ACTION_TYPES;\nexport type ExecutableCopilotAction = CanonicalExecutable;\n\n/** The proposal as it was streamed (what the user saw and confirmed). */\nexport interface CopilotProposal {\n  actionType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  /** The revision the proposal was made against (null when unknown). */\n  revision: number | null;\n  summary: string;\n}\n\n/** Lowercase hex sha256 over an arbitrary string (server-side hasher). */\nexport function sha256Hex(text: string): string {\n  return createHash('sha256').update(text).digest('hex');\n}\n\n/**\n * The tamper-binding fingerprint: sha256 over the canonical proposal\n * string (copilot-proposal.ts is the single source of the format).\n * The `propose_action` tool stamps this onto the streamed card; the\n * confirm request must echo it.\n */\nexport function proposalFingerprint(p: CopilotProposal): string {\n  return sha256Hex(canonicalProposalString(p));\n}\n\nexport interface CopilotExecuteRequest {\n  proposal: CopilotProposal;\n  /** Echoed fingerprint of `proposal` — must match exactly. */\n  fingerprint: string;\n  /**\n   * Caller-stable key (the UI sends the message id). Stored on the\n   * execution record for traceability; the domain idempotency keys are\n   * derived from the proposal itself so retries stay deterministic.\n   */\n  idempotencyKey: string;\n  /** The authenticated HTTP request (used for endpoint delegation). */\n  httpRequest: NextRequest;\n}\n\nexport type CopilotActionCode =\n  | 'executed'\n  | 'not_allowed'\n  | 'tampered'\n  | 'unauthorized'\n  | 'stale'\n  | 'ineligible'\n  | 'interrupted'\n  | 'audit_unavailable'\n  | 'failure';\n\nexport interface CopilotExecuteResult {\n  code: CopilotActionCode;\n  message: string;\n  /** Present for `executed`: which single domain action was invoked. */\n  action?: string;\n}\n\nconst executeRequestSchema = z.object({\n  proposal: z.object({\n    actionType: z.string().min(1).max(64),\n    targetId: z.string().min(1).max(200),\n    revision: z.number().int().nonnegative().nullable().optional(),\n    summary: z.string().min(10).max(500),\n  }),\n  fingerprint: z.string().regex(/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/),\n  idempotencyKey: z.string().min(8).max(200),\n});\n\nexport type ParsedCopilotExecuteRequest = z.infer<\n  typeof executeRequestSchema\n> & {\n  proposal: CopilotProposal;\n};\n\n/**\n * Parse a raw execute body. `revision: undefined` normalizes to\n * `null` (an unknown revision can never CAS, so the dispatcher treats\n * it as stale for actions that require one).\n */\nexport function parseCopilotExecuteRequest(raw: unknown):\n  | {\n      ok: true;\n      value: ParsedCopilotExecuteRequest;\n    }\n  | { ok: false; error: string } {\n  const parsed = executeRequestSchema.safeParse(raw);\n  if (!parsed.success) {\n    return {\n      ok: false,\n      error: parsed.error.issues[0]?.message ?? 'Invalid body',\n    };\n  }\n  return {\n    ok: true,\n    value: {\n      ...parsed.data,\n      proposal: {\n        ...parsed.data.proposal,\n        revision: parsed.data.proposal.revision ?? null,\n      },\n    },\n  };\n}\n\n/** Lifecycle of a durable execution record (see the module header). */\nexport type CopilotActionState =\n  | 'accepted'\n  | 'executing'\n  | 'succeeded'\n  | 'failed';\n\n/**\n * The durable per-confirmation record. Redacted by construction: no\n * parcel addresses, no recipient emails, no draft text — only the\n * action type, target id, fingerprint, the caller key, and outcome\n * phrases.\n */\nexport interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  actionType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  fingerprint: string;\n  idempotencyKey: string;\n  state: CopilotActionState;\n  /** Terminal outcome code (null until the record is terminal). */\n  code: CopilotActionCode | null;\n  /** Redacted outcome message (empty until the record is terminal). */\n  message: string;\n  /** Which domain action ran (null until executed). */\n  action: string | null;\n  acceptedAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n  /** How many times this confirmation has been (re)claimed. */\n  attempts: number;\n}\n\nconst EXECUTIONS_COLLECTION = 'copilotActionExecutions';\n\n/**\n * A non-terminal record younger than this is treated as genuinely\n * in-flight (a concurrent confirmation); older than this it is\n * considered crashed and is reclaimable by a retry. Five minutes covers\n * the slowest domain seam (the mail send) with wide margin.\n */\nexport const IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000;\n\n/**\n * Scrub anything that could be a secret or personal input out of a\n * message before it is persisted: email addresses, URLs, and very long\n * opaque tokens. Outcome messages are fixed phrases by construction,\n * but delegated-route error text is external input and gets scrubbed\n * too.\n */\nexport function redactSensitive(text: string): string {\n  return text\n    .replace(/[a-z0-9._%+-]+@[a-z0-9.-]+\\.[a-z]{2,}/gi, '[redacted-email]')\n    .replace(/https?:\\/\\/\\S+/gi, '[redacted-url]')\n    .replace(/\\S{80,}/g, '[redacted-token]')\n    .slice(0, 500);\n}\n\nfunction nowIso(): string {\n  return new Date().toISOString();\n}\n\nfunction executionDocRef(\n  db: ReturnType<typeof getFirestoreDb>,\n  uid: string,\n  fingerprint: string\n) {\n  return db\n    .collection('users')\n    .doc(uid)\n    .collection(EXECUTIONS_COLLECTION)\n    .doc(fingerprint);\n}\n\n/**\n * A record is \"freshly in-flight\" while it is non-terminal and younger\n * than the grace window. Non-terminal records that are older (or whose\n * timestamp is unusable) are crashed and may be reclaimed by a retry.\n */\nfunction isFreshInFlight(\n  record: CopilotActionExecution,\n  nowMs: number = Date.now()\n): boolean {\n  if (record.state !== 'accepted' && record.state !== 'executing') {\n    return false;\n  }\n  const updated = Date.parse(record.updatedAt ?? '');\n  return !Number.isNaN(updated) && nowMs - updated < IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS;\n}\n\nfunction isTerminal(record: CopilotActionExecution): boolean {\n  return record.state === 'succeeded' || record.state === 'failed';\n}\n\n/** Map a terminal record back to the result a duplicate gets replayed. */\nfunction replayResult(record: CopilotActionExecution): CopilotExecuteResult {\n  const code =\n    record.code ?? (record.state === 'succeeded' ? 'executed' : 'failure');\n  return {\n    code,\n    message: record.message || 'This confirmation was already processed.',\n    action: record.action ?? undefined,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Persist a TERMINAL execution record for a gate-level rejection\n * (allowlist / tamper). Uses the same idempotent claim semantics as\n * the execution path: an existing terminal record is replayed, a fresh\n * in-flight one yields interrupted, everything else becomes terminal\n * with this gate's outcome.\n */\nasync function recordGateOutcome(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  code: CopilotActionCode,\n  message: string\n): Promise<CopilotExecuteResult> {\n  const { proposal, fingerprint, idempotencyKey } = req;\n  const result: CopilotExecuteResult = { code, message };\n  try {\n    const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, fingerprint);\n    const got = await docRef.get();\n    if (got.exists) {\n      const record = got.data() as CopilotActionExecution;\n      if (isTerminal(record)) return replayResult(record);\n      if (isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n        return {\n          code: 'interrupted',\n          message:\n            'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n        };\n      }\n      // Stale non-terminal: settle it with this gate's outcome.\n      await docRef.update({\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        updatedAt: nowIso(),\n      });\n    } else {\n      const t = nowIso();\n      await docRef.create({\n        actionType: proposal.actionType,\n        targetId: proposal.targetId,\n        fingerprint,\n        idempotencyKey,\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        acceptedAt: t,\n\n[611 more lines in file. Use offset=331 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196366831}}
{"type":"message","id":"46436c59","parentId":"362b5df5","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:13:43.451Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm updating the checkpoint notes with what I've discovered. I've confirmed that the canonical resolver already exists in the codebase with a clear precedence order for handling explicit values, provenance, and unknown cases, plus contradiction detection. Now I'm mapping out the gaps in how each consumer is calling this resolver—the property detail endpoint is passing null for provenance when it should be reading the confirmed county record source instead.\n\nThe other consumers like the coverage API, screening, worker, and search route are all correctly passing provenance from the record snapshot, but the polling read route for searches has no coverage guard at all, which is a critical gap. I'm also seeing that there's a best-effort county backfill happening in the worker that swallows failures, and I need to make that an idempotent persistence operation instead. The screening page is another consumer that needs to be aligned with the resolver's output.\n\nFor the copilot-actions module, I'm looking at a 940-line file that manages a state machine for action executions (accepted → executing → succeeded/failed), keyed by fingerprint with a 5-minute grace period for reclaims. The current reclaim logic does a read-then-unconditional update without a compare-and-swap, which creates a race condition I need to fix with a transaction. I'm also seeing that the targetId and idempotencyKey are being persisted verbatim in the record, but the plan calls for storing validated canonical identifiers or keyed hashes instead. The Explore agent is still running in the background, and I have the seed anchor structure and 9B gateway context to work with.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b3e7d641ff5e913","name":"checkpoint_notes","arguments":{"current":"WU1+WU3 investigation (task #1 of 10). Worktree feat/records-agent-launch @ a9eeff9. I (27B parent) am reading the core files directly; a background 9B Explore agent (id 0a64b795-e776-47f) is still running a broad WU1+WU3 survey (was at 86% context — may finish slowly or be abandoned; results are bonus, not blocking). Next: finish reading copilot-actions.ts (offset 331+) and the remaining WU1 consumers, then design and implement WU1 in the parent session.","completed":["Read capabilities.ts in full — canonical resolver resolveCountyCoverage(county, confirmedSourceId) already exists with explicit>provenance>unknown ordering, contradiction detection (recorded, NOT fail-closed), registry-only lookup, notCoveredPayload + screeningCoverageRow projections","Mapped all resolveCountyCoverage consumers with line refs","Read recorded-documents firestore lib in full (495 lines): deterministic searchId rdsearch:{propertyId}:r{rev}, transactional enqueue, CAS revision transitions","Read agent-worker.ts county section: requireLiveCounty run-time re-check (uses provenance), backfillCountyBestEffort exists but swallows failures with console.warn"],"findings":["WU1 GAP 1 (contradiction not fail-closed): resolveCountyCoverage records contradiction but explicit county still WINS routing (returns live for explicit Cuyahoga even when provenance says otherwise). Plan requires: explicit vs snapshot provenance conflict must FAIL CLOSED with a typed review state. Current contradiction is only a message note in notCoveredPayload.","WU1 GAP 2 (property detail ignores provenance): src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts:69 GET and :171 PATCH call resolveCountyCoverage(county, null) — the deep-dive never backfills from the confirmed county record's snapshot provenance. A legacy county-less property with a confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot shows 'unknown' here but 'live' in the worker/search routes. Also src/app/api/coverage/route.ts uses explicit-only BY DESIGN (light projection — but then a legacy property is miscounted as unknown there; plan says all surfaces must agree)","WU1 GAP 3 (polling read unguarded): GET /api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/route.ts returns the raw search JSON with NO coverage guard — an unavailable (non-live) property exposes stale county-specific results as current. No route.ts at recorded-documents/ root; the 'collection' read is this polling endpoint + possibly the deep-dive","WU1 GAP 4 (backfill not durable/idempotent-by-contract): agent-worker.ts backfillCountyBestEffort silently swallows persistence failure (console.warn, continue). Plan: idempotent persistence/reconciliation op, do NOT swallow failures, never infer from state/address. firestore/properties.ts has updateWatchlistItemCounty + backfillWatchlistCounty (need to inspect CAS behavior)","Consistent (not gaps): screening inputs (src/lib/screening/inputs.ts coverageForScreening passes record.snapshot.provenance.sourceId), county mutation routes (confirm/refresh/resolve), recorded-documents search POST gate (passes provenance, 422 notCoveredPayload), worker requireLiveCounty","WU3 STATE (copilot-actions.ts, 940 lines): execution record users/{uid}/copilotActionExecutions/{fingerprint}, states accepted→executing→succeeded/failed, fields {actionType,targetId,fingerprint,idempotencyKey,state,code,message,action,acceptedAt,updatedAt,attempts}, IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS=5min. Reclaim path (recordGateOutcome ~line 290+; execute path not yet read): READ then UNCONDITIONAL docRef.update — NOT a transaction/CAS → two concurrent retries can both see a stale non-terminal record and both transition. recordGateOutcome writes state:'failed' for gate outcomes on a stale record (note: gate outcomes force failed even for tamper/not_allowed)","WU3: targetId (raw, caller-controlled, max 200) and idempotencyKey (raw, 8-200) are persisted VERBATIM in the execution record (seen in recordGateOutcome create branch) — plan: store validated canonical identifiers or keyed hashes instead; redactSensitive() only scrubs message (emails/urls/80+char tokens), not the identifier fields","Schema: CopilotActionExecution has NO schemaVersion field; types/county-records.ts has COUNTY_RECORDS_SCHEMA_VERSION=1 (pattern to follow). Plan: version the execution schema if required, stay backward-compatible","Seed anchor: users/{uid}/demoSeedMeta/anchor; seeder reset-then-write, --fresh-anchor rotates","Demo properties (from prior docs): confirmed Cuyahoga, ambiguous Cuyahoga (2 candidates → confirmation_required), search-in-progress Cuyahoga (confirmed record + search_incomplete run), planned Summit, uncovered Portage, unknown county"],"decisions":["WU1 will be implemented in the PARENT session (high-reasoning per plan): (a) extend CountyCoverage with a typed contradiction/review outcome that fails closed (status 'review' or explicit contradiction ⇒ not-live), (b) property-detail GET+PATCH and /api/coverage consume provenance via the confirmed county record read, (c) polling read route gets the coverage guard envelope, (d) replace best-effort backfill with an idempotent reconcileCounty operation that surfaces failures","WU3 (Copilot CAS reclaim) also parent-session: Firestore runTransaction with read-before-write revision/lease comparison; loser re-reads and returns interrupted/replay","Mechanical units (WU2/WU4/WU5/WU6/WU7) to be delegated to 9B ImplementationWorkers with exact file lists + verification commands, one at a time (serialized gateway)","All tests stay network-free and deterministic; live 9B proofs remain opt-in"],"failed_approaches":["Naive 'just pass provenance everywhere' is NOT sufficient: the contradiction must FAIL CLOSED (plan) — current design intentionally keeps explicit-wins; changing it changes UI banner/worker semantics, so I must design the typed review state deliberately before editing (do not let a 9B subagent make this call)"],"blockers":["None hard; the 9B Explore agent is slow (86% context after 95s) — I stopped depending on it and am reading files directly"],"verification":["curl http://192.168.93.107:8082/v1/models → 200 (9B gateway up)","git status: clean except untracked final-audit-gap-closure plan doc; HEAD a9eeff9"],"next_action":"Read copilot-actions.ts offset 331→end (execute path, reclaim, redaction, finalize) and src/lib/firestore/properties.ts (updateWatchlistItemCounty/backfillWatchlistCounty) to complete the WU1+WU3 picture; then request deeper reasoning and implement WU1."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":99422,"output":1957,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":331,"totalTokens":101379,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788196366834,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8d71815aad705a1e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
