]/route.ts:69 GET and :171 PATCH call resolveCountyCoverage(county, null) — the deep-dive never backfills from the confirmed county record's snapshot provenance. A legacy county-less property with a confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot shows 'unknown' here but 'live' in the worker/search routes. Also src/app/api/coverage/route.ts uses explicit-only BY DESIGN (light projection — but then a legacy property is miscounted as unknown there; plan says all surfaces must agree)","WU1 GAP 3 (polling read unguarded): GET /api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/route.ts returns the raw search JSON with NO coverage guard — an unavailable (non-live) property exposes stale county-specific results as current. No route.ts at recorded-documents/ root; the 'collection' read is this polling endpoint + possibly the deep-dive","WU1 GAP 4 (backfill not durable/idempotent-by-contract): agent-worker.ts backfillCountyBestEffort silently swallows persistence failure (console.warn, continue). Plan: idempotent persistence/reconciliation op, do NOT swallow failures, never infer from state/address. firestore/properties.ts has updateWatchlistItemCounty + backfillWatchlistCounty (need to inspect CAS behavior)","Consistent (not gaps): screening inputs (src/lib/screening/inputs.ts coverageForScreening passes record.snapshot.provenance.sourceId), county mutation routes (confirm/refresh/resolve), recorded-documents search POST gate (passes provenance, 422 notCoveredPayload), worker requireLiveCounty","WU3 STATE (copilot-actions.ts, 940 lines): execution record users/{uid}/copilotActionExecutions/{fingerprint}, states accepted→executing→succeeded/failed, fields {actionType,targetId,fingerprint,idempotencyKey,state,code,message,action,acceptedAt,updatedAt,attempts}, IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS=5min. Reclaim path (recordGateOutcome ~line 290+; execute path not yet read): READ then UNCONDITIONAL docRef.update — NOT a transaction/CAS → two concurrent retries can both see a stale non-terminal record and b