{"type":"message","id":"0aabeefc","parentId":"855c8e9b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:21:11.913Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-acb14c6b33fcbd61","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"157:  provenance: {\n===\nexport interface StoredCountyRecord {\n  schemaVersion: typeof COUNTY_RECORDS_SCHEMA_VERSION;\n  /**\n   * Denormalized owner (the document always lives under `users/{uid}`;\n   * server consumers must never re-derive identity from the path alone).\n   * Backfilled from the path on the first CAS write of a legacy doc.\n   */\n  ownerUid: string;\n  /**\n   * Monotonic optimistic-concurrency revision. Legacy (pre-CAS) documents\n   * carry no field and READ as 0; the first CAS transition bumps them to 1.\n   * Every committed transition (success or failure) bumps by exactly 1,\n   * atomically with the record write and its canonical outbox event.\n   */\n  revision: number;\n  /** When this record was first stored (ISO). Legacy: backfilled from `updatedAt`. */\n  createdAt: string;\n  status: StoredCountyRecordStatus;\n  /** The normalized address last resolved (drift detection). */\n  resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress | null;\n  /** Pending candidates (only in confirmation_required). Bounded. */\n  candidates: StoredCandidate[] | null;\n  /** Last successfully retrieved snapshot (last-known-good). */\n  snapshot: CountyParcelSnapshot | null;\n  unsupportedReason: 'state_not_supported' | 'provider_unsupported' | null;\n  lastRefresh: {\n    at: string;\n    ok: boolean;\n    error: CountyRecordsErrorInfo | null;\n  } | null;\n  updatedAt: string;\n}\n===\n44:export interface WatchlistItem {\n45-  /** Stable Crexi property id (the document id). */\n46-  id: string;\n47-  address: string | null;\n48-  city: string | null;\n49-  state: string | null;\n50-  zipCode: string | null;\n51-  /**\n52-   * Canonical county identity (M1): the ONLY routing key for county\n53-   * coverage. `null` (or absent on legacy docs) means UNKNOWN — never\n54-   * inferred from state/address and never defaulted to a covered county.\n55-   */\n56-  county: CountyIdentity | null;\n57-  propertyType: string | null;\n58-  title: string | null;\n59-  /** Crexi's own listing id, for reference. */\n60-  crexiId: string | null;\n61-  listingUrl: string | null;\n62-  thumbnailUrl: string | null;\n63-  /** Captured financial snapshot (null where the listing omits it). */\n64-  price: number | null;\n65-  sizeSqFt: number | null;\n66-  pricePerSqFt: number | null;\n67-  /** ISO timestamp of the snapshot above. */\n68-  capturedAt: string;\n69-  verdict: WatchlistVerdict | null;\n70-  addedAt: string;\n71-}\n72-\n73-/** The client-safe subset of WatchlistItem a search result carries. */\n74-export interface WatchlistSnapshot {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196871913}}
{"type":"message","id":"726db904","parentId":"0aabeefc","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:21:11.913Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b6934edd3e4b445d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      raw = await request.json();\n    } catch {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: 'objectId must be a positive integer' },\n        { status: 400, headers: NO_STORE }\n      );\n    }\n    const parsed = bodySchema.safeParse(raw);\n    if (!parsed.success) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        {\n          error:\n            'objectId must be a positive integer and expectedRevision a non-negative integer',\n        },\n        { status: 400, headers: NO_STORE }\n      );\n    }\n    const { objectId, expectedRevision } = parsed.data;\n\n    const record = await getCountyRecord(user.id, property.id);\n    if (!record) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: 'No county record for this property' },\n        { status: 404, headers: NO_STORE }\n      );\n    }\n\n    // M1 coverage gate: confirmation work only runs for a live county. A\n    // legacy confirmed parcel still passes via confirmed-source backfill\n    // (the snapshot's source proves the county); anything else fails\n    // closed with zero writes.\n    const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n      property.county ?? null,\n      record.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n    );\n    if (coverage.status !== 'live') {\n      return NextResponse.json(notCoveredPayload(coverage), {\n        status: 422,\n        headers: NO_STORE,\n      });\n    }\n\n    if (record.revision !== expectedRevision) {\n      return countyRecordChangedResponse(record);\n    }\n    if (record.status !== 'confirmation_required' || !record.resolvedAddress) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: 'No candidates pending confirmation' },\n        { status: 409, headers: NO_STORE }\n      );\n    }\n    if (\n      !record.candidates?.some((candidate) => candidate.objectId === objectId)\n    ) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: 'Parcel is not among the stored candidates' },\n        { status: 409, headers: NO_STORE }\n      );\n    }\n\n    const result = await enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(\n      user.id,\n      property.id,\n      'county_confirm',\n      {\n        expectedRevision,\n        objectId,\n        address: record.resolvedAddress,\n        county: coverage.county,\n      },\n      expectedRevision\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788196871913}}
{"type":"message","id":"621f107e","parentId":"726db904","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:21:36.120Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting point: the synchronous confirm route says \"legacy confirmed parcels still pass via confirmed-source backfill (the snapshot's source proves the county).\" But wait — a record with status `confirmation_required` typically has no snapshot yet (snapshot is set at confirm time). For a `confirmation_required` record, `record.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId` is null (no snapshot yet) — so the provenance fallback only helps for records that have a snapshot (confirmed / failed refresh). Hmm — actually, for a record in `confirmation_required` state derived from a resolution search against a county source… the resolution search itself knows the source. Does StoredCountyRecord save the source of the resolution? The `provenance` field is on `snapshot` (CountyParcelSnapshot). In `confirmation_required`, the snapshot is null. So the source of the candidate list is… let me check: does the `resolve` flow save the source ID somewhere on the record (e.g., `resolvedSourceId`)? Let me check the types and the resolve route. If not, then a legacy (county-less) property in the `confirmation_required` state resolves to coverage `unknown` → the confirm route returns 422 — even though the resolution was performed against the Cuyahoga source. This is another potential gap: for a county-less property with a `confirmation_required` record, the only provenance is… hmm, wait — how does a county-less property even get a county record in the first place? The resolve route's gate: let me check the resolve route — it also gates on coverage (line 74). If the property is county-less (unknown), the resolve gate fails (not live) → no resolve is ever enqueued. So the only way for a county-less legacy property to have a confirmed snapshot is if it was created before M1 (legacy data) — which is exactly the migration case: the old records that had county work done before the county-identity field existed. In that case, the record has a confirmed snapshot with provenance sourceId. So: legacy county-less property + confirmed snapshot (cuyahoga) → provenance backfill works (the record has a snapshot). The `confirmation_required` case for a county-less property can't arise in the M1 flow (the gate blocks it), but in legacy data it could exist… in that case the record has no snapshot → no provenance → unknown → 422. This is fail-closed and honest — acceptable (a human sets the county explicitly).\n\nSo, to check the legacy migration case, let me check which status the seed's \"confirmed\" property has, and check whether the seeder creates any county-less legacy property with a confirmed snapshot. From the final report: \"6 properties cover all screen categories: confirmed / ambiguous (confirmation required) / search-in-progress Cuyahoga fixtures, planned Summit, uncovered Portage, unknown county.\" The \"unknown county\" one — does it have a county record? Probably not (unknown). Let me check whether there's any seeded property without a county but with a confirmed snapshot (the WU1 test case \"legacy confirmed Cuyahoga\"). The plan's unit test matrix mentions \"legacy confirmed Cuyahoga.\" If the seed doesn't have one, then the emulator integration test (WU1) must create such a property (via a test helper) and then verify the reconciliation.\n\nLet me check the seed file for the county fields and the county records of the 6 properties.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2fa7ad98809d33e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"county\" scripts/seed-records-demo.ts | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":127221,"output":770,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":725,"totalTokens":127991,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timest