{"type":"message","id":"308cb298","parentId":"c748c65f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:26:22.138Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I ended up removing the definition of the `note` variable, but the remaining branches (planned, not_covered, unknown) are still referencing it. Originally, `note` was appending a note about the contradiction to all blocked branches. Now that contradiction ⇒ review has become a dedicated branch, the other branches will never have a contradiction (a contradiction triggers review first)... wait, is that really true? In the new resolveCountyCoverage, if contradiction is non-null → it becomes a review branch. Therefore, in planned/not_covered/unknown, contradiction will always be null. So it's fine to remove `note` from those branches — I just need to delete the `, note` reference. Let me check the current text around lines 400–435.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cae2ef4f253d394","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":55,"offset":385,"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":140569,"output":239,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":159,"totalTokens":140808,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788197173344,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8868c6c4b258a32c","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
