{"type":"compaction","id":"63c111b6","parentId":"643bc749","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:31:54.010Z","summary":"\n\n## Goal\n- Implement the immutable plan **Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan** from `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md` / untracked `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`.\n- Close the nine verified audit gaps, reconcile closeout evidence against one exact commit, then stop for `GoalJudge` and independent read-only `GoalVerifier` evaluation.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use the main session’s currently selected PLAN / ORCHESTRATOR / YOLO mode and available tools; do not assume unavailable capabilities.\n- `GoalJudge` cannot mutate the goal; `GoalVerifier` is read-only acceptance verification.\n- Preserve all user changes and never disable/bypass pre-commit hooks, tests, authorization checks, provider gates, CAS, or idempotency controls.\n- Preserve county fail-closed behavior, explicit Copilot confirmation, durable audits, fixture honesty, product deferrals, and all existing checks.\n- Never infer Cuyahoga from Ohio/state/address, fabricate provenance, or turn external deferrals into fake functionality.\n- Work in `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch` on branch `feat/records-agent-launch`, audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` / short `a9eeff9`.\n- Deterministic suites must remain network-free; local-9B validation is opt-in, serial, and uses `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Ran `git status --short --branch`, `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git branch --show-current`, `git remote -v`.\n- [x] Confirmed repo state:\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard 450773f [main]`\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch a9eeff9 [feat/records-agent-launch]`\n  - Untracked: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`\n  - Remote: `origin git@github.com:Brickspect/dashboard.git`\n- [x] Read prior material:\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\n- [x] Checked `todo` list: **No tasks**.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Begin implementation of the final audit-gap closure plan, starting with **Work unit 1 — Canonical legacy county reconciliation**. No source changes have been made yet.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Work in the existing records-agent worktree**: Continue on `feat/records-agent-launch` rather than starting a new branch, because the audit plan explicitly anchors to audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` and existing closeout docs.\n- **Follow the plan’s execution order**: county resolver/reconciliation first, then Copilot atomic reclaim/redaction, provenance rollout, theme/screening/local-stack lanes, documentation/seed evidence, missing browser/integration evidence, and full verification.\n- **Treat prior closeout as context, not proof**: New claims must come from newly executed checks against a single recorded commit; unavailable evidence must be reported as unavailable.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Inspect and confirm the current untracked plan file `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md` and reconcile it with the immutable `original-plan.md` snapshot.\n2. Implement **Work unit 1**:\n   - Create one canonical county-coverage resolver/service receiving property plus confirmed county-record provenance.\n   - Resolution order: explicit normalized county → verified confirmed county snapshot as bounded migration signal → unknown.\n   - Fail closed and surface a typed review state when explicit county conflicts with snapshot provenance.\n   - Add idempotent persistence/reconciliation for county-less legacy records without swallowing failures or inferring from state/address.\n   - Make property detail, `/api/coverage`, screening inputs, county mutation routes, worker selection, recorded-document routes, and task creation consume the same canonical result.\n   - Apply the canonical coverage guard to recorded-document collection and search-polling reads.\n   - Add unit matrix, emulator duplicate-reconciliation, route contract, and zero-write tests.\n3. Implement **Work unit 3**:\n   - Replace read-then-unconditional-update reclaim in `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts` with a Firestore transaction/CAS.\n   - Compare execution state, lease timestamp/version, and attempt count before transitioning to `executing`.\n   - Ensure exactly one concurrent caller acquires an expired execution; losers return interrupted/replay without dispatch.\n   - Stop persisting caller-controlled `targetId` and `idempotencyKey` verbatim; store validated canonical identifiers or keyed hashes.\n   - Add concurrent reclaim, failure-injection, replay, redaction, stale-revision, cross-user, malformed-proposal, and audit-unavailable tests.\n4. Implement **Work unit 2**:\n   - Extend the shared provenance presentation contract for feed and task surfaces.\n   - Add typed source identity, provider mode, trust/status, confidence, freshness/as-of fields where supported by domain records.\n   - Map dashboard feed cards and agent-task/property links through the shared contract.\n   - Render explicit unavailable values; label workflow/system-only activity rather than inventing provenance.\n   - Add table-driven and component regression tests.\n5. Implement **Work units 4–6**:\n   - `src/app/viewport.ts`: advertise only approved light color scheme/theme; remove active `.dark` production token block and launch-surface `dark:` variants; prevent layout/providers from reactivating system dark mode.\n   - Screening columns: align header/row order to `Property, County, Verdict, As of, Reason, Required checks, Action`; verify responsive/focus/mobile behavior.\n   - `scripts/records-local-stack.sh`: deterministic local-model config, exported variables take precedence, safe `.env.local` fallback, derive `/v1/models` from normalized base URL, optional probe only, preserve process-owned shutdown and unrelated-worker preservation.\n6. Implement **Work unit 7**:\n   - Update `src/app/api/test-routes.md` to actual non-live payload fields/reason unions.\n   - Remove stale claim that `searching` is a stored county-record status.\n   - Reconcile final report/closeout totals, commands, Prettier status, and commit identity against newly executed evidence.\n   - Commit reproducible seed-twice integration test comparing document IDs, counts, and representative normalized payload hashes against Firestore emulator.\n7. Implement **Work unit 8**:\n   - Add missing browser and integration evidence: streamed Copilot proposal card persistence, confirmation Tab/Escape/mobile behavior, screening unavailable zero-write paths, provenance tests for feed/tasks/owner requests/mail/deep-dive summaries, recorded-document read-route unavailable/reconciled states, omnibox accessible-name/Copilot-only behavior, and concurrent Copilot reclaim integration.\n8. Run **Work unit 9** full verification at one exact commit:\n   - `git diff --check`\n   - LSP diagnostics for edited files including `src/app/globals.css`\n   - type-check\n   - ESLint\n   - Prettier check and fixes\n   - complete unit suite with exact counts\n   - serial integration suite where required\n   - focused Records Agent Playwright desktop/mobile suites\n   - route crawl and interaction audit\n   - seed-twice emulator verification\n   - county contradiction and unavailable zero-write rehearsal\n   - concurrent Copilot reclaim rehearsal\n   - local-stack `.env.local` probe and unrelated-worker preservation tests\n   - optional serial local-9B `/v1/models`, validator, live chat, and streamed-proposal proof with `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`\n9. Update both closeout reports with the same commit SHA, exact commands/exits/counts, skipped tests, environment limitations, and intentional deferrals, then stop for `GoalJudge` and `GoalVerifier`.\n\n## Critical Context\n- `loopId`: `7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866`\n- `originalPlan` path: `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md`\n- `originalPlan` hash: `b1642915c461fd2e2b379dd15404f144542a94533bea65b33b1b9e0fd0a1637a`\n- Audited commit: `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be`\n- Current branch/worktree:\n  - branch `feat/records-agent-launch`\n  - worktree `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch`\n  - main checkout `~/brickspect/dashboard` on `main` at `450773f`\n- Key files:\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\n  - `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts`\n  - `src/app/viewport.ts`\n  - `scripts/records-local-stack.sh`\n  - `src/app/api/test-routes.md`\n- Prior closeout commits referenced in `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`:\n  - `346765c`, `ae7c143`, `3b273a6`, `760710c`, `7654baa`, `ae6f77a`, `1484465`, `1b2976e`, `1a4301f`\n- Local 9B provider contract:\n  - `AI_PROVIDER=local`\n  - `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`\n  - `LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://192.168.93.107:8082/v1`\n  - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=none`\n  - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp`\n  - `LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=300000`\n  - Probe only `GET http://192.168.93.107:8082/v1/models`; never probe `/health`.\n- `verifier.requiredValidation`: “Re-run the focused checks required by the acceptance criteria.”\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n\n\n## Original Request\nThe user typed \"icontinue\" (typo for \"continue\"), asking the assistant to proceed with executing the **Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan** — a 9-work-unit plan to close remaining audit discrepancies in a Next.js + Firestore codebase. The plan file is `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md` (untracked). The work happens in worktree `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch` on branch `feat/records-agent-launch` at commit `a9eeff9` (clean tree).\n\n## Early Progress\n- **Environment/local-mode confirmation**: Main model is `qwen38-main/qwen3.8-27b` (vLLM `192.168.93.107:18020`); subagents must use local 9B `qwopus-subagent/qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp` (gateway `192.168.93.107:8082`, **serialized** — no parallel 9B calls; 98k ctx, 16k max output). Verified gateway reachable via `ctx_execute` curl.\n- **Todo list created** (10 items): explore + WUs 1–9.\n- **Background Explore subagent** (id `0a64b795-e776-47f`) launched for WU1+WU3 survey but ran slowly (86% context after ~95s); assistant stopped depending on it and read files directly.\n- **WU1 (county coverage) gaps identified**:\n  1. `resolveCountyCoverage` records contradiction but explicit county still wins routing — plan requires **fail-closed typed review state**.\n  2. Property detail GET/PATCH (`src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts:69,:171`) passes `null` for provenance → legacy county-less property shows `unknown` here but `live` in worker/search routes.\n  3. `/api/coverage` uses explicit-only by design (light projection) — plan says all surfaces must agree.\n  4. Recorded-documents read paths (`GET /recorded-documents` root and `GET /searches/[searchId]` polling) have **no coverage guard** — stale county-specific results exposed as current.\n  5. `backfillCountyBestEffort` (agent-worker.ts) swallows persistence failures with `console.warn`; `backfillWatchlistCounty` (firestore/properties.ts) is **non-atomic** read-then-set (race with concurrent explicit PATCH). Plan demands idempotent transactional reconciliation that never swallows failures or infers from state/address.\n  6. Sync confirm route (`confirm/route.ts`) does NOT call backfill — only worker does (3 sites).\n- **WU3 (Copilot CAS reclaim) gaps identified**:\n  1. `claimExecution` does `docRef.get()` **outside** any transaction → unconditional `docRef.update` → two concurrent retries both reclaim and both dispatch. Fix: `runTransaction` with in-tx basis verification (state+updatedAt+attempts).\n  2. `recordGateOutcome` has the same read-then-unconditional-update race.\n  3. `targetId` and `idempotencyKey` (caller-controlled) are persisted **verbatim** in the execution record. Plan: store keyed hashes.\n  4. No `schemaVersion` on `CopilotActionExecution` docs.\n  5. Records are **audit-only** (no reader in src/ outside copilot-actions.ts itself) → low blast radius for hash transformation.\n- **WU1/WU3 implementation decisions** (parent session, high-reasoning):\n  - WU1: extend `CountyCoverage` with fail-closed contradiction; make property-detail/coverage consumers pass provenance; add coverage guard envelope to recorded-documents reads (additive fields, backward-compatible with `isSearchResponse`); replace best-effort backfill with transactional `reconcileWatchlistCounty`.\n  - WU3: `runTransaction`-based claim + gate-outcome with in-tx CAS; keyed-hash redaction at all write sites; `schemaVersion: 2`; document crash boundary.\n- **Mechanical units** (WU2 provenance, WU4 theme, WU5 screening columns, WU6 local-stack script, WU7 docs) to be delegated to 9B `ImplementationWorker` subagents one at a time (serialized gateway), with exact file lists + verification commands.\n- **3 checkpoint notes** committed to `~/.pi/agent/notes/9b3f771d-.../NOTES.md` (generations 1–3) capturing all findings, decisions, blockers, and next actions.\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- **Next action** (from checkpoint gen 3): call `request_deeper_reasoning` for the WU1 fail-closed contradiction design (changes route status semantics across ~6 surfaces), then implement WU1 in the parent session. WU1 files to modify: `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts`, `src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts`, `src/app/api/coverage/route.ts`, `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/route.ts` + `searches/[searchId]/route.ts`, `src/lib/firestore/properties.ts` (new transactional reconcile), `src/lib/agent-worker.ts` (call sites), `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/confirm/route.ts`, + unit tests.\n- **Key type definitions**: `CountyCoverage` has `status: 'live'|'planned'|'not_covered'|'unknown'` + optional `contradiction` + `county` + `message`; `RecordedSearchResponse = RecordedSearch | RecordedSearchNotFound`; `CopilotActionExecution` has fields `{actionType, targetId, fingerprint, idempotencyKey, state, code, message, action, acceptedAt, updatedAt, attempts}`.\n- **Existing test harness**: `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts` has a fake-Firestore harness that special-cases `copilotActionExecutions` (line ~99); will need `runTransaction` support for concurrent-reclaim tests. `CasOptions.delayBeforeCommitMs` pattern already exists in `firestore/county-records.ts` for transaction-barrier testing.\n- **UI backward-compat constraint**: `isSearchResponse` in `recorded-documents-section.tsx` checks only `'status' in value && SEARCH_STATUSES.has(status)` — additive fields (coverage, authoritative) keep it passing without UI changes.\n- **9B subagent quality risk**: 9B coder may struggle with complex units; mitigation is small scope (≤3–5 files), exact briefs, parent verification of every diff. If a worker fails, parent implements directly.\n- **WU8/WU9** (missing browser/integration evidence, full verification + closeout) come last; live 9B proofs are opt-in/serial; deterministic suites must remain network-free. Prettier has pre-existing repo-wide drift (44 files on branch, 109 on main) — WU9 must reconcile honestly.\n\n<read-files>\n/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/dev/pi-subagents-local/README.md\n/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/copilot/proposals/execute/route.ts\n/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/rec