{"type":"message","id":"05e4af8b","parentId":"41898def","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:36:36.956Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The checkpoint (7th generation) was just committed and is accurate. The properties list route returns raw WatchlistItem via sanitize, and the pill on the properties page is computed client-side from `p.county ?? null` (explicit-only, line 778). For consistency, the list route should provide per-item coverage. The properties page (UI) fetches from /api/properties. Options:\n\n(a) Add `coverage` to the list response (as a per-item wrapper) — the route needs to do a getCountyRecord read per item (same as /api/coverage).\n(b) Have the properties page fetch /api/coverage and join — the coverage endpoint returns an aggregation per county, not per property, so the join logic on the client side for review status becomes incomplete (review requires per-property provenance).\n\n(a) is correct. Change the list response shape: currently it returns an array of sanitized items (check the return statement around line 74). Let me take a look at that part.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae57f4b22cbe4bda","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '55,100p' src/app/api/properties/route.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":75051,"output":259,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":212,"totalTokens":75310,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788197788462,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bff297e1144709a8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9f56cfb0","parentId":"05e4af8b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:36:37.004Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-ae57f4b22cbe4bda","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    pricePerSqFt: numOrNull(body.pricePerSqFt),\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * GET /api/properties — the user's watchlist (Crexi properties they\n * track), read from Firestore. Consumed by the /properties page, the\n * dashboard pipeline table, and /property/[id].\n */\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  try {\n    const user = await getUserFromRequest(request);\n    if (!user) {\n      return NextResponse.json(\n        { error: 'Unauthorized' },\n        { status: 401, headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } }\n      );\n    }\n\n    const items = await listWatchlistItems(user.id);\n    const projections = await getLatestScreeningProjection(\n      user.id,\n      items.map((i) => i.id)\n    );\n    // Additive: existing `items` consumers are unchanged; consumers that\n    // need the verdict merge by propertyId.\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { items, screening: projections },\n      { headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } }\n    );\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('Error in /api/properties:', error);\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: 'Internal server error' },\n      { status: 500, headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } }\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * POST /api/properties — add a Crexi search result to the user's\n * watchlist (idempotent upsert: re-watching refreshes the snapshot and\n * keeps any verdict already set).\n */\nexport async function POST(request: NextRequest) {\n  try {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788197797004}}
{"type":"message","id":"314ada7d","parentId":"9f56cfb0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:37:06.975Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The properties list route returns `{ items, screening }`. Add a parallel array `coverage` aligned by index (or a map of propertyId → coverage note). A parallel array indexed the same way as `items` is the simplest and matches how the screening projections are merged (they use propertyId). For clarity, I'll use `Record<string, CoverageNote>` keyed by propertyId — the UI merges by id. Actually, the UI (properties/page.tsx:778) computes the pill client-side from p.county — I'll update it to use the provided coverage if available, and fall back to the explicit-only resolution if not.\n\nLet me add the following to the route:\n```ts\nconst countyRecords = await Promise.all(\n  items.map((item) => getCountyRecord(user.id, item.id))\n);\n...\nconst coverage: Record<string, ...> = {};\nitems.forEach((item, i) => {\n  coverage[item.id] = coverageNote(\n    resolveCountyCoverage(\n      countyIdentityForProperty(item.county ?? undefined, item.state),\n      countyRecords[i]?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n    )\n  );\n});\nreturn { items, screening: projections, coverage };\n```\n\nWait — countyIdentityForProperty(item.county ?? undefined, item.state): this normalizes the explicit county. In properties/[id]/route.ts, I passed `property.county ?? null` directly to resolveCountyCoverage (without normalizing via countyIdentityForProperty). Hmm — there's an inconsistency in which normalization the resolver receives: /api/coverage uses countyIdentityForProperty (normalizes code + state disambiguation), while the property detail route passes the raw item.county. resolveCountyCoverage internally does normalizeCountyCode in the contradiction base comparison, and lookupCountyCapability also normalizes. The difference: countyIdentityForProperty also normalizes the NAME and disambiguates the state token. For the canonical result, both paths end up at the same registry lookup (lookupCountyCapability normalizes the code). The only difference is in the display of `county` in the not_covered fallback (raw vs. normalized identity). Trivial. To keep it fully consistent, should I use countyIdentityForProperty in the property detail route as well? The property detail route currently passes the raw `property.county ?? null`. To keep the input 100% identical across all surfaces, let me make the property detail route use countyIdentityForProperty too. Let me check what countyIdentityForProperty does — it's imported from capabilities in the properties/[id] route. I'll update that call to wrap it.\n\nNext, the recorded-documents route. I'll start with the edit to the properties list first.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a676c5968f6bd62","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"import {\n  listWatchlistItems,\n} from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { getCountyRecord } from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';\nimport {\n  countyIdentityForProperty,\n  coverageNote,\n  resolveCountyCoverage,\n} from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';","oldText":"import {\n  listWatchlistItems,\n} from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { countyIdentityForProperty } from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';"},{"newText":"    const items = await listWatchlistItems(user.id);\n    const projections = await getLatestScreeningProjection(\n      user.id,\n      items.map((i) => i.id)\n    );\n    // Additive: existing `items` consumers are unchanged; consumers that\n    // need the verdict merge by propertyId. `coverage` carries the same\n    // canonical per-property resolution (explicit county + confirmed-\n    // snapshot provenance) every other surface uses, so the list pill can\n    // never disagree with the deep-dive or /api/coverage.\n    const countyRecords = await Promise.all(\n      items.map((item) => getCountyRecord(user.id, item.id))\n    );\n    const coverage: Record<string, ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>> = {};\n    items.forEach((item, index) => {\n      coverage[item.id] = coverageNote(\n        resolveCountyCoverage(\n          countyIdentityForProperty(item.county ?? undefined, item.state),\n          countyRecords[index]?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n        )\n      );\n    });\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { items, screening: projections, coverage },\n      { headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } }\n    );","oldText":"    const items = await listWatchlistItems(user.id);\n    const projections = await getLatestScreeningProjection(\n      user.id,\n      items.map((i) => i.id)\n    );\n    // Additive: existing `items` consumers are unchanged; consumers that\n    // need the verdict merge by propertyId.\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { items, screening: projections },\n      { headers: { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } }\n    );"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/route.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":75715,"output":1162,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":574,"totalTokens":76877,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788197797008,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bb504764073b6e28","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
