{"type":"message","id":"7f0b8654","parentId":"90362e9e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:45:26.621Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Next, I'll add `RecordedCoverageNote` to types/recorded-documents.ts, and then update the two read routes. The read routes currently return a plain RecordedSearchResponse. Plan: the response will be the search result + additional `{ authoritative: boolean; coverage: RecordedCoverageNote }` — but wait, if I make these required additional fields, wouldn't that break the `isSearchResponse` check? No — isSearchResponse only checks whether status is included in the set. However, the component types the fetch result as RecordedSearchResponse, and the actual JSON has extra fields — since the component's code only accesses the known fields, there's no runtime problem. That said, on the TypeScript side: if the route returns the extended type and the component receives RecordedSearchResponse, structurally there's no problem.\n\nShould `authoritative` also be added to the not_started (root) response? Yes, for consistency (the plan says \"apply the canonical coverage guard to recorded document collection and search polling reads\" — the root read is the collection read). Add it to both.\n\nType definitions:\n```ts\n/**\n * The client-safe coverage note attached to recorded document reads\n * (collection + polling). When the property's county coverage is no longer live,\n * the read sets `authoritative: false` so that stale county-specific results are\n * not presented as current authoritative data.\n */\nexport interface RecordedCoverageNote {\n  status: 'live' | 'planned' | 'not_covered' | 'unknown' | 'review';\n  county: { code: string; name: string } | null;\n  message: string | null;\n}\n\n/** A recorded read with a coverage guard (collection list + polling). */\nexport type RecordedSearchGuardedResponse = RecordedSearchResponse & {\n  authoritative: boolean;\n  coverage: RecordedCoverageNote;\n};\n```\n\nHmm — wait, the root endpoint currently returns either a not_started payload, or a RecordedSearch (when the latest search exists). Let me re-check what the root GET returns: it returns either the `notStartedPayload` or the latest RecordedSearch. Both get the guard fields.\n\nNext, the routes. I'll write a shared helper in shared.ts:\n\n```ts\nimport { resolveCountyCoverage, coverageNote } from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';\n\n/**\n * The canonical coverage guard for recorded document reads — the exact\n * same inputs as the search enqueue gate (explicit county + provenance of\n * the confirmed snapshot). Live → the read remains authoritative. Non-live →\n * the read returns (the data is persisted) but the response declares\n * `authoritative: false` with a typed note, so that stale county-specific\n * results are never presented as current.\n */\nexport async function recordedReadGuard(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string\n): Promise<{\n  authoritative: boolean;\n  coverage: ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>;\n}> {\n  const property = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n  const record = property ? await getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId) : null;\n  if (!property) {\n    return {\n      authoritative: false,\n      coverage: { status: 'unknown', county: null, message: '...' },\n    };\n  }\n  const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n    property.county ?? null,\n    record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n  );\n  return {\n    authoritative: coverage.status === 'live',\n    coverage: coverageNote(coverage),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nThen in each route's GET: after loading the response, spread `{ ...guard }` into the payload.\n\nI'll update shared.ts (add the helper) and both routes. First, let me check shared.ts (it's small — I saw it in the summary: NO_STORE, manualNextSteps, notStartedPayload, isSearchResponse). I'll read it.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-963d8fdf01e004e3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":102677,"output":905,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":848,"totalTokens":103582,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198301573,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a5d610d60119c0c2","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"5016eb39","parentId":"7f0b8654","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:45:26.642Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-963d8fdf01e004e3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Shared helpers for the recorded-documents API routes.\n *\n * Same contract as the county-records routes: authenticated, the property\n * must be in the CALLER's own watchlist (resolved server-side), per-user\n * rate limited, no-store, force-dynamic.\n */\nimport { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport type { StoredCountyRecord } from '@/types/county-records';\nimport { requireWatchedProperty } from '../county-records/shared';\n\nconst NO_STORE = { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } as const;\n\nexport { NO_STORE };\n\nexport type WatchedPropertyAuth = {\n  user: { id: string };\n  property: import('@/types/records-dashboard').WatchlistItem;\n};\n\n/**\n * The canonical 409 for \"the county record changed since you looked at\n * it\" — the caller must reload the property (which re-renders the county\n * AND the recorded state) before retrying.\n */\nexport function countyRecordChangedResponse(\n  current: StoredCountyRecord\n): NextResponse {\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    { error: 'county_record_changed', state: current },\n    { status: 409, headers: NO_STORE }\n  );\n}\n\n/** 404 helper for an unknown search id (or another owner's search). */\nexport function searchNotFoundResponse(): NextResponse {\n  return NextResponse.json(\n    { error: 'Recorded search not found' },\n    { status: 404, headers: NO_STORE }\n  );\n}\n\n/**\n * Authentication wrapper for the recorded-documents routes. (The county\n * shared's `requireWatchedProperty` does the real work; this keeps the\n * routes from importing across feature trees directly.)\n */\nexport async function requireRecordedProperty(\n  request: NextRequest,\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n): Promise<WatchedPropertyAuth | NextResponse> {\n  const auth = await requireWatchedProperty(request, params);\n  return auth;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788198326642}}
{"type":"message","id":"8a36b57e","parentId":"5016eb39","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:45:42.866Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, let's implement it:\n\n1. `types/recorded-documents.ts`: Add RecordedCoverageNote + guarded response type.\n2. `shared.ts`: Add a `recordedReadGuard` helper (fetches property + county record, computes the canonical coverage note + authoritative flag).\n3. `recorded-documents/route.ts` GET: Append the guard to the response.\n4. `searches/[searchId]/route.ts` GET: Append the guard to the response (including the not_started payload).\n5. UI `recorded-documents-section.tsx`: Display the notification when authoritative === false.\n\nAlright, let's write these edits. Starting with the types.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-862fd48044a480c6","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"export interface RecordedSearchNotFound {\n  status: 'not_started';\n  searchId: null;\n  propertyId: string;\n  manualNextSteps: string[];\n}\n\n/** What the list/search routes return. */\nexport type RecordedSearchResponse = RecordedSearch | RecordedSearchNotFound;\n\n/**\n * Client-safe coverage note attached to recorded-document READS (the\n * collection list and the search poll). When the property's county\n * coverage is no longer live — it went planned/not-covered/unknown, or\n * landed in the fail-closed review state after the search ran — the read\n * carries `authoritative: false` plus this note, so a stale county-\n * specific result is never presented as current authoritative data. The\n * stored documents remain available (they were real at retrieval time).\n */\nexport interface RecordedCoverageNote {\n  status: 'live' | 'planned' | 'not_covered' | 'unknown' | 'review';\n  county: { code: string; name: string } | null;\n  message: string | null;\n}\n\n/** A recorded read plus its coverage guard (additive fields). */\nexport type RecordedSearchGuardedResponse = RecordedSearchResponse & {\n  authoritative: boolean;\n  coverage: RecordedCoverageNote;\n};","oldText":"export interface RecordedSearchNotFound {\n  status: 'not_started';\n  searchId: null;\n  propertyId: string;\n  manualNextSteps: string[];\n}\n\n/** What the list/search routes return. */\nexport type RecordedSearchResponse = RecordedSearch | RecordedSearchNotFound;"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/types/recorded-documents.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":104062,"output":577,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":146,"totalTokens":104639,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198326647,"responseId":"chatcmpl-94948da6e579cbd3","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
