{"type":"message","id":"ed0f54c1","parentId":"819c40ad","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:46:42.303Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Damn it — in my edit I ended up replacing the `requireRecordedProperty` function with an incomplete placeholder body. This was a mistake: I wrote a draft of the guard, but I mistakenly put a placeholder inside, and I deleted the actual `requireRecordedProperty` function that other routes depend on. I need to do the following:\n\n1. Restore `requireRecordedProperty` as-is.\n2. Properly add `recordedReadGuard` with the actual implementation (use getWatchlistItem + getCountyRecord).\n\nAlright, let me rewrite the relevant part of the file correctly.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI accidentally clobbered `requireRecordedProperty` with a draft — restoring it and adding the real guard:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a17c5dfc14476fe7","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"/**\n * Authentication wrapper for the recorded-documents routes. (The county\n * shared's `requireWatchedProperty` does the real work; this keeps the\n * routes from importing across feature trees directly.)\n */\nexport async function requireRecordedProperty(\n  request: NextRequest,\n  params: Promise<{ id: string }>\n): Promise<WatchedPropertyAuth | NextResponse> {\n  const auth = await requireWatchedProperty(request, params);\n  return auth;\n}\n\n/**\n * The canonical coverage guard for recorded-document READS (the collection\n * list and the search poll). It resolves coverage from EXACTLY the same\n * inputs the search enqueue gate uses — the explicit county plus the\n * confirmed-snapshot provenance — so a read can never disagree with what\n * the gate would do today:\n *\n *   - live:      the read stays `authoritative: true`; the result is\n *                presented as current.\n *   - not live:  the stored result is still returned (it was real when\n *                retrieved) but `authoritative: false` with a typed note,\n *                so a stale county-specific result is never presented as\n *                current authoritative data.\n */\nexport async function recordedReadGuard(\n  user: { id: string },\n  propertyId: string\n): Promise<{\n  authoritative: boolean;\n  coverage: ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>;\n}> {\n  const [property, record] = await Promise.all([\n    getWatchlistItem(user.id, propertyId),\n    getCountyRecord(user.id, propertyId),\n  ]);\n  if (!property) {\n    // The route auth already 404'd for an unwatched property; this branch\n    // is defensive only and fails closed.\n    return {\n      authoritative: false,\n      coverage: {\n        status: 'unknown',\n        county: null,\n        message: 'This property has no county identified yet.',\n      },\n    };\n  }\n  const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n    property.county ?? null,\n    record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n  );\n  return {\n    authoritative: coverage.status === 'live',\n    coverage: coverageNote(coverage),\n  };\n}","oldText":"/**\n * The canonical coverage guard for recorded-document READS (the collection\n * list and the search poll). It resolves coverage from EXACTLY the same\n * inputs the search enqueue gate uses — the explicit county plus the\n * confirmed-snapshot provenance — so a read can never disagree with what\n * the gate would do today:\n *\n *   - live:      the read stays `authoritative: true`; the result is\n *                presented as current.\n *   - not live:  the stored result is still returned (it was real when\n *                retrieved) but `authoritative: false` with a typed note,\n *                so a stale county-specific result is never presented as\n *                current authoritative data.\n */\nexport async function recordedReadGuard(\n  user: { id: string },\n  propertyId: string\n): Promise<{\n  authoritative: boolean;\n  coverage: ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>;\n}> {\n  const property = await requireWatchedProperty.__placeholder__;\n  throw new Error('unused');\n}"},{"newText":"import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport type { StoredCountyRecord } from '@/types/county-records';\nimport { requireWatchedProperty } from '../county-records/shared';\nimport { resolveCountyCoverage, coverageNote } from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';\nimport { getWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { getCountyRecord } from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';","oldText":"import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport type { StoredCountyRecord } from '@/types/county-records';\nimport { requireWatchedProperty } from '../county-records/shared';\nimport { resolveCountyCoverage, coverageNote } from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":105860,"output":1183,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":125,"totalTokens":107043,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198367318,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b782ff7f28b5b52f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
