ter `setSearch(payload);` → add `setCoverageNotice(guardNotice(payload));`.\n- Add a helper function near isSearchResponse:\n```ts\nfunction guardNotice(payload: RecordedSearchResponse): string | null {\n  const guard = payload as RecordedSearchResponse & {\n    authoritative?: boolean;\n    coverage?: { message: string | null };\n  };\n  return guard.authoritative === false && guard.coverage?.message\n    ? guard.coverage.message\n    : null;\n}\n```\n- The render block after the notice block:\n```tsx\n          {coverageNotice && (\n            <p\n              role=\"status\"\n              data-testid=\"recorded-coverage-notice\"\n              style={{\n                margin: '0 0 12px',\n                padding: '8px 10px',\n                border: '1px solid #F59E0B',\n                background: '#FFFBEB',\n                color: '#92400E',\n                fontSize: 13,\n                ...WRAP,\n              }}\n            >\n              {coverageNotice}\n            </p>\n          )}\n```\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a05c180e8dc066e2","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"function errorMessage(payload: unknown, fallback: string): string {\n  if (\n    typeof payload === 'object' &&\n    payload !== null &&\n    'error' in payload &&\n    typeof payload.error === 'string'\n  ) {\n    return payload.error;\n  }\n  return fallback;\n}\n\n/**\n * The additive coverage guard the recorded-read routes append\n * (`authoritative` + `coverage` note). A non-authoritative read (the\n * property's coverage went non-live after the search ran) shows the\n * server-provided message verbatim — never invented text.\n */\nfunction guardNotice(payload: RecordedSearchResponse): string | null {\n  const guard = payload as RecordedSearchResponse & {\n    authoritative?: boolean;\n    coverage?: { message: string | null };\n  };\n  return guard.authoritative === false && guard.coverage?.message\n    ? guard.coverage