{"type":"message","id":"668da801","parentId":"b4c4ebba","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:53:03.939Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b7c3b5d853baa50f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"343:async function backfillCountyBestEffort(\n544:  await backfillCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage.county);\n632:  await backfillCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage.county);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788198783939}}
{"type":"message","id":"c27b163a","parentId":"668da801","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:53:15.418Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Two call sites (line 544 is confirm, line 632 is refresh). The auto-confirm path — let me check what it's doing (the earlier grep for \"backfillWatchlistCounty\" only hit line 350, which is inside a local helper, so auto-confirm is... wait, the earlier auto-confirm code (lines 300-336) isn't calling backfill at all! Let me double-check: the auto-confirm handler is calling `confirmCountyParcel` — and after that? The earlier grep for `backfill` only showed 343 (the definition), 350 (inside the helper), 544, and 632. So auto-confirm is not doing backfill — this is a gap: when the worker auto-confirms a unique match, it doesn't reconcile the county of legacy properties. The plan says to make reconciliation idempotent and durable — auto-confirm should also reconcile (it's the same confirm semantics). Let me add a call there too.\n\nNext, I'll implement reconcileWatchlistCounty. I'll replace the body of backfillWatchlistCounty with the transactional version and rename it. But other code (tests?) might be importing backfillWatchlistCounty — grep only shows the worker importing it. Let me also check the tests:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af43e9c4320c8926","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn \"backfillWatchlistCounty\\|reconcileWatchlistCounty\" src/ --include=\"*.test.ts\" --include=\"*.test.tsx\" | head; echo ===; sed -n '300,342p' src/lib/agent-worker.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":126262,"output":365,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":278,"totalTokens":126627,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198783943,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a8053fc4c91fa329","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"44174b4e","parentId":"c27b163a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:53:15.508Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-af43e9c4320c8926","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"===\n */\nfunction providerFor(\n  ctx: WorkerContext,\n  county: CountyIdentity\n): CountyRecordsProvider {\n  return ctx.provider ?? getCountyRecordsProvider(county);\n}\n\n/**\n * M1 run-time re-check: the property's canonical coverage must be `live`\n * NOW (the world may have changed since enqueue), and — when the task\n * input captured a county — it must still match. Fails closed with a\n * blocking error and ZERO county writes.\n */\nasync function requireLiveCounty(\n  item: WatchlistItem,\n  record: StoredCountyRecord | null,\n  expectedCounty: CountyIdentity | null | undefined\n): Promise<LiveCoverage> {\n  const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n    item.county ?? null,\n    record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null\n  );\n  if (coverage.status !== 'live') {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'unsupported_county',\n      notCoveredPayload(coverage).message\n    );\n  }\n  if (\n    expectedCounty &&\n    normalizeCountyCode(expectedCounty.code) !==\n      normalizeCountyCode(coverage.county.code)\n  ) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'county_changed',\n      'The property\\u2019s county changed since this work was queued. Reload and re-run it.'\n    );\n  }\n  return coverage;\n}\n\n/** Best-effort: persist the county on a legacy item once confirmed. */\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788198795508}}
{"type":"message","id":"2571716d","parentId":"44174b4e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T17:54:05.846Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are no tests referencing backfillWatchlistCounty. The auto-confirm path (runCountyAutoConfirm, ~line 262-336) doesn't backfill — I'll add reconcile there too.\n\nWhat I'm about to implement:\n\n1. **firestore/properties.ts**: Replace `backfillWatchlistCounty` with `reconcileWatchlistCounty` (transactional). Need to import `countyBase` and `normalizeCountyCode` from capabilities. Also the outcome type.\n\n2. **agent-worker.ts**:\n   - Import reconcileWatchlistCounty instead of backfillWatchlistCounty.\n   - Replace the local `backfillCountyBestEffort` with `reconcileCountyFor(uid, item, county, sourceId)`: call reconcile; if the result is 'reconciled' → log at info level (optional); 'explicit_conflict' → log at info level (review state will be displayed on the read side); 'property_gone'/'already_reconciled' → do nothing; throw → console.error with the full context (don't rethrow → the task succeeds; the confirm is durable).\n\n   Wait — \"don't swallow persistence failures.\" If I catch and log at error level, is that \"swallowing\"? The difference from before: the previous code was `console.warn` (silent-ish). Plan intent: failures must be surfaced and must not silently masquerade as success. A console.error with structured context, plus idempotent re-attempts on the next county work, plus the read side still agreeing via provenance = honest handling. The task's success semantics: the domain action (parcel confirm/refresh) succeeded; the auxiliary identity reconciliation degraded. To be maximally honest, log at error level with the exact identifiers and document it in the module header's crash-boundary comment. This aligns with the plan's \"no silent failures.\"\n\n   Actually — hmm, let me reconsider: wouldn't it be better to fail the task as transient, so the retry re-runs the confirm? No: the confirm has already been committed; re-running the confirm is a CAS conflict (stale revision) → block. Failing the task would cause it to be retried with a stale expectedRevision → blocked — worse. So: confirm durable + task success + error-level log + idempotent reconcile on the next county work. This is the correct engineering.\n\n   - Add a third call site to the auto-confirm path: after the `confirmCountyParcel` success block (around ~line 305-316): `void reconcile...`? No — await it, with the same non-fatal handling.\n   - requireLiveCounty: add a review branch:\n   ```ts\n   if (coverage.status === 'review') {\n     throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n       'county_review',\n       notCoveredPayload(coverage).message\n     );\n   }\n   ```\n   before the generic unsupported_county throw. (notCoveredPayload handles review with a dedicated message.)\n\n3. Also, `confirmCountyParcel`/`refreshCountyParcel` take a casOptions parameter — no change needed.\n\nNow let me write the properties.ts changes.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've confirmed the test doesn't reference the old function and that auto-confirm is missing the reconcile step. Now I'll implement the transactional reconcile.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9283ffd07430ef09","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport { countyBase, normalizeCountyCode } from '@/lib/county-records/capabilities';\nimport type {\n  CountyIdentity,\n  WatchlistItem,\n  WatchlistSnapshot,\n} from '@/types/records-dashboard';","oldText":"import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport type {\n  CountyIdentity,\n  WatchlistItem,\n  WatchlistSnapshot,\n} from '@/types/records-dashboard';"},{"newText":"/**\n * The outcome of reconciling a property's county identity against the\n * county proven by a CONFIRMED parcel snapshot (source provenance, never\n * an inference from state/address).\n */\nexport type CountyReconcileOutcome =\n  | { status: 'reconciled'; county: CountyIdentity }\n  | { status: 'already_reconciled'; county: CountyIdentity }\n  | {\n      status: 'explicit_conflict';\n      county: CountyIdentity;\n      stored: CountyIdentity;\n    }\n  | { status: 'property_gone' };\n\n/**\n * Transactional, idempotent county reconciliation (the canonical write\n * for legacy county-less properties).\n *\n * Unlike the retired read-then-write backfill, the check and the write\n * happen inside ONE Firestore transaction, so a concurrent explicit\n * PATCH can never be clobbered (and a reconcile can never race a\n * simultaneous reconcile):\n *\n *   - property absent           → `property_gone` (no write)\n *   - explicit county, different → `explicit_conflict` (NO write) — an\n *     explicit assertion is never overwritten by provenance; the\n *     mismatch surfaces as the fail-closed `review` coverage state on\n *     every read surface until a human resolves it\n *   - explicit county, same base → `already_reconciled` (no write;\n *     idempotent — the stored identity is returned, not the derived one)\n *   - county absent             → writes `{ county, countyReconciledFrom,\n *     countyReconciledAt }` (merge) → `reconciled`\n *\n * Errors PROPAGATE (they are never swallowed here): a failed write after\n * a durable confirm leaves the property county-less but every surface\n * still agrees through provenance, and the next county work reconciles\n * again (idempotent). Callers decide how to surface the failure.\n */\nexport async function reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  county: CountyIdentity,\n  sourceId: string\n): Promise<CountyReconcileOutcome> {\n  const db = getFirestoreDb();\n  return db.runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n    const ref = propertiesCollection(uid).doc(propertyId);\n    const doc = await tx.get(ref);\n    if (!doc.exists) return { status: 'property_gone' as const };\n    const existing = parseCountyIdentity(\n      (doc.data() as { county?: unknown })?.county\n    );\n    if (existing) {\n      const sameBase =\n        countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(existing.code) ?? '') ===\n        countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(county.code) ?? '');\n      return sameBase\n        ? { status: 'already_reconciled', county: existing }\n        : { status: 'explicit_conflict', county, stored: existing };\n    }\n    tx.set(\n      ref,\n      {\n        county,\n        countyReconciledFrom: sourceId,\n        countyReconciledAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n      },\n      { merge: true }\n    );\n    return { status: 'reconciled', county };\n  });\n}","oldText":"export async function backfillWatchlistCounty(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  county: CountyIdentity\n): Promise<boolean> {\n  const ref = propertiesCollection(uid).doc(propertyId);\n  const doc = await ref.get();\n  if (!doc.exists) return false;\n  const existing = parseCountyIdentity(\n    (doc.data() as { county?: unknown })?.county\n  );\n  if (existing) return false;\n  await ref.set({ county }, { merge: true });\n  return true;\n}"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/firestore/properties.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":126973,"output":1755,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":673,"totalTokens":128728,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198795511,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a3f0d75d441dff47","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
