{"type":"message","id":"8a33cdf4","parentId":"4c08de8b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:09:39.311Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nThe advisory is saying that the import of `getCountyRecord` is unused in that test file — I imported it, but the new test isn't using it directly (the mock's default handles it). Just like the case in properties/[id], I should either use it in an assertion, or remove the import. In the recorded-documents test, the guard behavior is being verified through the body (the authoritative/coverage assertions) — the import isn't needed. I'll remove the unused import (the mock stays, and that's the important part).\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-856835ae693fb454","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"import { getUserFromRequest } from '@/lib/auth';\nimport { getWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { getLatestRecordedSearch } from '@/lib/firestore/recorded-documents';\nimport { checkRateLimit } from '@/lib/rate-limiter';","oldText":"import { getUserFromRequest } from '@/lib/auth';\nimport { getWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { getCountyRecord } from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';\nimport { getLatestRecordedSearch } from '@/lib/firestore/recorded-documents';\nimport { checkRateLimit } from '@/lib/rate-limiter';"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":74715,"output":363,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":127,"totalTokens":75078,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788199768736,"responseId":"chatcmpl-bc8296fbc04b1e58","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
