{"type":"message","id":"39a3ea45","parentId":"883243d5","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:13:10.193Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bc4be597f38310ae","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"18: *                    registry.\n32:/** A wired (or roadmapped) county in the capability registry. */\n48: * The capability registry — the ONLY place county coverage is declared.\n155:    // The registry is the canonical display name for a known county —\n182: * registry lookup, the contradiction check, and the provider selection\n183: * gates: a bare county slug ('cuyahoga') and the registry slug\n198:  // A bare slug (no state token) resolves when exactly one registry county\n218:  sourceId: CountyRecordsSourceId | null | undefined\n220:  if (!sourceId) return null;\n222:  // `cuyahoga-fixture`); match the registry entry by its county base so\n224:  const base = sourceId.replace(/-(arcgis|fixture)$/, '');\n314:  // so a bare 'cuyahoga' and the registry's 'cuyahoga-oh' are the same\n315:  // county (registry base slugs are unique) and do NOT contradict.\n===\n__tests__/\naddress.ts  12.2K\ncapabilities.ts  17.0K\nconfig.ts  4.6K\ncuyahoga-arcgis.ts  17.6K\nfixtures.ts  9.2K\nprovider.ts  4.3K\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788199990193}}
{"type":"message","id":"9c87288a","parentId":"39a3ea45","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:13:15.462Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Line 224 of capabilities.ts: `const base = sourceId.replace(/-(arcgis|fixture)$/, '')` — meaning 'cuyahoga-fixture' → base 'cuyahoga' → matches a registry county whose base slug is 'cuyahoga' (cuyahoga-oh). And 'lorain-fixture' → 'lorain' → matches lorain-oh if lorain is in the registry. Let me check the contents of the registry — which counties are registered.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a553d8ea4673e6d9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '48,110p' src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":82370,"output":157,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":108,"totalTokens":82527,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788199990197,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8045b0bf598bd41b","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"8b6a2322","parentId":"9c87288a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:13:15.508Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a553d8ea4673e6d9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" * The capability registry — the ONLY place county coverage is declared.\n * Adding a county to coverage is a code change to this table (a provider\n * source plus a live entry), never an address or state inference.\n */\nexport const COUNTY_CAPABILITIES: readonly CountyCapability[] = [\n  {\n    code: 'cuyahoga-oh',\n    name: 'Cuyahoga County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'live',\n    source: { id: 'cuyahoga-arcgis', label: CUYAHOGA_SOURCE.label },\n    eta: null,\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'summit-oh',\n    name: 'Summit County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'planned',\n    source: null,\n    eta: 'Q4 2026',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'franklin-oh',\n    name: 'Franklin County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'planned',\n    source: null,\n    eta: '2027',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'lorain-oh',\n    name: 'Lorain County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'not_covered',\n    source: null,\n    eta: null,\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'lake-oh',\n    name: 'Lake County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'not_covered',\n    source: null,\n    eta: null,\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'medina-oh',\n    name: 'Medina County',\n    state: 'OH',\n    status: 'not_covered',\n    source: null,\n    eta: null,\n  },\n];\n\nconst CAPABILITY_BY_CODE = new Map(COUNTY_CAPABILITIES.map((c) => [c.code, c]));\n\n/**\n * Normalize a raw county string into a stable slug:\n *   'Cuyahoga County'  → 'cuyahoga'\n *   'cuyahoga-oh'      → 'cuyahoga-oh'\n *   '  LORAIN county ' → 'lorain'\n *   'Franklin County, OH' → 'franklin-oh'\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788199995508}}
{"type":"message","id":"f610e0fb","parentId":"8b6a2322","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:13:29.905Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nRegistry: Cuyahoga (live, source cuyahoga-arcgis), Summit (planned), Franklin (planned), Lorain (not_covered), Lake, Medina (not_covered).\n\nNow — how does the provenance resolution work? Lines 218-224: sourceId → base (with the -(arcgis|fixture) suffix stripped) → \"match the registry entry by that county's base.\" So 'lorain-fixture' → 'lorain' → matches registry entry lorain-oh. But wait — can a county with status 'not_covered' be the source of a CONFIRMED snapshot? A confirmed parcel snapshot comes from a provider search — in the fixture mode, the provider only has a Cuyahoga fixture (cuyahoga-fixture / cuyahoga-arcgis). Lorain is not_covered — it has no source. A confirmed snapshot with provenance sourceId 'lorain-fixture' shouldn't be producible in reality, but for a unit test that directly mocks getCountyRecord, it's fine as data.\n\nSo why did the test get 'live' instead of 'review'? resolveCountyCoverage(explicit=cuyahoga-oh, confirmedSourceId='lorain-fixture') → provenance county = lorain-oh (via the base match) → contradiction → should become review. But the test received authoritative=true (live). So either the provenance resolution returned null (no match), or... wait — maybe the problem is this: my mock returned `{ snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'lorain-fixture' } } }`, and the route reads `record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId`. That matches. Hmm, but maybe the guard in shared.ts isn't passing the sourceId...? Or maybe the base-matching function only matches sources of counties that have a source in the registry? Let me read the resolution function at lines 218-230.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-827353b6c097abb2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '210,260p' src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":83066,"output":478,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":428,"totalTokens":83544,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788199995511,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a028283c50d2a36e","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8cb9fd7","parentId":"f610e0fb","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:13:29.950Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-827353b6c097abb2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" * The county a confirmed county-record snapshot belongs to: the source\n * that produced the snapshot IS the county's authority (a parcel confirmed\n * from the Cuyahoga layer — live OR its fixture stand-in — is in\n * Cuyahoga). This is provenance from the source itself — not an inference\n * from state or address — so it is a valid, honest backfill for a property\n * that was added without county identity.\n */\nexport function countyForSourceId(\n  sourceId: CountyRecordsSourceId | null | undefined\n): CountyIdentity | null {\n  if (!sourceId) return null;\n  // A source id is `{county}-{variant}` (e.g. `cuyahoga-arcgis`,\n  // `cuyahoga-fixture`); match the registry entry by its county base so\n  // both the live and the fixture variant backfill to the same county.\n  const base = sourceId.replace(/-(arcgis|fixture)$/, '');\n  const cap = COUNTY_CAPABILITIES.find((c) =>\n    c.source ? c.source.id.replace(/-(arcgis|fixture)$/, '') === base : false\n  );\n  if (!cap) return null;\n  return { code: cap.code, name: cap.name };\n}\n\n/**\n * The property's EXPLICIT county and the county proven by a CONFIRMED\n * parcel snapshot disagree (for example, an explicit Summit County plus a\n * Cuyahoga-confirmed parcel). A present contradiction is a FAIL-CLOSED\n * review state (`status: 'review'`): the explicit county is displayed but\n * no county work may run — a confirmed parcel is a stronger claim than a\n * user assertion, and only a human may resolve which one stands.\n */\nexport type CountyCoverageContradiction = {\n  explicit: CountyIdentity;\n  provenance: CountyIdentity;\n} | null;\n\n/** The canonical coverage result — the ONLY shape consumers may use. */\nexport type CountyCoverage =\n  | {\n      status: 'live';\n      county: CountyIdentity;\n      eta: null;\n      source: { id: CountyRecordsSourceId; label: string };\n      contradiction?: CountyCoverageContradiction;\n    }\n  | {\n      status: 'planned';\n      county: CountyIdentity;\n      eta: string;\n      source: null;\n      contradiction?: CountyCoverageContradiction;\n    }\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200009950}}
{"type":"message","id":"8a9df7eb","parentId":"d8cb9fd7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:14:00.599Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it: `countyForSourceId` only matches registry entries where `c.source` is non-null. Lorain has `source: null` (it's not covered) → no match → returns null → no provenance → no contradiction → 'live'. In other words, in this design, the only county that can be proven via a snapshot source is a county that has a provider source, i.e., only Cuyahoga (live). Therefore, the only possible contradiction is: an explicit county other than Cuyahoga + a Cuyahoga-confirmed parcel (or explicit Cuyahoga + ... — the only source is Cuyahoga, so a contradiction requires the explicit county ≠ Cuyahoga).\n\nSo my test fixture using 'lorain-fixture' is semantically invalid (no provider exists for Lorain — a confirmed Lorain snapshot cannot exist). A valid test: explicit county SUMMIT (or any county other than Cuyahoga) + provenance 'cuyahoga-fixture' (or 'cuyahoga-arcgis') → review.\n\nFix for searches/[searchId] test: WATCH_ITEM with county summit-oh (not the Cuyahoga WATCH_ITEM) + record sourceId 'cuyahoga-fixture' → review, message names Summit + Cuyahoga.\n\nAlso the new PATCH test in properties/[id]: it was asserting PATCH Summit + record cuyahoga-fixture → review. This should work (Summit explicit + Cuyahoga provenance → contradiction). But that suite also had 1 failure — could it be the same test failing because...? Summit explicit + Cuyahoga provenance: countyForSourceId('cuyahoga-fixture') → Cuyahoga. Different base from Summit → review. It should pass. I need to check which test failed there — I'll run it with output. Also, the expected values for the contradiction object: explicit {code:'summit-oh', name:'Summit County'}, provenance {code:'cuyahoga-oh', name:'Cuyahoga County'} — matches the registry names. No problem.\n\nNow I'll run the properties/[id] suite to see the 1 failure, and fix the searches/[searchId] test.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98b284b62407f953","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it('flags a contradictory property as non-authoritative on the poll path', async () => {\n    // The confirmed parcel proves Cuyahoga while the explicit county is\n    // Summit — fail-closed: the stored run is still returned, but only\n    // with the review guard attached.\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ...WATCH_ITEM,\n      county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n    });\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture' } },\n    });\n    (getRecordedSearchById as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(search());\n\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://test/api'), params());\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.status).toBe('running');\n    expect(body.authoritative).toBe(false);\n    expect(body.coverage.status).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.coverage.county).toEqual({\n      code: 'summit-oh',\n      name: 'Summit County',\n    });\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Summit County');\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Cuyahoga County');\n  });\n});","oldText":"  it('flags a contradictory property as non-authoritative on the poll path', async () => {\n    // The confirmed parcel proves Lorain while the explicit county is\n    // Cuyahoga — fail-closed: the stored run is still returned, but only\n    // with the review guard attached.\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(WATCH_ITEM);\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'lorain-fixture' } },\n    });\n    (getRecordedSearchById as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(search());\n\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://test/api'), params());\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.status).toBe('running');\n    expect(body.authoritative).toBe(false);\n    expect(body.coverage.status).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Lorain County');\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Cuyahoga County');\n  });\n});"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/__tests__/route.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":84090,"output":1148,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":477,"totalTokens":85238,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200009953,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ae7ed38944e9f97f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
