{"type":"message","id":"254b69e2","parentId":"7f9c560b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:14:49.971Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-925ad835f65be7e3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"447:export function coverageNote(coverage: CountyCoverage): {\n448-  status: CountyCoverage['status'];\n449-  county: { code: string; name: string } | null;\n450-  message: string | null;\n451-  /** Present only for `review`: the two counties that disagree. Lets a\n452-   *  client reconstruct the exact `CountyCoverage` union member without a\n453-   *  second fetch (the review variant requires a non-null contradiction).\n454-   */\n455-  contradiction?: {\n456-    explicit: { code: string; name: string };\n457-    provenance: { code: string; name: string };\n458-  };\n459-} {\n460-  if (coverage.status === 'live') {\n461-    return { status: 'live', county: coverage.county, message: null };\n462-  }\n463-  const payload = notCoveredPayload(coverage);\n464-  const note: ReturnType<typeof coverageNote> = {\n465-    status: coverage.status,\n466-    county: payload.county,\n467-    message: payload.message,\n468-  };\n469-  if (coverage.status === 'review') {\n470-    note.contradiction = {\n471-      explicit: coverage.contradiction.explicit,\n472-      provenance: coverage.contradiction.provenance,\n473-    };\n474-  }\n475-  return note;\n476-}\n477-\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200089971}}
{"type":"message","id":"db26e235","parentId":"254b69e2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:14:55.699Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"coverageNote for review sets message = notCoveredPayload(coverage).message. So the message should exist... unless the PATCH route isn't using coverageNote and is returning the raw CountyCoverage object (which doesn't have a message field). Let me check how the PATCH in properties/[id]/route.ts is constructing the coverage response — my edit. I'll take a look.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a794b4e94fcb026","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"coverage\" src/app/api/properties/\\[id\\]/route.ts | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":87834,"output":127,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":77,"totalTokens":87961,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200089976,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ba54888547bc9673","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"75b446d3","parentId":"db26e235","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:14:55.748Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9a794b4e94fcb026","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"67:    // M1: the resolved coverage for this property's county — the deep-dive\n69:    // infers coverage from state). Canonical resolver with the SAME inputs\n74:    const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n79:      { property, crexi, screening: screening?.run ?? null, coverage },\n96: * the updated item plus the resolved coverage so the UI can immediately\n179:    // The post-update coverage uses the same canonical inputs as every\n183:    const coverage = resolveCountyCoverage(\n188:      { property: updated, coverage },\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200095748}}
{"type":"message","id":"b51e3c95","parentId":"75b446d3","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:15:06.205Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me confirm the details.\n\nConfirmed: the properties/[id] route returns the raw `CountyCoverage` object (`coverage`) as-is — it's not `coverageNote(coverage)`. The raw CountyCoverage review member has `contradiction`, but no `message` field (the message is inside `notCoveredPayload(coverage)`, i.e., the 422 payload). So the test's `body.coverage.message` is legitimately undefined — the detail/PATCH response shape is the raw coverage union, and the client (deep-dive UI / banner) derives the message via notCoveredPayload or its own mapping.\n\nTherefore, this is a test-side issue, not an implementation bug: the detail/PATCH contract is to return the complete CountyCoverage (status/county/eta/source/contradiction), not the slim note. The banner component receives the full coverage and renders the message itself (the banner's review case I wrote renders the message — it's probably calling notCoveredPayload internally, or building the text from contradiction).\n\nTest fix: assert the fields of the raw union: `body.coverage.status === 'review'`, `body.coverage.county` (the explicit summit), `body.coverage.contradiction.{explicit,provenance}`, `body.coverage.eta` — wait, what shape does the review member of the union have? Let me check the review variant of CountyCoverage — does it have eta/source? To write the correct assertion, let me look at the review variant of the union and how the banner consumes it.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9252d19a17f91c8d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '260,340p' src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":88109,"output":382,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":332,"totalTokens":88491,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200095751,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8f679ab8d285058c","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"037251a5","parentId":"b51e3c95","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:15:06.251Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9252d19a17f91c8d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    }\n  | {\n      status: 'not_covered';\n      county: CountyIdentity;\n      eta: null;\n      source: null;\n      contradiction?: CountyCoverageContradiction;\n    }\n  | {\n      status: 'unknown';\n      county: null;\n      eta: null;\n      source: null;\n      contradiction?: CountyCoverageContradiction;\n    }\n  | {\n      status: 'review';\n      county: CountyIdentity;\n      eta: null;\n      source: null;\n      contradiction: NonNullable<CountyCoverageContradiction>;\n    };\n\n/** The live branch of CountyCoverage — guarantees a usable county identity. */\nexport type LiveCoverage = Extract<CountyCoverage, { status: 'live' }>;\n\n/**\n * Resolve the canonical coverage for a property.\n *\n * @param county          The property's explicit county identity (null when\n *                        the property has none).\n * @param confirmedSourceId The source id behind a CONFIRMED county-record\n *                        snapshot, when one exists (source-provenance\n *                        backfill for legacy properties).\n *\n * Never returns a live result for a property that has no county identity\n * and no confirmed county source — unknown stays unknown. When the\n * explicit county and the confirmed-snapshot provenance prove DIFFERENT\n * counties, the result is the fail-closed `review` state: the explicit\n * county is displayed, but no county work runs until a human resolves the\n * contradiction (even if one of the two is a covered county).\n */\nexport function resolveCountyCoverage(\n  county: CountyIdentity | null | undefined,\n  confirmedSourceId: CountyRecordsSourceId | null | undefined\n): CountyCoverage {\n  const explicit = county ?? null;\n  const provenance = confirmedSourceId\n    ? countyForSourceId(confirmedSourceId)\n    : null;\n  // The explicit county wins for a MISSING identity (provenance backfills\n  // it). When both exist and name different counties, that is a\n  // contradiction — a fail-closed review state, never a routing input.\n  // The comparison is slug-based with the 2-letter state token stripped,\n  // so a bare 'cuyahoga' and the registry's 'cuyahoga-oh' are the same\n  // county (registry base slugs are unique) and do NOT contradict.\n  const countyBaseOf = (code: string) =>\n    countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(code) ?? '');\n  const contradiction: CountyCoverageContradiction =\n    explicit != null &&\n    provenance != null &&\n    countyBaseOf(explicit.code) !== countyBaseOf(provenance.code)\n      ? { explicit, provenance }\n      : null;\n\n  if (contradiction) {\n    // Fail closed: display the explicit county (the user's assertion) but\n    // block all county work — a confirmed parcel is a stronger claim than\n    // the assertion, and only a human may decide which stands.\n    const cap = lookupCountyCapability(contradiction.explicit.code);\n    return {\n      status: 'review',\n      county: {\n        code: contradiction.explicit.code,\n        name: cap ? cap.name : contradiction.explicit.name,\n      },\n      eta: null,\n      source: null,\n      contradiction,\n    };\n  }\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200106250}}
{"type":"message","id":"9ba6873e","parentId":"037251a5","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:15:25.087Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate further. Let me check the details.\n\nConfirmed: the raw `CountyCoverage` review member = `{ status: 'review', county, eta: null, source: null, contradiction }` — there is no `message` field. The detail/PATCH response returns this raw union. So my test's `message` assertion is wrong against the contract — the message is derived on the client side (the banner builds its own text from the contradiction via notCoveredPayload).\n\nTest fix: remove the message assertion and instead assert `body.coverage.eta).toBeNull()`, `body.coverage.source).toBeNull()`, and the exact shape of the union. Update the test accordingly.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bed0227d3bb2836","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    const res = await PATCH(patch({ county: { name: 'Summit' } }), params());\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.coverage.status).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.coverage.county).toEqual({\n      code: 'summit-oh',\n      name: 'Summit County',\n    });\n    // The raw coverage union on this surface carries no message — the\n    // client renders the review text from the contradiction pair.\n    expect(body.coverage.eta).toBeNull();\n    expect(body.coverage.source).toBeNull();\n    expect(body.coverage.contradiction).toEqual({\n      explicit: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n      provenance: { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' },\n    });\n  });\n});","oldText":"    const res = await PATCH(patch({ county: { name: 'Summit' } }), params());\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.coverage.status).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.coverage.county).toEqual({\n      code: 'summit-oh',\n      name: 'Summit County',\n    });\n    expect(body.coverage.contradiction).toEqual({\n      explicit: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n      provenance: { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' },\n    });\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Summit County');\n    expect(body.coverage.message).toContain('Cuyahoga County');\n  });\n});"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":89249,"output":647,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":146,"totalTokens":89896,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200106254,"responseId":"chatcmpl-877a2294b4c0b3f7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
