{"type":"message","id":"20daaf1d","parentId":"1e6f8649","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:21:43.058Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nAll 8 are failing with a 5000ms test timeout — this is an environmental factor (the suite's overall execution time of 45 seconds suggests that the tests are slow in this environment, or the Firestore emulator is being slow), not a semantic assertion failure. The first failure occurs at line 99 (the start of the test) — it's a timeout. These tests perform a full emulator round trip, so they may normally be passing with a longer effective time budget, but the per-test 5-second timeout is too strict for this run (the 50-second budget for 8 tests = 5 seconds each, meaning everything is timing out).\n\nThe key question: is this a pre-existing environmental slowness (the emulator is cold / the machine is under load), or is my guard change adding latency? My guard adds one extra getCountyRecord read per GET route call — a single document read, and even in the emulator it should be on the order of a few milliseconds. It's not something that would push 8 full-flow tests over a 5-second timeout.\n\nCheck the git status of this file — is it tracked and unchanged? My changes only touched the routes under src/app/api/.../recorded-documents (route.ts, shared.ts, searches/[searchId]/route.ts). This integration test file — was it passing before my changes? I can check: stash my changes? No — safer: run this test file in a clean state at commit a9eeff9 using `git stash`? That would disturb the working tree. Alternative: use `git worktree`? Even simpler: check whether the tests were passing at a9eeff9 according to the previous session's closeout — the closeout docs record that the integration suite was passing (the serial integration suite). But the environment may have changed (the emulator's state, machine load from my parallel jest runs).\n\nThe practical approach: first run just this suite alone (no other load), possibly with increased parallelism. If it still times out, check whether the Firestore emulator is even healthy in the first place (is the emulator running on the default port? Is the test starting its own emulator?). Let me check the test setup (the top of the file) to see how the emulator is being provisioned.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-893e61866a41af16","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":98,"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":97184,"output":561,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":491,"totalTokens":97745,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200486058,"responseId":"chatcmpl-98bbc8f3311b5817","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"37072852","parentId":"20daaf1d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:21:43.114Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-893e61866a41af16","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * Integration tests for the recorded-document search (Task 5).\n *\n * Runs against the local Firestore emulator (localhost:8095 — set by\n * jest.setup.integration.js). The provider is the deterministic fixture\n * (injected per test with a scenario), so the full pipeline — enqueue\n * seam → claim → run → terminal → idempotent re-run — is exercised\n * end-to-end with no network. Each test uses unique owner/property ids;\n * cross-user queries are scoped to the test's own owner so parallel test\n * files sharing the emulator cannot interfere.\n */\nimport { upsertWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport { enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent } from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';\nimport {\n  enqueueRecordedSearchIfCurrent,\n  getLatestRecordedSearch,\n  listLatestRecordedSearchesForOwner,\n  getRecordedSearchById,\n  startRecordedSearch,\n  completeRecordedSearch,\n  recordedSearchIdFor,\n} from '@/lib/firestore/recorded-documents';\nimport { processOneTask } from '@/lib/agent-worker';\nimport { CuyahogaRecorderFixtureProvider } from '@/lib/recorded-documents/provider';\nimport { RECORDED_INDEX_CONFIG } from '@/lib/recorded-documents/config';\nimport type { WatchlistSnapshot } from '@/types/records-dashboard';\nimport type { AgentTask } from '@/types/agent-tasks';\nimport type { RecordedSearch } from '@/types/recorded-documents';\n\nconst WATCH_SNAPSHOT: WatchlistSnapshot = {\n  address: '5180 Broadview Rd',\n  city: 'Cleveland',\n  state: 'OH',\n  zipCode: '44143',\n  county: { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' },\n  propertyType: 'residential',\n  title: 'Broadview Rd House',\n  crexiId: 'crexi-cr-rd',\n  listingUrl: 'https://crexi.com/listing/cr-rd',\n  thumbnailUrl: 'https://crexi.com/thumb/cr-rd.jpg',\n  price: 350000,\n  sizeSqFt: 1800,\n  pricePerSqFt: 194.44,\n};\n\nconst ADDR = {\n  street: '5180 broadview road',\n  unit: null,\n  city: 'cleveland',\n  state: 'OH',\n  zip: '44143',\n};\n\nconst runId = () => `${Date.now()}-${Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e6)}`;\n\nasync function seedWatchlist(uid: string, propertyId: string): Promise<void> {\n  await upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, {\n    ...WATCH_SNAPSHOT,\n    crexiId: propertyId,\n  });\n}\n\n/** Resolve the county record (fixture: one exact match → auto-confirmed). */\nasync function confirmParcel(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  workerId: string\n): Promise<RecordedSearch['countyRecordRevision']> {\n  const enq = await enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(\n    uid,\n    propertyId,\n    'county_resolve',\n    { expectedRevision: 0, address: ADDR },\n    0\n  );\n  if (!enq.task) throw new Error('county resolve enqueue failed');\n  await processOneTask(enq.task, { workerId });\n  // The fixture auto-confirms: r1 (resolve) + r2 (confirm).\n  return 2;\n}\n\nfunction recordedCtx(scenario?: string) {\n  return {\n    workerId: 'w-rd-int',\n    recordedProvider: new CuyahogaRecorderFixtureProvider(),\n    recordedScenario: scenario,\n  };\n}\n\nasync function searchBy(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  rev: number\n): Promise<RecordedSearch | null> {\n  return getRecordedSearchById(uid, recordedSearchIdFor(propertyId, rev));\n}\n\ndescribe('recorded-document search (emulator)', () => {\n\n[304 more lines in file. Use offset=99 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200503114}}
{"type":"message","id":"a2b1e1f4","parentId":"37072852","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:22:20.083Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nAdvisory only — no action needed. I'm past the checkpoint deadline, and the state has significantly changed: the resolve unit suite is green (10/10); the emulator integration suite fails 8/8 with 5-second timeouts (a class of environmental factors). I'll update the checkpoint, and then determine whether the timeouts are a pre-existing issue (environmental factors) or caused by my own changes.\n\nPlan:\n1. Checkpoint.\n2. Check whether the Firestore emulator is running and healthy (ps / curl to 8095).\n3. If the emulator is healthy, run the integration suite again standalone (in a low-load state) — the earlier run had 2 jest processes running concurrently (my previous command ran the resolve suite and then the integration test — sequentially, but still). If it's still timing out, compare against the baseline: use git stash to run the same suite at the a9eeff9 baseline? That's risky but reversible. Actually a cleaner approach: use `git worktree` — the main checkout ~/brickspect/dashboard is on the main branch at 450773f, not a9eeff9. Can I create a temporary worktree of the feat branch at a9eeff9? The branch currently has my uncommitted changes, but a worktree checked out at a9eeff9 (detached) would give me a clean baseline. `git worktree add /tmp/baseline-a9eeff9 a9eeff9 --detach`. Then run the same suite there (needs node_modules — share via symlink, or the worktree needs npm install… the dashboard's node_modules — a detached worktree at the repo root would need its own install; but I can symlink node_modules from the main checkout). This is a solid A/B test.\n\nFirst: check the emulator's health and rerun the suite standalone.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bec531c604b6c262","name":"checkpoint_notes","arguments":{"current":"WU1 in progress (parent; worktree .worktrees/records-agent-launch @ a9eeff9, branch feat/records-agent-launch; NO commits; implementation clean). UNIT TESTS ALL GREEN NOW: properties/[id] 14/14, searches/[searchId] 5/5, recorded-documents GET, capabilities, properties list, county-records/resolve 10/10 (fixed stale permissive assertion → review: reason 'review', eta null, /needs review/i + /paused/i). REMAINING WU1: (A) recorded-documents EMULATOR integration suite (__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts) fails 8/8 with 5000ms per-test TIMEOUTS (not assertion failures) — suite header says Firestore emulator at localhost:8085/8095 via jest.setup.integration.js; suite runs 45s total with each test hitting the 5s cap. DIAGNOSIS IN PROGRESS: check emulator health (ps/curl localhost:8095), re-run suite ALONE (no concurrent jest), and if still timing out do an A/B vs baseline: `git worktree add /tmp/baseline-a9eeff9 a9eeff9 --detach` + symlink node_modules, run the same suite there to prove pre-existing env slowness vs my change (my guard adds ONE extra getCountyRecord doc read per GET — shouldn't add seconds; processOneTask path also unchanged for recorded-documents). (B) WU1 tests: reconcile unit matrix (reconciled/already/conflict/gone) — new test file for reconcileWatchlistCounty (mock getFirestoreDb or use emulator); emulator: create legacy county-less property WITH confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot (seed lacks one), reconcile twice → stable county, zero dup tasks/events; route agreement (detail/coverage/list/recorded-read same status+county); review zero-write (resolve/confirm/refresh + recorded search POST → 422, no writes). (C) full unit suite, then commit WU1. THEN WU3 (Copilot CAS+redaction), WU2, WU4-7, WU8, WU9.","completed":["WU1 implementation: all 12 file groups","All WU1-affected unit suites green (resolve 10/10 after stale-expectation fix; properties/[id] 14/14; searches/[searchId] 5/5; recorded-documents GET green)"],"findings]\n[\"recorded-documents emulator integration: 8/8 timeout at 5000ms (per-test) — all tests die in their first emulator round-trip; likely environmental (emulator health/cold start/machine load), not my guard (one extra doc read)\", \"confirmParcel helper in that suite returns revision 2 after resolve+auto-confirm — if my worker review-branch change altered that flow it would fail differently (assertion, not timeout)\"]\n</parameter":"","decisions":["A/B test against a detached a9eeff9 worktree (shared node_modules via symlink) if the standalone re-run still times out — to separate environment slowness from my change before spending more time"],"failed_approaches":["Running the integration suite in the same command as another jest invocation — concurrent load may have contributed to the timeouts; standalone re-run is the next step"],"blockers":[],"verification":["resolve unit 10/10; properties/[id] unit 14/14; searches/[searchId] 5/5; recorded-documents GET unit green"],"next_action":"Check Firestore emulator health (process list + curl localhost:8095), re-run the recorded-documents integration suite standalone; if still all-timeouts, set up the /tmp/baseline-a9eeff9 detached worktree with symlinked node_modules and run the same suite there for the A/B comparison."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":98717,"output":1339,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":411,"totalTokens":100056,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200503118,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b20b9d100453c39c","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
