{"type":"message","id":"085258f5","parentId":"5303388b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:22:40.260Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nThe Firestore emulator is not running (no process, HTTP 000 = connection failure). That explains the 8/8 timeouts: the tests are waiting for a response from localhost:8095 that will never arrive.\n\nSo, how are the other integration tests in this repo being run? There should be a mechanism — maybe jest.setup.integration.js launches the emulator, or the project's convention is to start it manually (scripts/records-local-stack.sh? or `firebase emulators:start`?). The header of the recorded-documents integration test says \"runs against the local Firestore emulator (localhost:8095 — configured by jest.setup.integration.js)\" — \"configured\" (i.e., the env var setting), not \"launched\". So the convention is: the developer starts the emulator separately (probably a script). Let me check jest.setup.integration.js and the package.json scripts / README for the emulator startup procedure.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aae81fc108656810","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat jest.setup.integration.js 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"emulator\" package.json | head; ls scripts/ | grep -i \"emul\\|stack\\|firebase\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":100542,"output":271,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":204,"totalTokens":100813,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200552744,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a8b0488a380e7659","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
