{"type":"message","id":"0a200fb0","parentId":"3aa57391","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:22:40.322Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-aae81fc108656810","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import '@testing-library/jest-dom';\nimport dotenv from 'dotenv';\nimport path from 'path';\n\n// Load environment variables from .env.local if it exists\n// This allows integration tests to access real API keys\ntry {\n  dotenv.config({ path: path.join(process.cwd(), '.env.local') });\n} catch {\n  // .env.local doesn't exist or can't be loaded, which is fine\n}\n\n// Set mock environment variables for tests, but only if they're not already set\n// This allows integration tests to use real values from .env.local\nif (!process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY) {\n  process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY = 'test-api-key';\n}\n\n// Firestore integration tests run against the local emulator only.\n// .env.local (loaded above) can override these; the defaults keep the\n// tests working on a clean checkout with the docker-compose emulator.\nif (!process.env.FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST) {\n  process.env.FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST = 'localhost:8095';\n}\nif (!process.env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID) {\n  process.env.FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID = 'demo-brickspect-dashboard';\n}\n\n// Always set NODE_ENV to test for Jest\nprocess.env.NODE_ENV = 'test';\n\n// Enable development authentication bypass for integration/E2E tests\n// This allows tests to bypass Firebase authentication with mock tokens\nprocess.env.ALLOW_DEV_AUTH = 'true';\n\n// Remove GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID to avoid conflict with dev auth bypass\n// Integration tests mock Firebase authentication and don't need the real project ID\ndelete process.env.GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID;\n\n// The AI provider chain is configured per environment (.env.local), not\n// forced here: chat tests stub the model selection, and the local 9B\n// gateway is the default for developers when LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL is set.\n\n// Don't mock fetch for integration tests - use Node.js built-in fetch\n// Node.js 18+ has built-in fetch available\n\n// Mock TextEncoder and TextDecoder if not available\nglobal.TextEncoder =\n  global.TextEncoder ||\n  class TextEncoder {\n    encode(str) {\n      return new Uint8Array([...str].map((c) => c.charCodeAt(0)));\n    }\n  };\n\nglobal.TextDecoder =\n  global.TextDecoder ||\n  class TextDecoder {\n    decode(bytes) {\n      if (!bytes) return '';\n      return String.fromCharCode(...bytes);\n    }\n  };\n\n// Mock AbortController if not available\nglobal.AbortController =\n  global.AbortController ||\n  class AbortController {\n    constructor() {\n      this.signal = {\n        aborted: false,\n        addEventListener: jest.fn(),\n        removeEventListener: jest.fn(),\n      };\n    }\n\n    abort() {\n      this.signal.aborted = true;\n    }\n  };\n\n// Mock Next.js router for integration tests\njest.mock('next/navigation', () => ({\n  useRouter() {\n    return {\n      push: jest.fn(),\n      replace: jest.fn(),\n      prefetch: jest.fn(),\n    };\n  },\n  useSearchParams() {\n    return new URLSearchParams();\n  },\n  usePathname() {\n    return '';\n  },\n}));\n\n// Clean up after each test\nafterEach(() => {\n  jest.clearAllMocks();\n});\nrecords-local-stack.sh\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200560322}}
{"type":"message","id":"641aa2a0","parentId":"0a200fb0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:22:46.660Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to look into this further. Let me check the details.\n\nThe setup says this: \"The default keeps the tests working with the docker-compose emulator on a clean checkout.\" So the emulator is provided via docker-compose. Let me check the firestore emulator service in docker-compose.yml, and the records-local-stack.sh script (WU6 touches this — maybe it starts the emulator). Let me look at the compose file and the local-stack script.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be6be3dcf725bdcc","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls docker-compose* 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"firestore\\|8095\" docker-compose.yml 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; head -60 scripts/records-local-stack.sh"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":101565,"output":166,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":92,"totalTokens":101731,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200560326,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a7001a0a0aace457","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"c6d1e7cd","parentId":"641aa2a0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:22:46.740Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-be6be3dcf725bdcc","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"docker-compose.yml  232B\n2:  firestore-emulator:\n5:      gcloud emulators firestore start\n6:        --host-port=0.0.0.0:8095\n9:      - '8095:8095'\n===\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Local-stack runbook for the records agent (Task 13).\n#\n#   scripts/records-local-stack.sh start   — bring up the full local stack\n#   scripts/records-local-stack.sh status  — health report (exit 0 = healthy)\n#   scripts/records-local-stack.sh reset   — stop, wipe emulator state +\n#                                            run artifacts, start fresh\n#   scripts/records-local-stack.sh stop    — stop only what `start` started\n#\n# What `start` brings up (in order):\n#   1. Firestore emulator via docker compose (port 8095, project\n#      demo-brickspect-dashboard)\n#   2. MCP server check (default http://localhost:8090/mcp) — checked,\n#      NOT started: it lives in the mcp-server-go repository; if it is\n#      down, the exact remediation commands are printed\n#   3. local 9B model probe (/v1/models) — OPTIONAL; deterministic tests\n#      do not require it (it is reported, never required)\n#   4. `next dev` on a DEDICATED records-test port (3210 by default;\n#      RECORDS_APP_PORT overrides) with fixture-only providers\n#      (COUNTY_RECORDS_MODE=fixture, RECORDED_DOCUMENTS_MODE=fixture) and\n#      dev auth via `npm run dev:bypass` — the exact server pattern of\n#      playwright.agent.config.ts (ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=true,\n#      GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID empty). The production guard lives in\n#      src/lib/auth.ts itself (dev auth throws under NODE_ENV=production,\n#      which `next dev` is not).\n#   5. one agent worker pointed at the emulator\n#\n# PIDs and logs live in .records-local-stack/ (gitignored). `stop` kills\n# only the process trees rooted at the PIDs recorded there and stops\n# the emulator container. It never uses pattern matching (no pkill):\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n}\n[302 more lines]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200566740}}
