{"type":"message","id":"56057f7a","parentId":"eeb9a3f4","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:24:38.790Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-877584a1fa124a1e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"16-import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\n17-\n18-jest.mock('@/lib/firebase/admin', () => ({\n19-  getFirestoreDb: jest.fn(),\n20-}));\n21-\n22-/**\n23- * In-memory stand-in for the users/{uid}/agentTasks chain: refs carry\n24: * their `id`; `runTransaction` runs get/set against the same state map\n25- * (exposed as `state` for persistence assertions).\n26- */\n27-function makeDb(seed: Record<string, object> = {}) {\n28-  const state: Record<string, unknown> = {};\n29-  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(seed)) state[k] = v;\n30-  const leaf = (id: string) => ({\n31-    id,\n32-    get: jest.fn().mockImplementation(() =>\n33-      Promise.resolve({\n34-        exists: state[id] !== undefined,\n35-        id,\n36-        data: () => state[id],\n37-      })\n38-    ),\n39-    set: jest.fn().mockImplementation((data: unknown) => {\n40-      state[id] = data;\n41-      return Promise.resolve();\n42-    }),\n43-    delete: jest.fn().mockImplementation(() => {\n44-      delete state[id];\n45-      return Promise.resolve();\n46-    }),\n47-  });\n48-  const db = {\n49-    state,\n50-    collection: jest.fn().mockReturnValue({\n51-      doc: jest.fn().mockReturnValue({\n52-        collection: jest.fn().mockReturnValue({\n53-          doc: jest.fn().mockImplementation((id: string) => leaf(id)),\n54-        }),\n55-      }),\n56-    }),\n57:    runTransaction: jest\n58-      .fn()\n59-      .mockImplementation(\n60-        (\n61-          fn: (tx: {\n62-            get: (ref: { id: string }) => Promise<unknown>;\n63-            set: (ref: { id: string }, data: unknown) => Promise<unknown>;\n64-          }) => Promise<unknown>\n65-        ) =>\n66-          fn({\n67-            get: (ref: { id: string }) =>\n68-              Promise.resolve({\n69-                exists: state[ref.id] !== undefined,\n70-                id: ref.id,\n71-                data: () => state[ref.id],\n72-              }),\n73-            set: (ref: { id: string }, data: unknown) => {\n74-              state[ref.id] = data;\n75-              return Promise.resolve();\n76-            },\n77-          })\n78-      ),\n79-  };\n80-  return db;\n81-}\n82-\n83-function baseTask(over: Partial<AgentTask> = {}): AgentTask {\n84-  return {\n85-    taskId: 't1',\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788200678790}}
{"type":"message","id":"7c0cdca9","parentId":"56057f7a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:26:08.974Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The harness pattern is clear. There's one problem for my reconcile tests: `tx.set(ref, data, { merge: true })` — the fake's tx.set has to handle the merge options (the 3rd argument). Also, my reconcile code does `propertiesCollection(uid).doc(propertyId)` — that's `db.collection('users').doc(uid).collection('properties').doc(id)`. The existing fake db's chain: `collection()` returns a fixed object, `doc()` returns an object that has `collection()`, which returns an object with `doc(id)`. In the existing makeDb, the mock for `collection().doc().collection().doc` is a single chain that doesn't depend on uid (the state keys are just leaf ids) — for my tests, the state key should be `${uid}:${propertyId}`, or else the doc chain needs to track (uid, id). I'll write my own makeDb variant that handles uid-scoped properties docs and a merge-aware tx.set.\n\nMy reconcile implementation:\n```ts\nconst db = getFirestoreDb();\nreturn db.runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n  const ref = propertiesCollection(uid).doc(propertyId);\n  const doc = await tx.get(ref);\n  ...\n  tx.set(ref, {...}, { merge: true });\n});\n```\npropertiesCollection(uid) = getFirestoreDb().collection('users').doc(uid).collection('properties').\n\nNote: propertiesCollection calls getFirestoreDb() again — the mock returns the same db object (jest.fn() with a mockReturnValue), so no problem.\n\nFake:\n```ts\nfunction makeDb(seed: Record<string, object | undefined> = {}) {\n  const state: Record<string, unknown> = { ...seed };\n  const key = (uid: string, id: string) => `${uid}:${id}`;\n  const users = {\n    doc: (uid: string) => ({\n      collection: (name: string) => {\n        if (name === 'properties') {\n          return {\n            doc: (id: string) => {\n              const k = key(uid, id);\n              return {\n                id,\n                get: () => Promise.resolve({ exists: state[k] !== undefined, id, data: () => state[k] }),\n                set: (data: unknown, opts?: { merge?: boolean }) => {\n                  if (opts?.merge) state[k] = { ...(state[k] as object), ...data };\n                  else state[k] = data;\n                  return Promise.resolve();\n                },\n              };\n            },\n          };\n        }\n        throw new Error('unexpected collection ' + name);\n      },\n    }),\n  };\n  const db = {\n    state,\n    collection: (name: string) => (name === 'users' ? users : (() => { throw new Error('unexpected collection ' + name); })()),\n    runTransaction: (fn) => fn({\n      get: (ref) => { const k = ...; ... } \n    }),\n  };\n}\n```\n\nWait — tx.get(ref) receives a ref object `{id}` from propertiesCollection(uid).doc(propertyId). To resolve the key, the ref needs to carry the uid. I can make the leaf doc object `{ id, uid }` — an extra property doesn't break the types. In runTransaction, `get: (ref) => { const k = `${(ref as {uid:string}).uid}:${ref.id}`; return Promise.resolve({exists: state[k]!==undefined, id: ref.id, data: () => state[k]}); }`, and `set: (ref, data, opts) => { const k = ...; merge or replace; }`.\n\nTest cases:\n1. property_gone: no seed → {status:'property_gone'}, state unchanged (no key).\n2. reconciled: seed {address: 'x'} (no county) → outcome is reconciled, county is written with countyReconciledFrom=sourceId, countyReconciledAt is a string; the second call → already_reconciled (county exists and same base), county is unchanged (same object reference value), no new writes (verify with a jest.fn call counter on set, or the state value equality + set call count == 1).\n3. already_reconciled (explicit same base, different token): seed county {code:'cuyahoga', name:'Cuyahoga'} (bare slug) and reconcile with {code:'cuyahoga-oh'} → same base → already_reconciled, stored is returned, no writes.\n4. explicit_conflict: seed county {code:'summit-oh'}, reconcile with cuyahoga-oh → explicit_conflict, no writes, stored county is unchanged.\n5. error propagation: make tx.get reject → expect the reject to propagate (not be swallowed).\n\nAlso verify that a merge write doesn't drop existing fields (seed has address; after reconcile, the address remains).\n\nWhere to put it: a new file src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts.\n\nI'll write this now.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaa0a94f67cd0f76","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"/**\n * Unit tests for reconcileWatchlistCounty — the transactional, idempotent\n * county reconciliation (the ONLY write path for non-explicit counties).\n *\n * The fake Firestore below mirrors the agent-tasks-retry harness: an\n * in-memory `state` map that `tx.get`/`tx.set` operate on, so the\n * read-check-write of the transaction is observable as real persistence.\n */\nimport { reconcileWatchlistCounty } from '../properties';\nimport { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport type { CountyIdentity } from '@/types/records-dashboard';\n\njest.mock('@/lib/firebase/admin', () => ({\n  getFirestoreDb: jest.fn(),\n}));\n\nconst CUYAHOGA: CountyIdentity = { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' };\nconst SUMMIT: CountyIdentity = { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' };\n\ntype FakeDoc = {\n  id: string;\n  get: () => Promise<unknown>;\n  set: (data: unknown, opts?: { merge?: boolean }) => Promise<void>;\n};\ntype FakeDb = {\n  state: Record<string, unknown>;\n  collection: (name: string) => unknown;\n  runTransaction: (\n    fn: (tx: {\n      get: (ref: FakeDoc) => Promise<unknown>;\n      set: (ref: FakeDoc, data: unknown, opts?: { merge?: boolean }) => Promise<void>;\n    }) => Promise<unknown>\n  ) => Promise<unknown>;\n};\n\nfunction makeDb(seed: Record<string, object | undefined> = {}) {\n  const state: Record<string, unknown> = { ...seed };\n  const key = (doc: FakeDoc) =>\n    `${(doc as { uid?: string }).uid ?? 'default'}:${doc.id}`;\n\n  const propertyDoc = (uid: string, id: string): FakeDoc => ({\n    id,\n    get: () =>\n      Promise.resolve({\n        exists: state[`${uid}:${id}`] !== undefined,\n        id,\n        data: () => state[`${uid}:${id}`],\n      }),\n    set: (data, opts) => {\n      if (opts?.merge) {\n        state[`${uid}:${id}`] = {\n          ...((state[`${uid}:${id}`] as object) ?? {}),\n          ...data,\n        };\n      } else {\n        state[`${uid}:${id}`] = data;\n      }\n      return Promise.resolve();\n    },\n  });\n\n  const db: FakeDb = {\n    state,\n    collection: jest.fn((name: string) => {\n      if (name === 'users') {\n        return {\n          doc: (uid: string) => ({\n            collection: (sub: string) => {\n              if (sub === 'properties') {\n                return {\n                  doc: (id: string) =>\n                    Object.assign(propertyDoc(uid, id), { uid }),\n                };\n              }\n              throw new Error(`unexpected collection ${sub}`);\n            },\n          }),\n        };\n      }\n      throw new Error(`unexpected collection ${name}`);\n    }),\n    runTransaction: jest.fn((fn) =>\n      fn({\n        get: (ref) =>\n          Promise.resolve({\n            exists: state[`${(ref as { uid?: string }).uid ?? 'default'}:${ref.id}`] !== undefined,\n            id: ref.id,\n            data: () =>\n              state[`${(ref as { uid?: string }).uid ?? 'default'}:${ref.id}`],\n          }),\n        set: (ref, data, opts) => {\n          const k = `${(ref as { uid?: string }).uid ?? 'default'}:${ref.id}`;\n          if (opts?.merge) {\n            state[k] = { ...(state[k] as object), ...data };\n          } else {\n            state[k] = data;\n          }\n          return Promise.resolve();\n        },\n      })\n    ),\n  };\n  (getFirestoreDb as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue(db);\n  return db;\n}\n\ndescribe('reconcileWatchlistCounty', () => {\n  it('reconciles a county-less legacy property (merge write with provenance metadata)', async () => {\n    const db = makeDb({\n      'u1:prop-1': { address: '1 Main St', capturedAt: '2026-08-01T00:00:00Z' },\n    });\n\n    const outcome = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1',\n      'prop-1',\n      CUYAHOGA,\n      'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n\n    expect(outcome).toEqual({ status: 'reconciled', county: CUYAHOGA });\n    const stored = db.state['u1:prop-1'] as Record<string, unknown>;\n    // Merge write: pre-existing fields survive, provenance is recorded.\n    expect(stored.address).toBe('1 Main St');\n    expect(stored.county).toEqual(CUYAHOGA);\n    expect(stored.countyReconciledFrom).toBe('cuyahoga-fixture');\n    expect(typeof stored.countyReconciledAt).toBe('string');\n  });\n\n  it('is idempotent: a second reconcile is already_reconciled with no write', async () => {\n    const db = makeDb({\n      'u1:prop-1': { address: '1 Main St', capturedAt: '2026-08-01T00:00:00Z' },\n    });\n\n    const first = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1', 'prop-1', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n    expect(first.status).toBe('reconciled');\n    const afterFirst = db.state['u1:prop-1'];\n    const setCallsAfterFirst = (\n      db.runTransaction as jest.Mock\n    ).mock.results.length;\n\n    const second = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1', 'prop-1', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n    expect(second.status).toBe('already_reconciled');\n    expect(second.county).toEqual(CUYAHOGA);\n    // No second write: the persisted document is byte-identical.\n    expect(db.state['u1:prop-1']).toEqual(afterFirst);\n    // The second transaction ran (it must read to decide) but wrote nothing.\n    expect((db.runTransaction as jest.Mock).mock.results.length).toBe(\n      setCallsAfterFirst + 1\n    );\n  });\n\n  it('treats a same-base explicit county (different token) as already reconciled', async () => {\n    // Bare slug vs registry slug: same county after the state token is\n    // stripped — idempotent, and the stored identity is returned as-is.\n    const storedCounty = { code: 'cuyahoga', name: 'Cuyahoga County' };\n    const db = makeDb({\n      'u1:prop-1': { county: storedCounty, address: '1 Main St' },\n    });\n\n    const outcome = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1', 'prop-1', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n\n    expect(outcome).toEqual({\n      status: 'already_reconciled',\n      county: storedCounty,\n    });\n    expect(db.state['u1:prop-1']).toEqual({\n      county: storedCounty,\n      address: '1 Main St',\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('never overwrites a conflicting explicit county (explicit_conflict, zero writes)', async () => {\n    const storedCounty = SUMMIT;\n    const db = makeDb({\n      'u1:prop-1': { county: storedCounty, address: '1 Main St' },\n    });\n\n    const outcome = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1', 'prop-1', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n\n    expect(outcome.status).toBe('explicit_conflict');\n    if (outcome.status === 'explicit_conflict') {\n      expect(outcome.stored).toEqual(SUMMIT);\n      expect(outcome.county).toEqual(CUYAHOGA);\n    }\n    // The explicit assertion survives untouched — no countyReconciledFrom\n    // metadata, no county change.\n    expect(db.state['u1:prop-1']).toEqual({\n      county: SUMMIT,\n      address: '1 Main St',\n    });\n  });\n\n  it('reports property_gone without a write', async () => {\n    const db = makeDb({});\n\n    const outcome = await reconcileWatchlistCounty(\n      'u1', 'prop-404', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture'\n    );\n\n    expect(outcome).toEqual({ status: 'property_gone' });\n    expect(db.state).toEqual({});\n  });\n\n  it('propagates persistence failures (never swallows them)', async () => {\n    const db = makeDb({ 'u1:prop-1': { address: '1 Main St' } });\n    (db.runTransaction as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(\n      new Error('transaction aborted')\n    );\n\n    await expect(\n      reconcileWatchlistCounty('u1', 'prop-1', CUYAHOGA, 'cuyahoga-fixture')\n    ).rejects.toThrow('transaction aborted');\n  });\n});\n","path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":107845,"output":3347,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1099,"totalTokens":111192,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788200678794,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a90b8225e20464b7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
