{"type":"message","id":"6ff13d63","parentId":"210dfbdc","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:27:36.866Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reconcile unit matrix: 6/6 green on the first run. Next up is the emulator integration test. Model it on the recorded-documents integration test. Key questions:\n\n1. What does the seed do — I need to create a property with county:null (legacy). The recorded-documents test uses `upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, WATCH_SNAPSHOT)` with county set. I'll make it county: null.\n2. Task/enqueue helpers: `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(uid, propertyId, 'county_resolve', { expectedRevision: 0, address: ADDR }, 0)` followed by `processOneTask(enq.task, { workerId })`.\n3. After auto-confirm, the worker calls reconcileCountyBestEffort → reconcileWatchlistCounty writes county+countyReconciledFrom+countyReconciledAt to the property document.\n4. How to read the raw property document (including the extra fields countyReconciledFrom/At)? `getWatchlistItem` returns a WatchlistItem (parsed) — the extra fields aren't included in the type. To assert on countyReconciledFrom, I need the raw document. I can use getFirestoreDb() directly inside the test to read the raw document: `getFirestoreDb().collection('users').doc(uid).collection('properties').doc(propertyId).get()`.\n5. Counting tasks/events: collections users/{uid}/agentTasks and users/{uid}/agentEvents (need to verify the actual collection names — the agent-worker enqueues to some collection; let me check the names in the firestore library). Let me check what enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent writes to and which event collection exists.\n\nAlso, about the \"zero duplicate tasks\" assertion: the second reconcile call is a direct function call (not a task) — it shouldn't enqueue anything; the assertion is that the task count doesn't change after the second reconcile. And events too: the worker flow may create events (task lifecycle events). Count before/after.\n\nLet me chec