{"type":"message","id":"bd8417e2","parentId":"354a023d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:30:42.704Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9b7dd6c8869f6bb5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"295- * `revision`, and (when current) insert the task with its idempotency key\n296- * (Task 4). This is the seam the domain routes use: a stale caller can\n297- * never enqueue work against superseded state, and duplicate requests with\n298- * the same action + revision return the same task.\n299- */\n300:export async function enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(\n301-  uid: string,\n302-  propertyId: string,\n303-  kind: AgentTaskKind,\n304-  input: Record<string, unknown>,\n305-  expectedRevision: number\n306-): Promise<CountyEnqueueResult> {\n307-  const db = getFirestoreDb();\n308-  return db.runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n309-    const doc = await tx.get(countyRecordRef(uid, propertyId));\n310-    const current = doc.exists ? normalizeStoredRecord(doc.data()) : null;\n311-    if (current && current.revision !== expectedRevision) {\n312-      return {\n313-        stale: current,\n314-        task: null,\n315-        created: false,\n316-        recordRevision: current.revision,\n317-      };\n318-    }\n319-    const { task, created } = await enqueueTaskInTransaction(tx, {\n320-      ownerUid: uid,\n321-      kind,\n322-      propertyId,\n323-      input,\n324-      idempotencyKey: buildTaskIdempotencyKey(\n325-        kind,\n326-        propertyId,\n327-        expectedRevision\n328-      ),\n329-    });\n330-    return {\n331-      stale: null,\n332-      task,\n333-      created,\n334-      recordRevision: current?.revision ?? 0,\n335-    };\n336-  });\n337-}\n338-\n339-/**\n340- * Persist the result of a resolution run (CAS).\n341- *\n342- * - `expectedRevision` is the revision the CALLER observed (0 for a\n343- *   property with no record yet, or a legacy record). A mismatch aborts\n344- *   with `CountyRecordChangedError`.\n345- * - On success the record's revision bumps by 1 and the canonical\n346- *   `county_record_resolved` event commits in the same transaction.\n347- * - A prior snapshot (from an earlier confirmed parcel) is PRESERVED — a\n348- *   failed/empty re-resolution never destroys last-known-good.\n349- * - Throws `Error('Property not in your watchlist')` when the property\n350- *   isn't owned by `uid` (caller maps to 404).\n351- */\n352-export async function saveResolution(\n353-  uid: string,\n354-  propertyId: string,\n355-  args: {\n356-    status: 'confirmation_required' | 'no_match' | 'unsupported_county';\n357-    resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress;\n358-    /** Raw candidates (any count) — bounded + stripped here. */\n359-    candidates: ParcelCandidate[] | null;\n360-    unsupportedReason?: 'state_not_supported' | 'provider_unsupported' | null;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788201042704}}
{"type":"message","id":"41d66211","parentId":"bd8417e2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:31:00.772Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\n`enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent` has no coverage gate (it's a pure revision-CAS + idempotency enqueue). The coverage gate is on the route side (before enqueue). So in the integration test we can enqueue directly regardless of coverage — the worker's `requireLiveCounty` is the second line of defense, and this is exactly what test 3 is trying to verify (the worker-level fail-closed when the route gate is bypassed / state has changed).\n\nTest 3 flow:\n1. Seed a property with an explicit Summit county.\n2. Enqueue county_resolve (expectedRevision 0) + processOneTask → worker: requireLiveCounty(item Summit, record null) → resolveCountyCoverage(Summit, null) → 'planned' → throws WorkerBlockedError('unsupported_county') → blocked before search! Damn — the worker gates before the provider call. So we can't reach auto-confirm via resolve with an explicit Summit.\n\nAlternative honest path for test 3: seed a county record with a confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot directly (simulating a past confirmation — e.g. the property previously had no county, was confirmed, and then the user PATCHed to Summit → contradiction). Seeding the county record directly: use a firestore helper — is there a `setCountyRecord` / direct-write function? saveResolution/saveConfirmation are CAS operations with domain invariants. In the test we can use getFirestoreDb() directly to write the record document (the test is allowed to write raw state for setup purposes — other integration tests do the same kind of seeding). The shape of the record document needs to match normalizeStoredRecord's expectations: status 'confirmed', revision, snapshot {parcel..., provenance {sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture', ...}}.\n\nLet me check the shape of StoredCountyRecord + normalizeStoredRecord + a sample of a confirmed snapshot (from the recorded-documents test? That one didn't seed a record. Let me check the saved shape in saveConfirmation in county-records.ts).\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab111931787f7018","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"interface StoredCountyRecord\" -A 25 src/types/county-records.ts; grep -n \"export async function saveConfirmation\" -A 45 src/lib/firestore/county-records.ts | sed -n '1,50p'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":125885,"output":520,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":436,"totalTokens":126405,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788201042709,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b0cb28b3d0da453d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"2b8a9bd9","parentId":"41d66211","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:31:00.839Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-ab111931787f7018","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"192:export interface StoredCountyRecord {\n193-  schemaVersion: typeof COUNTY_RECORDS_SCHEMA_VERSION;\n194-  /**\n195-   * Denormalized owner (the document always lives under `users/{uid}`;\n196-   * server consumers must never re-derive identity from the path alone).\n197-   * Backfilled from the path on the first CAS write of a legacy doc.\n198-   */\n199-  ownerUid: string;\n200-  /**\n201-   * Monotonic optimistic-concurrency revision. Legacy (pre-CAS) documents\n202-   * carry no field and READ as 0; the first CAS transition bumps them to 1.\n203-   * Every committed transition (success or failure) bumps by exactly 1,\n204-   * atomically with the record write and its canonical outbox event.\n205-   */\n206-  revision: number;\n207-  /** When this record was first stored (ISO). Legacy: backfilled from `updatedAt`. */\n208-  createdAt: string;\n209-  status: StoredCountyRecordStatus;\n210-  /** The normalized address last resolved (drift detection). */\n211-  resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress | null;\n212-  /** Pending candidates (only in confirmation_required). Bounded. */\n213-  candidates: StoredCandidate[] | null;\n214-  /** Last successfully retrieved snapshot (last-known-good). */\n215-  snapshot: CountyParcelSnapshot | null;\n216-  unsupportedReason: 'state_not_supported' | 'provider_unsupported' | null;\n217-  lastRefresh: {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788201060839}}
{"type":"message","id":"3c8dfa53","parentId":"2b8a9bd9","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:31:48.528Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nAdvisory only — no action required. I'm past the checkpoint deadline (since the 26th generation, the only new info is the enqueue seam's behavior — no coverage gate; and the shape of StoredCountyRecord). I'll commit a checkpoint including these, and then write the integration tests.\n\nI still need the shape of CountyParcelSnapshot (the required fields) in order to seed a confirmed snapshot. I'll check the type and what the fixture returns (I'll copy from fixtures.ts, which constructs a complete snapshot with all the fields around lines 185-196). Also the shape of NormalizedPropertyAddress. Rather than reconstructing it by hand, an honest alternative: use the fixture provider directly inside the test to obtain the snapshot: `new CuyahogaRecorderFixtureProvider()` — no wait, that's the recorded-documents provider. The county fixture provider: CuyahogaArcGisFixtureProvider? In the recorded-documents integration tests, `recordedCtx` used `new CuyahogaRecorderFixtureProvider()` for recorded documents. For county records, the worker uses getCountyRecordsProvider(county), and in fixture mode it returns the county fixture provider — let me check what its snapshot looks like (the fixture provider in fixtures.ts, around line 185). If the provider exposes searchAddress/confirmParcel methods, I can use it in the test to generate an authentic snapshot and seed the record with the same fields the worker writes — that would be the most honest approach.\n\nA simpler and equally honest way: seed the record via the actual worker flow, but from a state where the gate passes: property with no county (legacy) → resolve → auto-confirmed (Cuyahoga, r2) → then PATCH the property's county to Summit (via updateWatchlistItemCounty — the actual seam) → this is exactly the real-world contradiction: confirmed Cuyahoga parcel + a user assertion of Summit. Then enqueue county_refresh (expectedRevision 2) → processOneTask → requireLiveCounty → review → blocked county_review. No raw seeding needed! The only raw operation is the user PATCH, and that goes through a real function.\n\nTest 3 flow (all real seams):\n1. Seed a legacy property with no county.\n2. Enqueue county_resolve (rev 0) + processOneTask → auto-confirmed r2; the worker reconciles the county to Cuyahoga (that's test 1's behavior — no problem, it's consistent).\n3. updateWatchlistItemCounty(uid, pid, SUMMIT) → the user asserts Summit (the real PATCH seam). Now: county Cuyahoga? No — updateWatchlistItemCounty overwrites the stored county to Summit. Wait: after step 2, the property's county = Cuyahoga (reconciled). PATCHing to Summit overwrites it → explicit Summit + confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot → contradiction → review.\n4. Enqueue county_refresh (expectedRevision 2) + processOneTask → blocked, code 'county_review'.\n5. Assert: the task's status is 'blocked' and error.code is 'county_review'; the property's county is still Summit; the county record's revision is still 2 (no refresh write); the snapshot is unchanged.\n\nThis is a fully honest test.\n\nRegarding the zero-write count in test 2: count the user documents before and after the second reconcile.\n\nI'll write the file now. I'll copy the imports and the ADDR constant from the recorded-documents integration tests. processOneTask import, upsertWatchlistItem, getWatchlistItem, updateWatchlistItemCounty, reconcileWatchlistCounty from '@/lib/firestore/properties'; enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent + getCountyRecord from '@/lib/firestore/county-records'; getAgentTask from '@/lib/firestore/agent-tasks' (confirm the function name — for reading the task document after processOneTask: processOneTask probably returns the result; the recorded-documents tests didn't read the task. I'll check the name of the task-reading helper: get