{"type":"message","id":"97fac1b1","parentId":"19acd2ab","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:35:08.860Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a1524a8a5b886dde","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":" * Confirm one of the stored candidates (CAS).\n *\n * - `objectId` must be a stored candidate; the parcel is RE-FETCHED by the\n *   caller before this is called, so the stored snapshot is always a\n *   verified current copy.\n * - `expectedRevision` is the caller's observed revision.\n * - Idempotent replay: if the record is ALREADY confirmed for this\n *   objectId, the current record is returned without a revision bump and\n *   without duplicating the event.\n * - Returns null when the property isn't owned or no record exists.\n * - Throws `CountyCandidateMismatchError` for unknown objectId / wrong\n *   status; `CountyRecordChangedError` on a revision conflict.\n */\nexport async function confirmCountyParcel(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  args: {\n    objectId: number;\n    parcelId: string;\n    parcelIdFormatted: string;\n    resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress;\n    snapshot: CountyParcelSnapshot;\n    expectedRevision: number;\n  },\n  options?: CasOptions\n): Promise<StoredCountyRecord | null> {\n  const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n  if (!item) return null;\n\n  const now = new Date().toISOString();\n  const result = await casTransition(\n    uid,\n    propertyId,\n    args.expectedRevision,\n    options,\n    (tx, current) => {\n      void tx;\n      if (!current) return { kind: 'no_record' };\n\n      // Idempotent replay of the winner (same parcel already confirmed):\n      // no revision bump, no duplicated event.\n      if (\n        current.status === 'confirmed' &&\n        current.snapshot?.provenance.objectId === args.objectId\n      ) {\n        return { kind: 'idempotent', current };\n      }\n      if (current.status !== 'confirmation_required') {\n        return { kind: 'candidate_mismatch' };\n      }\n      if (!current.candidates?.some((c) => c.objectId === args.objectId)) {\n        return { kind: 'candidate_mismatch' };\n      }\n\n      const updated: StoredCountyRecord = {\n        ...current,\n        schemaVersion: COUNTY_RECORDS_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n        revision: current.revision + 1,\n        status: 'confirmed',\n        candidates: null,\n        snapshot: args.snapshot,\n        unsupportedReason: null,\n        lastRefresh: { at: now, ok: true, error: null },\n        updatedAt: now,\n      };\n      return {\n        kind: 'write',\n        record: updated,\n        eventType: 'county_record_confirmed',\n      };\n    }\n  );\n\n  if (result.kind === 'idempotent') return result.current;\n  if (result.kind === 'no_record') return null;\n  if (result.kind === 'candidate_mismatch')\n    throw new CountyCandidateMismatchError();\n  if (result.kind === 'conflict')\n    throw new CountyRecordChangedError(result.current);\n  return result.record;\n}\n\n/**\n * Record a successful refresh (CAS): replace the confirmed snapshot.\n *\n * - `expectedRevision` is the caller's observed revision; a concurrent\n *   writer that advanced it wins (this call surfaces\n *   `CountyRecordChangedError` — the route 409s).\n * - Bumps the revision and commits `county_record_refreshed` atomically.\n * - Returns null when the property isn't owned, no record exists, or the\n *   record is not in a refreshable (confirmed) state.\n */\nexport async function saveCountySnapshot(\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788201308860}}
{"type":"message","id":"d69d0326","parentId":"97fac1b1","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:35:45.814Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nAdvisory only — no action needed. I'm past the checkpoint deadline. Changes since generation 28: I've read the signature of confirmCountyParcel (arguments: objectId, parcelId, parcelIdFormatted, resolvedAddress, snapshot (complete CountyParcelSnapshot including provenance), expectedRevision). Seeding requires the following: saveResolution (with a candidate) → confirmCountyParcel with the complete CountyParcelSnapshot (provenance's sourceId is 'cuyahoga-fixture', objectId matching the candidate).\n\nThe remaining big question is the snapshot shape — CountyParcelSnapshot is a large interface (schemaVersion, parcelId, parcelIdFormatted, address{}, owner, valuation{}, taxes{}, transfer{}, …, provenance{}, …). Hand-assembling it in the test is error-prone but feasible — or, better yet, get an authentic snapshot from the county fixture provider itself: the worker's fixture provider has a fetch/refresh method that returns a snapshot. Check the provider interface: CuyahogaArcGisFixtureProvider (fixtures.ts L196 `readonly source = ...`, around L185 sourceId 'cuyahoga-fixture'). It should have methods like resolveCandidates(address) and fetchParcel(objectId/parcelId) → CountyParcelSnapshot. If the test can call the fixture provider directly (new CuyahogaFixtureProvider()), we can obtain a genuine snapshot for the fixture address — the most authentic seeding.\n\nLet me check the provider interface and the fixture provider's methods. Also, what does the worker's confirm path call in order to re-fetch the parcel (around line 555 of the worker: confirmCountyParcel(...) with the snapshot from …). Let me look at the worker's runCountyConfirm to copy the exact provider call.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-afe371e72dcc0db3","name":"checkpoint_notes","arguments":{"current":"WU1 in progress (parent; worktree .worktrees/records-agent-launch @ a9eeff9, branch feat/records-agent-launch; NO commits; implementation clean; emulator UP on :8095). STATUS: all existing tests green; reconcile unit matrix 6/6 PASS. REWRITING county-reconcile integration test (old draft unreachable: audited worker blocks county-less props pre-provider). VERIFIED SEAMS: saveResolution(uid,pid,{status:'confirmation_required'|'no_match'|'unsupported_county', resolvedAddress, candidates, lastRefresh, expectedRevision}, casOptions) → r1; confirmCountyParcel(uid,pid,{objectId, parcelId, parcelIdFormatted, resolvedAddress, snapshot: CountyParcelSnapshot, expectedRevision}, options?) → confirmed r2 (idempotent on same objectId). NEXT: (1) find how the WORKER re-fetches the snapshot before confirmCountyParcel (read runCountyConfirm ~L540-575 of agent-worker.ts: which provider method, e.g. provider.fetchParcel / snapshotFor) — copy that call so the test's seeded snapshot is GENUINE fixture output (provider = getCountyRecordsProvider(CUYAHOGA) in fixture mode, or new CuyahogaArcGisFixtureProvider() if exported from fixtures.ts — verify export name); (2) rewrite test: seed property county:null → saveResolution(candidates=[one fixture candidate for 5180 broadview road]) → confirmCountyParcel(snapshot from provider) → THEN Test A: run county_refresh via processOneTask → worker reconciles county (county+countyReconciledFrom persisted); Test B: direct 2nd reconcileWatchlistCounty → already_reconciled + countUserDocs unchanged; Test C: updateWatchlistItemCounty(SUMMIT) → county_refresh → blocked 'county_review', zero writes. REMAINING: route-agreement tests + confirm/refresh/search-POST zero-write route tests; full unit suite; commit WU1. THEN WU3, WU2, WU4-7, WU8, WU9.","completed":["WU1 implementation: all 12 file groups (clean)","All existing unit + recorded-documents emulator tests green","Reconcile unit matrix 6/6 P