{"type":"message","id":"f6a3cf7a","parentId":"39bc1930","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:35:50.701Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a2b1b2c5c12e6ce7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"async function runCountyConfirm(\n  task: AgentTask,\n  ctx: WorkerContext\n): Promise<TaskSuccess> {\n  // SAFETY: the county confirm route builds this exact shape at enqueue\n  // time (objectId from the stored candidates, never the requester's raw\n  // parcel payload).\n  const input = task.input as unknown as CountyConfirmInput;\n  const uid = task.ownerUid;\n  const propertyId = task.propertyId;\n  const item = await requireWatchlistProperty(uid, propertyId);\n\n  const current = await getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId);\n  if (!current) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'no_record',\n      'There is no stored county record to confirm against.'\n    );\n  }\n\n  // M1 coverage gate (re-verified at run time; zero writes on failure).\n  const coverage = await requireLiveCounty(item, current, input.county);\n  const provider = providerFor(ctx, coverage.county);\n  const snapshot = await provider.fetchParcelSnapshot(\n    input.objectId,\n    scenarioOption(ctx)\n  );\n  if (snapshot === null) {\n    // Best-effort failure record (the caller's follow-up GET is the source\n    // of truth; a persistence conflict is logged, not propagated).\n    const info: CountyRecordsErrorInfo = {\n      code: 'parcel_gone',\n      message: publicMessageFor('parcel_gone'),\n    };\n    try {\n      if (current.snapshot) {\n        await recordCountyRefreshFailure(\n          uid,\n          propertyId,\n          info,\n          current.revision\n        );\n      } else if (current.resolvedAddress) {\n        await recordResolutionFailure(uid, propertyId, {\n          resolvedAddress: current.resolvedAddress,\n          error: info,\n          expectedRevision: current.revision,\n        });\n      }\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.warn(\n        `[agent-worker] best-effort confirm-failure record failed: ${String(error)}`\n      );\n    }\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n===FIXTURES===\n195:export class CuyahogaFixtureProvider implements CountyRecordsProvider {\n196:  readonly source = {\n223:  async resolveCandidates(\n275:  async fetchParcelSnapshot(\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788201350701}}
{"type":"message","id":"c1ba2b81","parentId":"f6a3cf7a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:36:21.219Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to look into this further. Let me check the details.\n\nThe worker's confirm path: `provider.fetchParcelSnapshot(objectId, scenario)` → CountyParcelSnapshot | null. The fixture provider `CuyahogaFixtureProvider` is exported from fixtures.ts. So in the test:\n\n```ts\nimport { CuyahogaFixtureProvider } from '@/lib/county-records/fixtures';\nconst provider = new CuyahogaFixtureProvider();\nconst candidates = await provider.resolveCandidates(ADDR);  // for the fixture address → 1 candidate\nconst snapshot = await provider.fetchParcelSnapshot(candidates[0].objectId);\n```\n\nThen seed: upsertWatchlistItem (county null) → saveResolution({status:'confirmation_required', resolvedAddress: ADDR, candidates, lastRefresh: {at, ok:true, error:null}, expectedRevision:0}) → confirmCountyParcel({objectId: candidates[0].objectId, parcelId: candidates[0].parcelId, parcelIdFormatted: candidates[0].parcelIdFormatted, resolvedAddress: ADDR, snapshot, expectedRevision:1}) → confirmed r2.\n\nWait — I need to check the exact argument type of saveResolution: {status, resolvedAddress, candidates, unsupportedReason?, lastRefresh?, expectedRevision}. From my earlier reading: `args: { status: 'confirmation_required'|'no_match'|'unsupported_county'; resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress; candidates: ParcelCandidate[] | null; unsupportedReason?: ... }` — and does it also take lastRefresh + expectedRevision? I saw that the worker's call to saveResolution includes lastRefresh and expectedRevision. Also, saveResolution takes casOptions as the 3rd argument — optional? The worker passes casOptionsFor(task). In the test, I can pass {actor:'test', taskRef:'seed'} — let me check the CasOptions type (from county-records.ts or types). The confirm/refresh calls pass an options?: CasOptions — optional, so omitting it is fine.\n\nAlso note: saveResolution's candidates type is ParcelCandidate[] (raw) — \"bounded + stripped here\". The fixture's resolveCandidates returns ParcelCandidate[] (the provider's raw candidates). Good — pass it through as-is.\n\nAnother nuance: `confirmCountyParcel` requires that the item exists in the watchlist (getWatchlistItem) — our seed has that.\n\nAnd the refresh test: `saveCountySnapshot` (L516) is the refresh write — the worker's runCountyRefresh calls provider.fetchParcelSnapshot then saveCountySnapshot. In test A, we run the actual worker's county_refresh via processOneTask — no raw seeding of the snapshot needed there.\n\nThe test file plan (rewritten):\n\n```ts\ndescribe('county reconciliation (emulator)', () => {\n  const provider = new CuyahogaFixtureProvider();\n  let candidates: ParcelCandidate[];\n  let snapshot: CountyParcelSnapshot;\n\n  beforeAll(async () => {\n    candidates = await provider.resolveCandidates(ADDR);\n    snapshot = (await provider.fetchParcelSnapshot(candidates[0].objectId))!;\n  });\n\n  async function seedLegacyConfirmed(uid, propertyId) {\n    await upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, {...county: null...});\n    const r1 = await saveResolution(uid, propertyId, {\n      status: 'confirmation_required',\n      resolvedAddress: ADDR,\n      candidates,\n      lastRefresh: { at: new Date().toISOString(), ok: true, error: null },\n      expectedRevision: 0,\n    });\n    // confirm via the real CAS seam\n    const c0 = candidates[0];\n    await confirmCountyParcel(uid, propertyId, {\n      objectId: c0.objectId,\n      parcelId: c0.parcelId,\n      parcelIdFormatted: c0.parcelIdFormatted,\n      resolvedAddress: ADDR,\n      snapshot,\n      expectedRevision: 1,\n    });\n  }\n  ...\n```\n\nHmm, wait — I need to double-check the argument order of saveResolution and the lastRefresh requirement. Also, whether saveResolution is a 3-arg form (uid, propertyId, args, options?) — from the worker's usage: `saveResolution(uid, propertyId, {...}, casOptionsFor(task))`. And is lastRefresh required? The worker's call included it. Let me quickly check the exact argument type before writing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaf3e84dc119f299","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '352,400p' src/lib/firestore/county-records.ts; grep -n \"interface CasOptions\\|type CasOptions\" -A 8 src/types/county-records.ts src/lib/firestore/county-records.ts 2>/dev/null | head -14"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":140593,"output":1032,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":939,"totalTokens":141625,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788201350705,"responseId":"chatcmpl-934f23e3b7fbec23","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"8bbd9e33","parentId":"c1ba2b81","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:36:21.282Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-aaf3e84dc119f299","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export async function saveResolution(\n  uid: string,\n  propertyId: string,\n  args: {\n    status: 'confirmation_required' | 'no_match' | 'unsupported_county';\n    resolvedAddress: NormalizedPropertyAddress;\n    /** Raw candidates (any count) — bounded + stripped here. */\n    candidates: ParcelCandidate[] | null;\n    unsupportedReason?: 'state_not_supported' | 'provider_unsupported' | null;\n    lastRefresh: {\n      at: string;\n      ok: boolean;\n      error: CountyRecordsErrorInfo | null;\n    } | null;\n    expectedRevision: number;\n  },\n  options?: CasOptions\n): Promise<StoredCountyRecord> {\n  const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n  if (!item) throw new Error('Property not in your watchlist');\n\n  const now = new Date().toISOString();\n  const result = await casTransition(\n    uid,\n    propertyId,\n    args.expectedRevision,\n    options,\n    (tx, current) => {\n      void tx;\n      const stored: StoredCountyRecord = {\n        schemaVersion: COUNTY_RECORDS_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n        ownerUid: uid,\n        revision: (current?.revision ?? 0) + 1,\n        createdAt: current?.createdAt ?? current?.updatedAt ?? now,\n        status: args.status,\n        resolvedAddress: args.resolvedAddress,\n        candidates:\n          args.status === 'confirmation_required' && args.candidates != null\n            ? toStoredCandidates(args.candidates)\n            : null,\n        // Last-known-good survives any re-resolution outcome.\n        snapshot: current?.snapshot ?? null,\n        unsupportedReason:\n          args.status === 'unsupported_county'\n            ? (args.unsupportedReason ?? null)\n            : null,\n        lastRefresh: args.lastRefresh,\n        updatedAt: now,\n      };\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts:76:export interface CasOptions {\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-77-  delayBeforeCommitMs?: number;\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-78-  /**\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-79-   * Who committed the transition (recorded on the outbox event): `client`\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-80-   * for the synchronous API path, `worker` for the durable agent worker.\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-81-   */\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-82-  actor?: 'client' | 'worker';\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-83-  /** The agent task that produced the transition (worker path). */\nsrc/lib/firestore/county-records.ts-84-  taskRef?: string | null;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788201381281}}
{"type":"message","id":"0bf96f82","parentId":"8bbd9e33","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:36:35.616Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All shapes confirmed. Next, rewrite the integration test. Details:\n\n- `saveResolution(uid, propertyId, { status:'confirmation_required', resolvedAddress: ADDR, candidates, lastRefresh: {at, ok:true, error:null}, expectedRevision: 0 })` → r1.\n- `confirmCountyParcel(uid, propertyId, { objectId, parcelId, parcelIdFormatted, resolvedAddress: ADDR, snapshot, expectedRevision: 1 })` → confirmed r2.\n- Test A (worker-driven reconciliation): seed the legacy confirmed state → countUserDocs → enqueue county_refresh (expectedRevision 2) → processOneTask → assert that the task succeeded, that the property's county = Cuyahoga, that countyReconciledFrom = 'cuyahoga-fixture', and that the user document count did not increase... no, wait — a successful refresh does write to the county record (saveCountySnapshot r3) + event. So the count does change. The zero-write assertion belongs to Test B (the direct second reconcile). Test A asserts the success of the reconciliation.\n- Test B (idempotent direct reconcile): seed → reconcile directly → reconciled (writes the county) → count the documents → reconcile again → already_reconciled, the count is unchanged, the county is unchanged.\n- Test C (review blocks the worker): seed legacy confirmed → updateWatchlistItemCounty(SUMMIT) → county_refresh → blocked 'county_review', the record's revision is unchanged (2), the county is still Summit.\n\nThe shape of the worker's refresh input: what does runCountyRefresh expect? From the route: the county_refresh input — let me check the shape of CountyRefreshInput: probably { expectedRevision, objectId? }. Let me check the worker's runCountyRefresh (around L674-745).\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0962a0fb8314350","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '698,745p' src/lib/agent-worker