{"type":"compaction","id":"d5c26f64","parentId":"31e4fc0c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:46:13.063Z","summary":"\n\n## Goal\n- Implement the immutable plan **Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan** from `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md` / untracked `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`.\n- Close the nine verified audit gaps, reconcile closeout evidence against one exact commit, then stop for `GoalJudge` and independent read-only `GoalVerifier` evaluation.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use the main session’s currently selected PLAN / ORCHESTRATOR / YOLO mode and available tools; do not assume unavailable capabilities.\n- `GoalJudge` cannot mutate the goal; `GoalVerifier` is read-only acceptance verification.\n- Preserve all user changes and never disable/bypass pre-commit hooks, tests, authorization checks, provider gates, CAS, or idempotency controls.\n- Preserve county fail-closed behavior, explicit Copilot confirmation, durable audits, fixture honesty, product deferrals, and all existing checks.\n- Never infer Cuyahoga from Ohio/state/address, fabricate provenance, or turn external deferrals into fake functionality.\n- Work in `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch` on branch `feat/records-agent-launch`, audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` / short `a9eeff9`.\n- Deterministic suites must remain network-free; local-9B validation is opt-in, serial, and uses `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`.\n- WU1 county-coverage changes must keep all surfaces canonical: explicit county plus confirmed-snapshot provenance are the same resolver inputs everywhere; non-live/review states must fail closed with zero writes.\n- Tooling constraints learned this session: the read-before-edit guard requires a **Read-tool** read of each file (sed/bash views do not count); `checkpoint_notes.current` must be ≤2048 chars (trim before committing); Jest patterns with bracketed paths like `[id]` must be quoted/escaped or they match zero files; curl with visible stdout is blocked by a hook (use `-o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\"`).\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Ran `git status --short --branch`, `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git branch --show-current`, `git remote -v`.\n- [x] Confirmed repo state:\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard 450773f [main]`\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch a9eeff9 [feat/records-agent-launch]`\n  - Untracked: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`\n  - Remote: `origin git@github.com:Brickspect/dashboard.git`\n- [x] Read prior material:\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\n- [x] Checked `todo` list: **No tasks**.\n- [x] Requested deeper reasoning (`request_deeper_reasoning`) for WU1 core because the fail-closed contradiction design ripples through route surfaces, worker, UI, and tests.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts`**\n  - Added a fifth `CountyCoverage` status: `review`.\n  - `review` is returned when explicit county and confirmed-snapshot provenance prove different counties after slug/base comparison.\n  - `review` is fail-closed: it is never `live`, even if one side is a covered county.\n  - `review` displays the explicit county and carries non-null `contradiction: { explicit, provenance }`.\n  - Updated `notCoveredPayload` so `reason` includes `'review'` and the message names both counties and says county work is paused. Exact review message: \"This property's county needs review: it is set to {explicit.name}, but a confirmed parcel proves it is in {provenance.name}. County work is paused until the county is resolved.\"\n  - Added `coverageNote(coverage)` helper returning client-safe `{ status, county, message, contradiction? }`; `contradiction` is set only for `review`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/county-records/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts`**\n  - Rewrote old permissive contradiction tests to fail-closed `review` semantics.\n  - Added tests for `notCoveredPayload(review)` and `coverageNote` behavior.\n  - Fixed import by adding `coverageNote`.\n  - Fixed stale test expecting old permissive note language.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/types/screening.ts`**\n  - Extended `ScreeningCoverage.status` to include `'review'`.\n  - No change needed in `src/lib/screening/inputs.ts` because `coverageForScreening` already forwards county-record snapshot provenance to `resolveCountyCoverage`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`.\n  - GET detail now resolves coverage with `property.county ?? null` plus `countyRecord?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null`.\n  - PATCH now resolves post-update coverage with the same provenance input so a contradictory county lands in `review` immediately.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/coverage/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`.\n  - Replaced explicit-only “light projection” with per-item county-record reads via `Promise.all(items.map((item) => getCountyRecord(user.id, item.id)))`.\n  - Each row resolves with `resolveCountyCoverage(identity, record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null)`.\n  - Added `review` to the deterministic `ORDER` map: `live: 0, planned: 1, not_covered: 2, review: 3`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`, `coverageNote`, `resolveCountyCoverage`.\n  - GET now returns additive `coverage: Record<string, ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>>` keyed by property id.\n  - Uses `countyIdentityForProperty(item.county ?? undefined, item.state)` plus per-item county-record provenance.\n  - Updated `src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts` to mock `@/lib/firestore/county-records` and assert additive coverage behavior.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/properties/page.tsx`**\n  - Added exported `PropertyCoverageNote` type with optional `contradiction`.\n  - `fetchWatchlist` now parses and returns the server-provided `coverage` map.\n  - Added `coverageByProperty` state.\n  - Both watchlist load paths set `coverageByProperty`; error path clears it.\n  - List pill now uses `coverageByProperty[p.id] ?? resolveCountyCoverage(p.county ?? null, null)`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/components/records-dashboard/county-coverage-banner.tsx`**\n  - Widened `CoveragePill` `coverage` prop from full `CountyCoverage` to `{ status: CountyCoverage['status'] }` so both full deep-dive coverage and list notes are accepted.\n  - Added amber `review` pill variant with `data-testid=\"coverage-pill-review\"`.\n  - Added `CountyCoverageBanner` `review` case naming both counties and explaining county work is paused.\n  - `showForm` now includes `review`; chip label renders `'Needs review'`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/types/recorded-documents.ts`**\n  - Added `RecordedCoverageNote`:\n    - `status: 'live' | 'planned' | 'not_covered' | 'unknown' | 'review'`\n    - `county: { code: string; name: string } | null`\n    - `message: string | null`\n  - Added `RecordedSearchGuardedResponse = RecordedSearchResponse & { authoritative: boolean; coverage: RecordedCoverageNote }`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`**\n  - Added `recordedReadGuard(user, propertyId)`.\n  - It reads `getWatchlistItem` and `getCountyRecord` in parallel.\n  - It resolves canonical coverage using the same inputs as the search POST gate:\n    - `property.county ?? null`\n    - `record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null`\n  - Returns `{ authoritative: coverage.status === 'live', coverage: coverageNote(coverage) }`.\n  - Restored `requireRecordedProperty` after an accidental placeholder clobber.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `recordedReadGuard`.\n  - GET root spreads `{ ...guard }` into both the inline `not_started` payload and the latest search response.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `recordedReadGuard`.\n  - GET search poll spreads `{ ...search, ...guard }` into the response.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/components/records-dashboard/recorded-documents-section.tsx`**\n  - Added `guardNotice(payload)` helper.\n  - Added `coverageNotice` state.\n  - `loadState` and poll path call `setCoverageNotice(guardNotice(payload))`.\n  - Renders amber notice when `authoritative === false` and `coverage.message` exists.\n  - Added `data-testid=\"recorded-coverage-notice\"`.\n  - Additive guard fields keep existing `isSearchResponse` checks passing.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/firestore/properties.ts` — transactional reconcile (replaces non-atomic backfill)**\n  - REMOVED `backfillWatchlistCounty` (non-atomic read-then-set, line ~94). Only caller was the worker; no test referenced it (grep-verified).\n  - Added `CountyReconcileOutcome` union type: `{ status: 'reconciled'; county } | { status: 'already_reconciled'; county } | { status: 'explicit_conflict'; county; stored } | { status: 'property_gone' }`.\n  - Added `reconcileWatchlistCounty(uid, propertyId, county, sourceId)` using `getFirestoreDb().runTransaction`:\n    - property absent → `property_gone` (no write)\n    - existing county, same base (after `countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(...))` on both) → `already_reconciled` (NO write; returns the STORED identity, not the derived one; no normalization)\n    - existing county, different base → `explicit_conflict` (NO write — explicit assertion never overwritten)\n    - county absent → `tx.set(ref, { county, countyReconciledFrom: sourceId, countyReconciledAt: new Date().toISOString() }, { merge: true })` → `reconciled`\n  - Errors PROPAGATE (never swallowed inside the function).\n  - Imports `countyBase, normalizeCountyCode` from `@/lib/county-records/capabilities`.\n  - Diagnostics clean.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/agent-worker.ts` — worker wiring**\n  - Import swapped: `backfillWatchlistCounty` → `reconcileWatchlistCounty` (L69).\n  - `requireLiveCounty` (L314): added explicit review branch BEFORE the generic `!== 'live'` check: `if (coverage.status === 'review') throw new WorkerBlockedError('county_review', notCoveredPayload(coverage).message)` — distinct code, since this is a human-only contradiction, not \"county unsupported\".\n  - Local helper `backfillCountyBestEffort` (L343, old numbering) replaced by `reconcileCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage)` (L364): early-returns if `item.county` (explicit never touched); calls `reconcileWatchlistCounty(uid, item.id, coverage.county, coverage.source.id)`; `explicit_conflict` → `console.info` (review state surfaces on read surfaces, no write); thrown error → `console.error` with property/county/source ids — NEVER rethrows (the CAS parcel confirm is already durable; failing/retrying the task would CAS-conflict on stale revision; idempotent re-attempt happens on next county work).\n  - Both call sites updated to `await reconcileCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage)`: L578 (auto-confirm branch inside `runCountyResolve` — unique match auto-confirms and now reconciles; comment updated to \"same transactional reconcile the explicit confirm lane uses\") and L666 (`runCountyConfirm`). Verified `runCountyRefresh` (L674) has NO backfill/reconcile call (refresh doesn't change identity) — nothing to do. Line numbers shifted +34 from pre-edit (544→578, 632→666).\n  - File diagnostics clean.\n- [x] **WU1 test fixes — all existing WU1-affected unit suites green**:\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts` (was 6/13 failing 500s): added `jest.mock('@/lib/firestore/county-records', () => ({ getCountyRecord: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(null) }))` + import (the route now imports `getCountyRecord`; the real one throws in unit env). Added new PATCH test \"lands in the fail-closed review state when the new county contradicts a confirmed parcel\": Summit assert + `getCountyRecord` mock `{ snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture' } } }` → 200, `body.coverage.status === 'review'`, county summit-oh, `eta` null, `source` null, `contradiction = { explicit: summit-oh, provenance: cuyahoga-oh }`. (First version asserted `body.coverage.message` — wrong: this surface returns the RAW `CountyCoverage` union which has no message field; message exists only in `notCoveredPayload`/`coverageNote` shapes.) Now **14/14 PASS**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added county-records mock (default null); added guard assertions to \"returns the latest search run\" (`authoritative: true`, `coverage.status: 'live'`, county code); added new test \"flags stored results as non-authoritative when coverage is not live\" (county-less item + null record → `authoritative: false`, `coverage.status: 'unknown'`, message contains 'county'). Removed the unused `getCountyRecord` import (mock presence is what mattered). Now **green**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added county-records mock + import; added guard assertions to \"returns the run\" (live → authoritative true) + new \"flags a contradictory property as non-authoritative on the poll path\". First version used `sourceId: 'lorain-fixture'` — INVALID (see decisions); corrected to explicit Summit county + `cuyahoga-fixture` provenance → `authoritative: false`, `coverage.status: 'review'`, message names both counties. Now **5/5 PASS**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/resolve/__tests__/route.test.ts`: 1 stale test (title already said \"fails closed, is surfaced for review\") asserted the OLD permissive payload (`reason: 'planned'`, `eta: 'Q4 2026'`, regex `/review the county/i`); updated to the new fail-closed payload: `reason: 'review'`, `eta: null`, regexes `/needs review/i` + `/paused/i` (matching the actual `notCoveredPayload` wording). Now **10/10 PASS**.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts` (NEW) — reconcile unit matrix, 6/6 PASS**\n  - Purpose-built fake-DB harness (pattern cloned from `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/agent-tasks-retry.test.ts`, which is the canonical fake-firestore harness): in-memory `state` map keyed `${uid}:${propertyId}`; `users/{uid}/properties/{id}` ref chain carrying `uid`; merge-aware `tx.set` (cast `data as Record<string, unknown>`); `runTransaction(fn)` runs `fn` against the same state.\n  - Tests: (1) `reconciled` — county-less seed gets county + `countyReconciledFrom: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` + string `countyReconciledAt` via merge, pre-existing `address` preserved; (2) idempotent 2nd call → `already_reconciled`, state byte-identical, one extra transaction (read) but no write; (3) same-base explicit (bare `'cuyahoga'` vs `'cuyahoga-oh'`) → `already_reconciled` returning the stored identity, no write; (4) `explicit_conflict` (Summit stored vs Cuyahoga derived) → no write, stored untouched, no `countyReconciledFrom` metadata; (5) `property_gone` → no write; (6) error propagation — `runTransaction` mock rejected → function rejects with 'transaction aborted' (never swallowed).\n  - Fixed 3 initial LSP errors: spreading `unknown` (cast to `Record<string, unknown>`), unused `key` helper (removed), union-narrowing (`expect(second.status).toBe()` does not narrow — assert whole object with `toEqual`).\n- [x] **Emulator environment restored**: `__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts` initially failed 8/8 with 5000ms per-test timeouts — root cause purely environmental: the docker-compose Firestore emulator (`localhost:8095`, project `demo-brickspect-dashboard`) was not running (HTTP 000, no process; `jest.setup.integration.js` only CONFIGURES the host, never launches it). Started it with `docker compose up -d firestore-emulator` (container `records-agent-launch-firestore-emulator-1`, HTTP 200 after ~8s). Re-ran the suite: **8/8 PASS** with the guard changes — the extra `getCountyRecord` read per GET route is harmless in the emulator.\n- [x] Committed checkpoint notes through generation **26** (sha256 `5319f8c7a781`) at `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/notes/9b3f771d-b43a-45a1-a4e6-1cad29d7d7c4/NOTES.md` (generations 14–26 committed during this segment).\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] **WU1 remaining — final test authoring + full verification + commit**\n  - **NOW WRITING** (at gen 26): `__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` (emulator) — 3 planned tests:\n    1. Auto-confirm reconciles a legacy county-less Cuyahoga property: seed via `upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, snapshot)` with `county: null` (the seed script has no such property), `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(uid, propertyId, 'county_resolve', { expectedRevision: 0, address: ADDR }, 0)` → `processOneTask(task, { workerId })` (fixture auto-confirms in one run → confirmed r2); assert raw property doc (via `getFirestoreDb().collection('users').doc(uid).collection('properties').doc(propertyId).get()`) has `county = cuyahoga-oh` + `countyReconciledFrom: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` + `countyReconciledAt`.\n    2. Idempotent re-attempt: record user-doc count (subcollections `properties` + per-prop `countyRecords`, `agentTasks`, `domainEvents`, `feedItems`, `actionItems`), call `reconcileWatchlistCounty` directly → `already_reconciled`, county unchanged, doc count unchanged (zero duplicate tasks/events).\n    3. Worker fail-closed: explicit Summit property + fixture auto-confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot (honest path: run resolve, which auto-confirms the Cuyahoga parcel) → enqueue `county_refresh` → `processOneTask` → task status `'blocked'` with `error.code: 'county_review'`; property county still Summit; county record revision unchanged.\n  - Route-agreement tests: contradictory property (explicit Summit + confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot) → detail GET, `/api/coverage`, `/api/properties` list, recorded-documents GET all report the same review status + county (add to existing route suites).\n  - Review zero-write route tests: `county-records/confirm` + `county-records/refresh` routes (like resolve's existing `expectZeroWrites` contradiction test) + recorded search POST → 422 with no task/search/event writes.\n  - Full unit suite run, then **commit WU1**.\n  - Then continue to WU3, WU2, WU4–7, WU8, WU9 per the plan.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Work in the existing records-agent worktree**: Continue on `feat/records-agent-launch` rather than starting a new branch, because the audit plan explicitly anchors to audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` and existing closeout docs.\n- **Follow the plan’s execution order**: county resolver/reconciliation first, then Copilot atomic reclaim/redaction, provenance rollout, theme/screening/local-stack lanes, documentation/seed evidence, missing browser/integration evidence, and full verification.\n- **Treat prior closeout as context, not proof**: New claims must come from newly executed checks against a single recorded commit; unavailable evidence must be reported as unavailable.\n- **WU1 contradiction is fail-closed `review`, not permissive annotation**: If explicit county and confirmed-snapshot provenance prove different counties, the result is `status: 'review'`; no county work runs until a human resolves it, even if one county is live.\n- **Review displays the explicit county**: The explicit county is the user assertion and is displayed; the provenance county is named in the message. The provenance-backed claim is treated as stronger for blocking routing, but the user-facing identity remains explicit until resolved.\n- **Canonical inputs are explicit county + confirmed-snapshot provenance**: Property detail, `/api/coverage`, `/api/properties` list, screening, county mutation routes, worker selection, and recorded-document reads all resolve from `resolveCountyCoverage(explicitCounty, confirmedSourceId)` (or equivalent normalized county identity plus the same provenance source id).\n- **Provenance is only a migration/backfill signal, never inferred from state/address**: A county-less legacy property with a confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot can resolve live through provenance; a county-less property without provenance stays unknown.\n- **Recorded-document reads get additive guard fields**: Stored search documents remain retrievable, but non-live coverage reads return `authoritative: false` plus a typed `coverage` note so stale county-specific results are not presented as current authoritative data.\n- **Additive recorded-read fields are backward-compatible**: The UI’s `isSearchResponse` checks only `status` membership in `SEARCH_STATUSES`, so `{ authoritative, coverage }` can be added without breaking existing consumers.\n- **`CoveragePill` accepts a minimal status shape**: Instead of forcing list rows to reconstruct a full `CountyCoverage` union member (including `eta`/`source`), the pill prop was widened to `{ status: CountyCoverage['status'] }`; the full `CountyCoverage` remains structurally compatible.\n- **`coverageNote` carries optional contradiction only for `review`**: This allows clients to reconstruct valid review semantics without exposing unnecessary internal details on non-review notes.\n- **Worker `county_review` blocked code is safe**: `WorkerBlockedError` accepts a free-form `code: string`, and `classifyWorkerFailure` (agent-worker.ts L237) maps ALL `WorkerBlockedError` instances to `kind: 'blocking'` → `blockTask` → task status `'blocked'` with `error: { code, message }`. `BLOCKING_WORKER_CODES` (`unsupported_county`, `county_changed`, `invalid_request`, `parcel_gone`) only classifies `CountyRecordsError` codes — no change needed there.\n- **Transactional county reconciliation must never overwrite explicit county**: A later reconcile may only write county when the property currently has no county. If an explicit county exists, the outcome is `already_reconciled` (same base) or `explicit_conflict` (different base); explicit user assertions are never silently overwritten.\n- **Reconcile failure after a durable confirm must not fail the task or roll back**: The CAS parcel confirm is the domain mutation; reconcile is an auxiliary idempotent consistency write. Worker catches and logs at `console.error` (with property/county/source ids) but never rethrows — failing the task would cause a retry against a stale expectedRevision (CAS conflict → worse), and every read surface still agrees via provenance until the next county work re-attempts reconcile.\n- **Same-base idempotency does not normalize**: If stored county is `'cuyahoga'` (bare) and derived is `'cuyahoga-oh'`, reconcile treats them as the same county (base comparison after stripping the state token) and writes nothing — honest idempotency, no silent rewrite of the user's stored token. `already_reconciled` returns the STORED identity, not the derived one.\n- **Only Cuyahoga can be proven by snapshot provenance**: `countyForSourceId(sourceId)` (capabilities.ts ~L218) strips the `-(arcgis|fixture)$` suffix and matches ONLY registry entries with non-null `source` — currently only Cuyahoga (live). So the only producible review contradiction is explicit non-Cuyahoga + Cuyahoga-confirmed parcel; `'lorain-fixture'` (Lorain is `not_covered`, source null) is not a producible source and resolves to null (no contradiction). Test fixtures must use `cuyahoga-fixture`/`cuyahoga-arcgis` provenance with a non-Cuyahoga explicit county.\n- **Two distinct response contracts — tests must match each surface**: detail/PATCH routes return the RAW `CountyCoverage` union (no `message` field; review member = `{ status: 'review', county, eta: null, source: null, contradiction }`); recorded-read routes and notes use `coverageNote`/`notCoveredPayload` shapes (which carry `message`). Asserting `body.coverage.message` on the detail surface is a test bug, not an implementation bug.\n- **Auto-confirm lives inside `runCountyResolve`**: The worker has three county handlers — `runCountyResolve` (L423; includes the unique-match auto-confirm branch that carried the backfill call), `runCountyConfirm` (L586), `runCountyRefresh` (L674, NO reconcile call — refresh doesn't change county identity). No separate auto-confirm handler exists; both reconcile call sites (L578, L666) cover auto-confirm + explicit confirm.\n- **Deeper reasoning was justified for WU1**: The WU1 core changes fail-closed semantics across many consumers; an `xhigh` pass was requested to reduce risk of subtle boundary errors.\n- **Check the emulator FIRST for integration-suite timeouts**: The recorded-documents 8/8 timeout episode was environmental (emulator not running), not a code regression — for any integration-suite failure, verify `localhost:8095` health before suspecting changes.\n- **The emulator stays running for the rest of the session**: started via `docker compose up -d firestore-emulator` (container `records-agent-launch-firestore-emulator-1`, port 8095, project `demo-brickspect-dashboard`); required by the in-progress county-reconcile emulator test and later WU8/WU9 integration/E2E work (seed-twice, concurrent reclaim).\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Finish and run `__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` (3 tests as specified in In Progress) against the running emulator: seed legacy county-less via `upsertWatchlistItem` (`WatchlistSnapshot` = `{address, city, state, zipCode, county, propertyType, title, crexiId, listingUrl, thumbnailUrl, price, sizeSqFt, pricePerSqFt}` — no `capturedAt`/`verdict`/`addedAt`); use `ADDR = { street: '5180 broadview road', unit: null, city: 'cleveland', state: 'OH', zip: '44143' }`; unique `runId()` per test; count user subcollections (`properties` + nested `countyRecords` per property, `agentTasks`, `domainEvents`, `feedItems`, `actionItems`) before/after for zero-write assertions.\n2. Add route-agreement tests (contradictory property → same review status + county across detail GET, `/api/coverage`, `/api/properties` list, recorded-documents GET) to the existing route test files.\n3. Add review zero-write route tests: `county-records/confirm` and `county-records/refresh` 422-with-no-writes (mirror resolve's `expectZeroWrites` pattern) + recorded search POST → 422 with no task/search/event writes.\n4. Run the full unit suite; then **commit WU1** (all files: capabilities, types, 3 property routes, page+banner, recorded-read types/guard/routes/section, properties.ts reconcile, agent-worker, and all test files).\n5. Proceed to **WU3** in `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts`:\n   - Replace read-then-unconditional-update reclaim with `runTransaction` CAS.\n   - Verify state, lease timestamp/version, and attempt count before transitioning to `executing`.\n   - Ensure exactly one concurrent caller wins; losers return interrupted/replay without dispatch.\n   - Stop persisting caller-controlled `targetId` and `idempotencyKey` verbatim; store validated canonical identifiers or keyed hashes.\n   - Add `schemaVersion` to `CopilotActionExecution` documents.\n   - Add concurrent reclaim, failure-injection, replay, redaction, stale-revision, cross-user, malformed-proposal, and audit-unavailable tests.\n6. Proceed to **WU2** provenance presentation:\n   - Extend shared provenance contract for feed/task surfaces.\n   - Add typed source identity, provider mode, trust/status, confidence, freshness/as-of fields where domain records support them.\n   - Map dashboard feed cards and agent-task/property links through the shared contract.\n   - Render explicit unavailable values; label workflow/system-only activity without inventing provenance.\n7. Proceed to **WU4–6**:\n   - `src/app/viewport.ts`: advertise only approved light color scheme/theme; remove active `.dark` production token block and launch-surface `dark:` variants.\n   - Screening columns: align header/row order to `Property, County, Verdict, As of, Reason, Required checks, Action`; verify responsive/focus/mobile behavior.\n   -