oute-agreement additions (detail/`/api/coverage`/list/recorded-read)\n  - Zero-write route tests (confirm, refresh, recorded search POST)\n- Key existing functions/types relevant to remaining WU1 work:\n  - `resolveCountyCoverage(county, confirmedSourceId)` in `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts` — registry: `cuyahoga-oh` (live, source `cuyahoga-arcgis`), `summit-oh` (planned, eta 'Q4 2026'), `franklin-oh` (planned, '2027'), `lorain-oh`/`lake-oh`/`medina-oh` (not_covered, source null).\n  - `countyForSourceId(sourceId)` in `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts` (~L218) — strips `-(arcgis|fixture)$`, matches only registry entries with non-null source.\n  - `notCoveredPayload(coverage)` (capabilities.ts L379) and `coverageNote(coverage)` (capabilities.ts L447).\n  - `getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId)` in `src/lib/firestore/county-records.ts`; county record stored at `users/{uid}/properties/{pid}/countyRecords/current`.\n  - `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent(uid, propertyId, kind, input, expectedRevision)` (county-records.ts L300–337) — revision CAS + idempotency key `buildTaskIdempotencyKey(kind, propertyId, expectedRevision)`; does NOT itself gate on coverage (route-level gates do).\n  - `upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, snapshot)` — seed seam.\n  - `processOneTask(task, { workerId })` in `src/lib/agent-worker.ts` — fixture mode auto-confirms within one `county_resolve` run (r2).\n  - Worker failure classification: `classifyWorkerFailure` (L230) — `CountyRecordChangedError` → `cas_conflict`; `WorkerBlockedError` → ALWAYS `blocking`; `CountyRecordsError` → blocking iff code in `BLOCKING_WORKER_CODES`, else transient; unknown → transient `internal_error`. `blockTask` (agent-tasks.ts L573) requires claimed/running + lease owner match (managed internally by processOneTask). `failTask` → status 'failed'.\n  - `AgentTask`: `status: AgentTaskStatus`, `error: AgentTaskPublicError | null` (`{ code, message }`).\n  - `WatchlistSnapshot`: `{address, city, state, zipCode, county, propertyType, title, crexiId, listingUrl, thumbnailUrl, price, sizeSqFt, pricePerSqFt}` (no capturedAt/verdict — those are on `WatchlistItem`).\n  - Fixture source: `sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'`, label \"Cuyahoga County Records — fixture data (development)\" (fixtures.ts L185–188); live source `cuyahoga-arcgis` (cuyahoga-arcgis.ts L500).\n  - User subcollections for zero-write counting: `properties` (+ nested `countyRecords` per property), `agentTasks`, `domainEvents`, `feedItems`, `actionItems`.\n  - Fake-firestore harness pattern: `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/agent-tasks-retry.test.ts` (state map + `runTransaction` closure); also used in `owner-requests.test.ts` and `src/lib/screening/__tests__/runs.test.ts`. `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts` has a fake harness special-casing `copilotActionExecutions` (will need `runTransaction` support for WU3).\n  - `recordedReadGuard(user, propertyId)` in `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`; `guardNotice(payload)` in `recorded-documents-section.tsx`; `PropertyCoverageNote` in `src/app/properties/page.tsx`.\n- Important semantic invariants:\n  - Explicit county is the only routing input except provenance backfill for missing county identity.\n  - Provenance backfill applies only when the explicit county is absent.\n  - Contradiction between explicit county and provenance is fail-closed `review`, not a routing note.\n  - County identity is never inferred from state/address; bare slug and registry slug are compared after stripping the two-letter state token.\n  - Non-live coverage states block county work with zero writes.\n  - Recorded-document reads may return stale stored results, but only with `authoritative: false` when coverage is no longer live.\n- Seed data context:\n  - `scripts/seed-records-demo.ts` currently seeds six demo properties with explicit county or null county, but it does **not** seed a county-less property with a confirmed county snapshot — the WU1 emulator test creates 