{"type":"message","id":"15f88f42","parentId":"9466b027","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:48:11.358Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The advisory is advisory only — no action needed. Checkpoint 30 committed. Reading the fixture provider's gate and the place where the message is thrown.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3af7f7325f432b7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '55,110p' src/lib/county-records/cuyahoga-arcgis.ts; echo ===FIXTURE-CTOR===; sed -n '195,235p' src/lib/county-records/fixtures.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":72923,"output":116,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":33,"totalTokens":73039,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788202085154,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b51773c73a0e7f10","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"95080db9","parentId":"15f88f42","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:48:11.411Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a3af7f7325f432b7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    super(message);\n    this.name = 'CountyRecordsError';\n  }\n\n  /** Public-safe info (no upstream text). */\n  info(): CountyRecordsErrorInfo {\n    return { code: this.code, message: this.message };\n  }\n}\n\n/** Stable public messages — the ONLY text ever surfaced to the client. */\nexport function publicMessageFor(code: CountyRecordsErrorCode): string {\n  switch (code) {\n    case 'source_unavailable':\n      return 'The county source could not be reached. Try again later.';\n    case 'source_malformed':\n      return 'The county source returned data we could not validate. Try again later.';\n    case 'unsupported_county':\n      return 'County records are not available for this property’s area yet.';\n    case 'invalid_request':\n      return 'This request could not be processed.';\n    case 'parcel_gone':\n      return 'This parcel no longer exists at the county source.';\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Per-feature attributes, validated before mapping. Optional fields use\n * `.nullish()` — the county genuinely nulls values. ObjectID is the one\n * required field (a feature without it is malformed data).\n */\nconst FeatureAttributesSchema = z.object({\n  ObjectID: z.number().int(),\n  parcel_id: z.string().max(32).nullish(),\n  par_addr_all: z.string().max(200).nullish(),\n  parcel_addr: z.string().max(20).nullish(),\n  parcel_predir: z.string().max(2).nullish(),\n  parcel_street: z.string().max(30).nullish(),\n  parcel_suffix: z.string().max(10).nullish(),\n  parcel_unit: z.string().max(10).nullish(),\n  parcel_city: z.string().max(30).nullish(),\n  parcel_zip: z.number().nullish(),\n  parcel_owner: z.string().max(300).nullish(),\n  last_transfer_date: z.number().int().nullish(),\n  last_sales_amount: z.number().nullish(),\n  grantor: z.string().max(300).nullish(),\n  grantee: z.string().max(300).nullish(),\n  tax_assessed_land: z.number().nullish(),\n  tax_assessed_improvement: z.number().nullish(),\n  tax_assessed_total: z.number().nullish(),\n  tax_market_total: z.number().nullish(),\n  cur_tax_year: z.number().nullish(),\n  net_tax_total: z.number().nullish(),\n  prev_net_tax_total: z.number().nullish(),\n  grand_total_balance: z.number().nullish(),\n  effective_rate: z.number().nullish(),\n===FIXTURE-CTOR===\nexport class CuyahogaFixtureProvider implements CountyRecordsProvider {\n  readonly source = {\n    id: 'cuyahoga-fixture' as const,\n    label: `${CUYAHOGA_SOURCE.label} — fixture data (development)`,\n  };\n\n  /**\n   * Selection gate (fixture stands in for the live provider's): the caller\n   * must be selected for Cuyahoga by a verified county identity — an\n   * Ohio address alone is not a selection, and `address.state` is never\n   * read here.\n   */\n  private requireOwnCounty(options?: CountyProviderOptions): void {\n    const own = countyForSourceId(this.source.id);\n    const given = options?.county;\n    const ok =\n      own != null &&\n      given != null &&\n      countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(given.code) ?? '') ===\n        countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(own.code) ?? '');\n    if (!ok) {\n      throw new CountyRecordsError(\n        'unsupported_county',\n        publicMessageFor('unsupported_county')\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  async resolveCandidates(\n    addr: NormalizedPropertyAddress,\n    options?: CountyProviderOptions\n  ): Promise<ParcelCandidate[]> {\n    this.requireOwnCounty(options);\n    const scenario = options?.scenario ?? 'exact';\n\n    switch (scenario) {\n      case 'upstream_failure':\n        throw new CountyRecordsError(\n          'source_unavailable',\n          publicMessageFor('source_unavailable')\n        );\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788202091411}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8f52ca3","parentId":"95080db9","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:48:19.724Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The advisory is just advice (a pattern that has existed for a while) — no action needed. Found it: `CuyahogaFixtureProvider.resolveCandidates(addr, options)` calls `requireOwnCounty(options)` — it throws 'unsupported_county' when `options.county` is missing or not Cuyahoga. My test was calling `provider.resolveCandidates(ADDR)` without the options → the gate throws. Fix: pass `{ county: CUYAHOGA, scenario: 'exact' }` (check the shape of CountyProviderOptions: {county?: CountyIdentity, scenario?: ...}). Also `fetchParcelSnapshot(objectId, options?)` probably has the same gate too — pass county there as well.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8681e1c4f199a0a1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"interface CountyProviderOptions\" -A 8 src/types/county-records.ts; grep -n \"async fetchParcelSnapshot\" -A 6 src/lib/county-records/fixtures.ts | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":74018,"output":222,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":148,"totalTokens":74240,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788202091414,"responseId":"chatcmpl-abb1c3e095ba3192","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
