{"type":"message","id":"2fcc5fc4","parentId":"3c86cb0e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:49:13.955Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-abff367657b95260","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    ✕ a review contradiction blocks worker county work with zero writes (184 ms)\n\n  ● county reconciliation (emulator) › a successful refresh durably reconciles a legacy county-less property\n\n    expect(received).toEqual(expected) // deep equality\n\n    Expected: {\"code\": \"cuyahoga-oh\", \"name\": \"Cuyahoga County\"}\n    Received: null\n\n      190 |     // refresh advanced the record exactly once.\n      191 |     const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n    > 192 |     expect(item?.county).toEqual(CUYAHOGA);\n          |                          ^\n      193 |     const raw = await rawPropertyDoc(uid, propertyId);\n      194 |     expect(raw.countyReconciledFrom).toBe('cuyahoga-fixture');\n      195 |     expect(typeof raw.countyReconciledAt).toBe('string');\n\n      at Object.toEqual (__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts:192:26)\n\n  ● county reconciliation (emulator) › a review contradiction blocks worker county work with zero writes\n\n    expect(received).toBe(expected) // Object.is equality\n\n    Expected: 4\n    Received: 5\n\n      246 |     expect(task.error?.code).toBe('county_review');\n      247 |     // Zero writes: the record is untouched and the assertion survives.\n    > 248 |     expect(await countUserDocs(uid)).toBe(before);\n          |                                      ^\n      249 |     const recordAfter = await getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId);\n      250 |     expect(recordAfter?.revision).toBe(recordBefore?.revision);\n      251 |     expect(recordAfter?.snapshot).toEqual(recordBefore?.snapshot);\n\n      at Object.toBe (__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts:248:38)\n\nTest Suites: 1 failed, 1 total\nTests:       2 failed, 1 passed,