{"type":"message","id":"f8ba5daa","parentId":"13dd88e7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:52:50.799Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-ba5409bdff295503","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      };\n      return {\n        kind: 'write',\n        record: stored,\n        eventType: 'county_record_resolved',\n      };\n    }\n  );\n  if (\n    result.kind === 'no_record' ||\n    result.kind === 'candidate_mismatch' ||\n    result.kind === 'idempotent'\n  ) {\n    // Unreachable for a resolve write (no preconditions can fail it) —\n    // fail closed rather than return a wrong shape.\n    throw new Error('Property not in your watchlist');\n  }\n  if (result.kind === 'conflict') {\n    throw new CountyRecordChangedError(result.current);\n  }\n  return result.record;\n}\n\n/**\n * Confirm one of the stored candidates (CAS).\n===AUTOCONFIRM===\n      status: 'confirmation_required',\n      resolvedAddress: address,\n      candidates: [selected],\n      lastRefresh: null,\n      expectedRevision: input.expectedRevision,\n    },\n    casOptionsFor(task)\n  );\n  // Confirm against the revision THIS run just committed, not the caller's\n  // observation (same rule the synchronous route used).\n  const confirmed = await confirmCountyParcel(\n    uid,\n    propertyId,\n    {\n      objectId: selected.objectId,\n      parcelId: snapshot.parcelId,\n      parcelIdFormatted: snapshot.parcelIdFormatted,\n      resolvedAddress: address,\n      snapshot,\n      expectedRevision: pending.revision,\n    },\n    casOptionsFor(task)\n  );\n  if (!confirmed || confirmed.snapshot === null) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n      'candidate_mismatch',\n      'The stored candidates no longer include this parcel; re-run the resolution.'\n    );\n  }\n  // Legacy reconciliation (idempotent): an auto-confirmed parcel proves the\n  // county, so a property that was added without county identity gets it\n  // persisted here — the same transactional reconcile the explicit confirm\n  // lane uses. An explicit county is never overwritten.\n  await reconcileCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage);\n  return { eventType: 'county_record_confirmed', record: confirmed };\n}\n\n/**\n * county_confirm: re-fetch the candidate's snapshot (the county is the\n * source of truth — never the requester's payload) and confirm it.\n */\nasync function runCountyConfirm(\n  task: AgentTask,\n  ctx: WorkerContext\n): Promise<TaskSuccess> {\n  // SAFETY: the county confirm route builds this exact shape at enqueue\n  // time (objectId from the stored candidates, never the requester's raw\n  // parcel payload).\n  const input = task.input as unknown as CountyConfirmInput;\n  const uid = task.ownerUid;\n  const propertyId = task.propertyId;\n  const item = await requireWatchlistProperty(uid, propertyId);\n\n  const current = await getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId);\n  if (!current) {\n    throw new WorkerBlockedError(\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788202370799}}
{"type":"message","id":"af22e324","parentId":"f8ba5daa","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:53:08.796Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nConfirmed: the worker's auto-confirmation path = saveResolution (r3, eventType 'county_record_resolved') → confirmCountyParcel (r4, 'county_record_confirmed') → reconcile. In other words, 2 events per re-resolution. Test A fix: revision 4, eventsBefore + 2.\n\nCheckpoint deadline — this time I'll commit a short checkpoint after the run. First, apply the edits.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b03bac3051ca07","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"    // The fixture's unique exact match auto-confirms: the worker commits\n    // the resolution (r3) and then the confirmation (r4), and reconciles\n    // the county identity durably, with its provenance. The metadata\n    // carries the registry's canonical source id — both the fixture and\n    // ArcGIS variants resolve to the same provenance county.\n    const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n    expect(item?.county).toEqual(CUYAHOGA);\n    const raw = await rawPropertyDoc(uid, propertyId);\n    expect(raw.countyReconciledFrom).toBe('cuyahoga-arcgis');\n    expect(typeof raw.countyReconciledAt).toBe('string');\n    const record = await getCountyRecord(uid, propertyId);\n    expect(record?.revision).toBe(4);\n    // Two new domain events: the resolution and the confirmation.\n    expect(await countSubcol(uid, 'domainEvents')).toBe(eventsBefore + 2);","oldText":"    // The fixture's unique exact match auto-confirms (r3) and the worker\n    // reconciles the county identity durably, with its provenance. The\n    // metadata carries the registry's canonical source id — both the\n    // fixture and ArcGIS variants resolve to the same provenance county.\n    const item = await getWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId);\n    expect(item?.