{"type":"message","id":"7049692c","parentId":"9697500f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:14.563Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a7c3c70cd658ade0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport { POST } from '../route';\nimport type {\n  CountyParcelSnapshot,\n  StoredCountyRecord,\n} from '@/types/county-records';\nimport type { WatchlistItem } from '@/types/records-dashboard';\n\njest.mock('@/lib/auth', () => ({ getUserFromRequest: jest.fn() }));\njest.mock('@/lib/firestore/properties', () => ({\n  getWatchlistItem: jest.fn(),\n}));\njest.mock('@/lib/firestore/county-records', () => ({\n  enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent: jest.fn(),\n  getCountyRecord: jest.fn(),\n  CountyRecordChangedError: class CountyRecordChangedError extends Error {\n    constructor(public readonly current: StoredCountyRecord) {\n      super('County record changed since the caller observed it');\n    }\n  },\n}));\njest.mock('@/lib/rate-limiter', () => ({\n  checkRateLimit: jest.fn(),\n  getRateLimitHeaders: jest.fn().mockReturnValue({}),\n}));\n\nimport { getUserFromRequest } from '@/lib/auth';\nimport { getWatchlistItem } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport {\n  enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent,\n  getCountyRecord,\n} from '@/lib/firestore/county-records';\nimport { checkRateLimit } from '@/lib/rate-limiter';\n\nconst params = () => ({ params: Promise.resolve({ id: 'prop-001' }) });\nconst NOW = '2026-08-22T00:00:00.000Z';\nconst SNAPSHOT = {\n  provenance: {\n    sourceUpdateAt: NOW,\n    taxBillUpdateAt: null,\n    retrievedAt: NOW,\n  },\n} as CountyParcelSnapshot;\n\nconst WATCH_ITEM: WatchlistItem = {\n  id: 'prop-001',\n  address: '1234 Euclid Ave',\n  city: 'Cleveland',\n  state: 'OH',\n  zipCode: '44109',\n  county: { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' },\n  propertyType: null,\n  title: null,\n  crexiId: null,\n  listingUrl: null,\n  thumbnailUrl: null,\n  price: null,\n  sizeSqFt: null,\n  pricePerSqFt: null,\n  capturedAt: NOW,\n  verdict: null,\n  addedAt: NOW,\n};\n\nfunction storedRecord(\n  over: Partial<StoredCountyRecord> = {}\n): StoredCountyRecord {\n  return {\n    schemaVersion: 1,\n    ownerUid: 'u1',\n    revision: 2,\n    createdAt: NOW,\n    status: 'confirmed',\n    resolvedAddress: null,\n    candidates: null,\n    snapshot: SNAPSHOT,\n    unsupportedReason: null,\n    lastRefresh: { at: NOW, ok: true, error: null },\n    updatedAt: NOW,\n    ...over,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction post(body: unknown = { expectedRevision: 2 }) {\n  return new NextRequest(\n    'http://localhost/api/properties/prop-001/county-records/refresh',\n    {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify(body),\n      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },\n    }\n  );\n}\n\nfunction queued(created = false) {\n  return {\n    stale: null,\n    task: { taskId: 'task-refresh-1', revision: 5 },\n    created,\n    recordRevision: 2,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction expectNoStore(response: Response) {\n  expect(response.headers.get('cache-control')).toBe('no-store');\n}\n\ndescribe('POST /api/properties/[id]/county-records/refresh', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    jest.clearAllMocks();\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(WATCH_ITEM);\n    (checkRateLimit as jest.Mock).mockReturnValue({\n      allowed: true,\n      limit: 10,\n      remaining: 9,\n      resetTime: new Date(0),\n    });\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(storedRecord());\n    (enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(queued());\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788202514563}}
{"type":"message","id":"0bb32be0","parentId":"7049692c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:41.365Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nBoth test files share the same mock structure. Now I'll add the review gate tests.\n\nFor CONFIRM (append after the last test, before the closing `});`):\n```ts\n  it('gates the review contradiction (explicit county vs confirmed parcel) with zero writes', async () => {\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ...WATCH_ITEM,\n      county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n    });\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(storedRecord({\n      snapshot: {\n        ...SNAPSHOT,\n        provenance: { ...SNAPSHOT.provenance, sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture' },\n      },\n    }));\n    const response = await POST(post(), params());\n    expect(response.status).toBe(422);\n    const body = await response.json();\n    expect(body.error).toBe('not_covered');\n    expect(body.reason).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.county).toEqual({ code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' });\n    expect(body.eta).toBeNull();\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/Summit County/);\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/Cuyahoga County/);\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/paused/);\n    expect(enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n    expectNoStore(response);\n  });\n```\n\nWait — the SNAPSHOT in the confirm test has provenance: {sourceUpdateAt, taxBillUpdateAt, retrievedAt} — a cast `as CountyParcelSnapshot`. The actual CountyParcelSnapshot.provenance should have sourceId. Spreading SNAPSHOT.provenance and adding sourceId should be fine.\n\nFor REFRESH: same pattern using storedRecord({snapshot: {...SNAPSHOT, provenance: {...SNAPSHOT.provenance, sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'}}}), item county is Summit → 422 review, enqueue is not called.\n\nNote that in the refresh test, the default item in WATCH_ITEM is Cuyahoga (live) — in the review case we override it to Summit.\n\nAlso — regarding the confirm route: the gate happens before the 404 check for `record`? No: the confirm route reads the record first (404 if absent), then the coverage gate. In the review test, the record exists (a confirmation_required with a last-known-good snapshot). Good.\n\nNext, the root agreement tests:\n1. Detail GET (src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts): add a test — an item with an explicit Summit county + a county record with a confirmed snapshot (provenance cuyahoga-fixture) → GET → 200 with body.coverage.status 'review', county summit-oh, eta null, source null, contradiction {explicit: summit-oh, provenance: cuyahoga-oh}. Check the current GET test setup in that file — there's a PATCH review test (I added it). Let me look at the existing GET test and the mocks (the file mocks @/lib/firestore/county-records with a default null; the county-records module mock returns {getCountyRecord}). In the new GET test, mock getCountyRecord to return the record.\n\n2. Coverage route (src/app/api/coverage/__tests__/route.test.ts): check the setup; add a contradictory item → row status 'review', county 'Summit County', positioned after not_covered in ORDER (review:3). The coverage route mocks... let me read it.\n\n3. Properties list: extend the existing coverage test — add a contradictory item → coverage note in the map with status review + contradiction.\n\n4. Recorded-documents GET: add a review case (item Summit + record snapshot cuyahoga-fixture → authoritative false, coverage.status 'review', message mentioning both).\n\nLet me read the coverage route test + the recorded GET test I already modified (I know its shape from before) + the details route GET section. To keep the context manageable, I'll read the coverage test first.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a71fea95acaa7518","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/