{"type":"message","id":"36b37fbf","parentId":"0bb32be0","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:41.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a71fea95acaa7518","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { NextRequest } from 'next/server';\nimport { GET } from '../route';\n\njest.mock('@/lib/auth', () => ({ getUserFromRequest: jest.fn() }));\njest.mock('@/lib/firestore/properties', () => ({\n  listWatchlistItems: jest.fn(),\n}));\n\nimport { getUserFromRequest } from '@/lib/auth';\nimport { listWatchlistItems } from '@/lib/firestore/properties';\nimport type { WatchlistItem } from '@/types/records-dashboard';\n\nfunction item(\n  id: string,\n  county: WatchlistItem['county'],\n  state: string | null = 'OH'\n): WatchlistItem {\n  return {\n    id,\n    address: null,\n    city: null,\n    state,\n    zipCode: null,\n    county,\n    propertyType: null,\n    title: null,\n    crexiId: null,\n    listingUrl: null,\n    thumbnailUrl: null,\n    price: null,\n    sizeSqFt: null,\n    pricePerSqFt: null,\n    capturedAt: '2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z',\n    verdict: null,\n    addedAt: '2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z',\n  };\n}\n\ndescribe('GET /api/coverage', () => {\n  it('returns 401 when unauthenticated', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(null);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    expect(res.status).toBe(401);\n  });\n\n  it('groups by county identity with live/planned/not-covered statuses', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (listWatchlistItems as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([\n      item('p1', { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' }),\n      item('p2', { code: 'cuyahoga-oh', name: 'Cuyahoga County' }),\n      item('p3', { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' }),\n      item('p4', { code: 'lorain-oh', name: 'Lorain County' }),\n    ]);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    expect(res.status).toBe(200);\n    const body = await res.json();\n\n    expect(body.coverage.counties).toEqual([\n      {\n        code: 'cuyahoga-oh',\n        name: 'Cuyahoga County',\n        state: 'OH',\n        status: 'live',\n        eta: null,\n        sourceLabel: expect.stringContaining('Cuyahoga'),\n        propertyCount: 2,\n      },\n      {\n        code: 'summit-oh',\n        name: 'Summit County',\n        state: 'OH',\n        status: 'planned',\n        eta: 'Q4 2026',\n        sourceLabel: null,\n        propertyCount: 1,\n      },\n      {\n        code: 'lorain-oh',\n        name: 'Lorain County',\n        state: 'OH',\n        status: 'not_covered',\n        eta: null,\n        sourceLabel: null,\n        propertyCount: 1,\n      },\n    ]);\n    expect(body.coverage.unknownCount).toBe(0);\n  });\n\n  it('never counts a state-only property as covered (unknown stays unknown)', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (listWatchlistItems as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([\n      // OH state, NO county identity: must land in unknownCount, never in a\n      // Cuyahoga count — the M1 regression this endpoint guards against.\n      item('p1', null, 'OH'),\n      item('p2', null, 'oh'),\n      item('p3', null, 'PA'),\n      item('p4', null, null),\n    ]);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.coverage.counties).toEqual([]);\n    expect(body.coverage.unknownCount).toBe(4);\n  });\n\n  it('reports no counties (and no unknown) for an empty watchlist', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (listWatchlistItems as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.coverage.counties).toEqual([]);\n    expect(body.coverage.unknownCount).toBe(0);\n  });\n\n  it('always returns the full registry roadmap (honesty as a feature)', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (listWatchlistItems as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    const body = await res.json();\n    const codes = body.coverage.roadmap.map(\n      (r: { code: string }) => r.code\n    );\n    expect(codes).toContain('cuyahoga-oh');\n    expect(codes).toContain('summit-oh');\n    expect(codes).toContain('lorain-oh');\n    // The roadmap carries the registry's statuses and ETAs verbatim.\n    const summit = body.coverage.roadmap.find(\n      (r: { code: string }) => r.code === 'summit-oh'\n    );\n    expect(summit).toMatchObject({ status: 'planned', eta: 'Q4 2026' });\n  });\n\n  it('reports a non-registry county as not_covered (never live)', async () => {\n    (getUserFromRequest as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({ id: 'u1' });\n    (listWatchlistItems as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue([\n      item('p1', { code: 'bexar-tx', name: 'Bexar County' }, 'TX'),\n    ]);\n    const res = await GET(new NextRequest('http://localhost/api/coverage'));\n    const body = await res.json();\n    expect(body.coverage.counties).toEqual([\n      {\n        code: 'bexar-tx',\n        name: 'Bexar County',\n        state: 'TX',\n        status: 'not_covered',\n        eta: null,\n        sourceLabel: null,\n        propertyCount: 1,\n      },\n    ]);\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788202541387}}
{"type":"message","id":"ea0369d8","parentId":"36b37fbf","timestamp":"2026-08-31T18:55:55.281Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to investigate this further. Let me check the details.\n\nThe coverage test file only mocks `@/lib/firestore/properties` (listWatchlistItems) — it does NOT mock `@/lib/firestore/county-records`! But my modified coverage route now imports getCountyRecord from that module → in the unit test environment, the real module gets loaded → does it touch firebase at import time? The route's import chain: county-records.ts imports getFirestoreDb from firebase/admin — importing the module is fine (lazy initialization), and the existing tests pass (per the summary, the properties route tests needed a mock because the route imports getCountyRecord; the coverage route — has it passed since my changes? The summary listed \"src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts\" (list) as passing with the mock added. As for the coverage route tests — in the gen-26 snapshot, only the properties list, [id], recorded GET/poll, and resolve were enumerated as updated. Was the coverage route test run? It wasn't on the green list… The gen-26 snapshot lists the passing suites, and coverage isn't on it. It may have broken with my route changes (importing getCountyRecord without a mock → does it throw in the unit environment? The real getCountyRecord calls getFirestoreDb() — in the unit environment, the firebase admin initialization might throw \"not initialized\" → the route returns 500).\n\nFirst, let me run the coverage route test to check the current state.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1f84d334692eda","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"npx jest \"src/app/api/coverage\" 2>&1 | grep -E \"Tests:|Suites:|✕|● \" | head -12","timeout":180}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":100908,"output":398,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"