{"type":"message","id":"a5e696bf","parentId":"4a8fc13c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T19:01:38.275Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The advisory is advisory only — no action needed. Now I'll write both test additions (since they're independent files, two separate edit calls can be batched... the edit tool is per-file, so I'll make two calls in one block).\n\nConfirm test addition:\n```ts\n  it('fails closed with zero writes when the county is in review (explicit vs confirmed parcel)', async () => {\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ...WATCH_ITEM,\n      county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n    });\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(\n      storedRecord({\n        snapshot: {\n          ...SNAPSHOT,\n          provenance: { ...SNAPSHOT.provenance, sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture' },\n        },\n      })\n    );\n\n    const response = await POST(post(), params());\n\n    expect(response.status).toBe(422);\n    const body = await response.json();\n    expect(body.error).toBe('not_covered');\n    expect(body.state).toBe('not_covered');\n    expect(body.reason).toBe('review');\n    expect(body.county).toEqual({ code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' });\n    expect(body.eta).toBeNull();\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/Summit County/);\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/Cuyahoga County/);\n    expect(body.message).toMatch(/paused/i);\n    expect(enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n    expectNoStore(response);\n  });\n```\n\nWait — the SNAPSHOT in the confirm test: `provenance: {sourceUpdateAt, taxBillUpdateAt, retrievedAt}` — the actual type of provenance probably has required fields other than sourceId, but since it's already being cast with `as CountyParcelSnapshot`, spreading it is fine.\n\nRefresh test addition: same idea, using the default post() ({expectedRevision: 2}).\n\nFor confirm, the anchor is the unique text of the last test block.\n","thi