{"type":"message","id":"b99adeb9","parentId":"89b80505","timestamp":"2026-08-31T19:02:55.295Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The refresh route test got \"planned\" instead of \"review\". Why? The refresh route's gate: `resolveCountyCoverage(property.county ?? null, record.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null)`. In the refresh test, the mock record is `storedRecord()`, with `snapshot: SNAPSHOT`, and SNAPSHOT's provenance = {sourceUpdateAt, taxBillUpdateAt, retrievedAt} — there's no sourceId! I only mocked the watch item's county (Summit), and didn't inject a snapshot with sourceId in the refresh test (I wrote \"mock item county Summit\" — but the refresh record's snapshot provenance has no sourceId → provenance is null → resolveCountyCoverage(Summit, null) = 'planned' (Summit is a planned county) → reason 'planned'.\n\nIn the confirm test, I was injecting sourceId into the snapshot (in the confirm record, the snapshot was null by default, so I added a snapshot with sourceId). In the refresh test, storedRecord() already has a snapshot (SNAPSHOT with no sourceId), and my test was only overriding the item's county.\n\nFix for the refresh test: override the record's snapshot provenance with sourceId 'cuyahoga-fixture':\n```ts\n(getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(\n  storedRecord({\n    snapshot: {\n      ...SNAPSHOT,\n      provenance: { ...SNAPSHOT.provenance, sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture' },\n    },\n  })\n);\n```\nThis reflects the confirm test. Applying it.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94aedf4f122bc318","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"  it('fails closed with zero writes when the county is in review (explicit county vs confirmed parcel)', async () => {\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ...WATCH_ITEM,\n      county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n    });\n    // The confirmed snapshot's provenance proves Cuyahoga — it contradicts\n    // the explicit Summit assertion.\n    (getCountyRecord as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(\n      storedRecord({\n        snapshot: {\n          ...SNAPSHOT,\n          provenance: {\n            ...SNAPSHOT.provenance,\n            sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture',\n          },\n        },\n      })\n    );\n\n    const response = await POST(post(), params());","oldText":"  it('fails closed with zero writes when the county is in review (explicit county vs confirmed parcel)', async () => {\n    (getWatchlistItem as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue({\n      ...WATCH_ITEM,\n      county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' },\n    });\n\n    const response = await POST(post(), params());"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/refresh/__tests__/route.test.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":120716,"output":704,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":343,"totalTokens":121420,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788202953465,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8c8796c6d4da0950","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
