t's write these edits carefully. First, to anchor the edits precisely, let me check the current exact text of the relevant sections. I have the full file content from the earlier read in this session. Key anchors:\n\n1. End of header:\n```\n *     non-terminal record that a later retry reclaims and reconciles\n *     (safe because every domain seam is idempotent/CAS-keyed).\n */\nimport { createHash } from 'crypto';\n```\n\n2. `import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';` — add the Transaction import.\n\n3. The interface block (per the read):\n```ts\nexport interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  actionType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  fingerprint: string;\n  idempotencyKey: string;\n  state: CopilotActionState;\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n4. Insert helpers after the `isTerminal`/`replayResult` functions (before recordGateOutcome).\n\n5. Replace recordGateOutcome (the whole function from `async function recordGateOutcome(` to its closing `}`).\n\n6. Replace claimExecution (from `async function claimExecution(` to its closing `}`).\n\nOne design detail regarding `withExecutionRecord`: the callback receives `tx` and `record`, and internally needs a docRef. Let's pass the docRef too, or have the callback build it. Cleaner: withExecutionRecord takes (uid, fingerprint, fn), where fn receives (tx, record, docRef). Hmm, passing the docRef from the caller is simpler:\n\n```ts\nasync function withExecutionRecord<T>(\n  docRef: ReturnType<...>['doc']... \n```\n\nThe type of docRef: `DocumentReference` from firebase-admin/firestore. executionDocRef returns that. So:\n\n```ts\nasync function withExecutionRecord<T>(\n  docRef: DocumentReference,\n  fn: (\n    tx: Transaction,\n    record: CopilotActionExecution | null\n  ) => T | Promise<T>\n): Promise<{ ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: unknown }> {\n  try {\n    const value = await getFirestoreDb().runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n      const got = await tx.get(docRef);\n      const record = got.exists\n        ? (got.data() as CopilotActionExecution)\n        : null;\n      return await fn(tx, record);\n    });\n    return { ok: true, value };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { ok: false, error };\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWait — one subtlety about the admin SDK's runTransaction retry semantics: if the closure throws, it's retried; if the commit fails (conflict), it's retried. If it exhausts `maxAttempts` (default 6), it rejects. Our catch converts that to 'unavailable'. Good.\n\nAnother subtlety — the fast-path read outside the transaction in claimExecution: after a fast-path read determines 'fresh' or 'reclaim', the transaction re-reads (a new snapshot). The transaction's decision is authoritative. Good.\n\nNext, about `decide()`: it's currently an inner closure that references nothing external — move it to module scope as `decideRecord`.\n\nThe recordGateOutcome replacement:\n\n```ts\nasync function recordGateOutcome(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  code: CopilotActionCode,\n  message: string\n): Promise<CopilotExecuteResult> {\n  const result: CopilotExecuteResult = { code, message };\n  const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, req.fingerprint);\n  const outcome = await withExecutionRecord(docRef, (tx, record) => {\n    if (record && isTerminal(record)) {\n      return { kind: 'replay', result: replayResult(record) } as const;\n    }\n    if (record && isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n      return {\n        kind: 'interrupted',\n        result: {\n          code: 'interrupted' as const,\n          message:\n            'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n        },\n      } as const;\n    }\n    // Stale non-terminal, or no record: settle it with this gate's\n    // outcome. The write happens inside the transaction, so a\n    // concurrent settler commits first and this call re-decides on\n    // retry (replaying the winner's outcome) instead of double-writing.\n    if (record) {\n      tx.update(docRef, {\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        updatedAt: nowIso(),\n      });\n    } else {\n      tx.create(\n        docRef,\n        buildExecutionRecord(uid, req, {\n          state: 'failed',\n          code,\n          message: redactSensitive(message),\n          action: null,\n          attempts: 1,\n        })\n      );\n    }\n    return { kind: 'settled' } as const;\n  });\n\n  if (!outcome.ok) {\n    // A gate rejection executed nothing, so nothing is lost by a failed\n    // audit write — but the caller must not be told a clean rejection.\n    console.error('Failed to record copilot action gate outcome:', outcome.error);\n    return {\n      code: 'audit_unavailable',\n      message:\n        'The confirmation could not be durably recorded, so no outcome was applied; retry the confirmation.',\n    };\n  }\n  if (outcome.value.kind === 'replay') return outcome.value.result;\n  if (outcome.value.kind === 'interrupted') return outcome.value.result;\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nThe claimExecution replacement:\n\n```ts\nasync function claimExecution(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest\n): Promise<\n  | { kind: 'proceed' }\n  | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'unavailable' }\n> {\n  const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, req.fingerprint);\n\n  // Fast path outside the transaction: a terminal duplicate and a\n  // fresh in-flight confirmation both end here without any write, and\n  // neither needs isolation.\n  const first = await docRef.get();\n  const firstDecision = decideRecord(\n    first.exists ? (first.data() as CopilotActionExecution) : null\n  );\n  if (firstDecision.kind === 'replay')\n    return { kind: 'replay', result: firstDecision.result };\n  if (firstDecision.kind === 'interrupted')\n    return { kind: 'interrupted', result: firstDecision.result };\n\n  // Create and reclaim race: decide and write inside ONE transaction.\n  // The Firestore snapshot read inside the transaction is what makes\n  // exactly one concurrent caller win:\n  //   - two creates: the first commit lands, the second's create\n  //     conflicts, the SDK re-runs the closure, which now sees the\n  //     fresh in-flight record and returns interrupted;\n  //   - two reclaims of a crashed record: the first commit stamps a\n  //     new updatedAt (fresh in-flight), the second re-runs against\n  //     that and returns interrupted.\n  // The loser never dispatches.\n  const outcome = await withExecutionRecord(docRef, (tx, record) => {\n    const decision = decideRecord(record);\n    switch (decision.kind) {\n      case 'fresh':\n        tx.create(\n          docRef,\n          buildExecutionRecord(uid, req, {\n            state: 'accepted',\n            code: null,\n            message: '',\n            action: null,\n            attempts: 1,\n          })\n        );\n        return { kind: 'proceed' } as const;\n      case 'replay':\n        return { kind: 'replay', result: decision.result } as const;\n      case 'interrupted':\n        return { kind: 'interrupted', result: decision.result } as const;\n      case 'reclaim':\n        tx.update(docRef, {\n          state: 'executing',\n          updatedAt: nowIso(),\n          attempts: (decision.record.attempts ?? 1) + 1,\n        });\n        return { kind: 'proceed' } as const;\n    }\n  });\n\n  if (!outcome.ok) {\n    console.error('Failed to claim copilot action execution record:', outcome.error);\n    return { kind: 'unavailable' };\n  }\n  return outcome.value;\n}\n```\n\nThe union type of outcome.value: `{kind:'proceed'} | {kind:'replay';result} | {kind:'interrupted';result}` — matches the return value.\n\nThe buildExecutionRecord helper:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * Build the durable record as CURRENT code writes it (schema v2): the\n * caller's identifiers never persist verbatim — they are stored as\n * keyed, irreversibly transformed references (keyedIdentifierRef) that\n * keep the record correlatable without letting a hostile or\n * model-generated input smuggle PII or secrets into the audit.\n */\nfunction buildExecutionRecord(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  fields: {\n    state: CopilotActionState;\n    code: CopilotActionCode | null;\n    message: string;\n    action: string | null;\n    attempts: number;\n  }\n) {\n  const t = nowIso();\n  return {\n    schemaVersion: EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n    actionType: req.proposal.actionType,\n    targetRef: keyedIdentifierRef(uid, req.fingerprint, 'target', req.proposal.targetId),\n    keyRef: keyedIdentifierRef(uid, req.fingerprint, 'key', req.idempotencyKey),\n    fingerprint: req.fingerprint,\n    ...fields,\n    acceptedAt: t,\n    updatedAt: t,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nkeyedIdentifierRef:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * A keyed, irreversibly transformed reference to caller-supplied\n * identifier material. The hash is keyed by (owner, proposal\n * fingerprint, field), so the same input always maps to the same\n * reference for the same owner and proposal (the record stays\n * correlatable for idempotency and traceability) while the raw value\n * cannot be recovered from the audit store — a hostile or\n * model-generated input can no longer smuggle PII or secrets into a\n * durable record.\n */\nexport function keyedIdentifierRef(\n  uid: string,\n  fingerprint: string,\n  field: 'target' | 'key',\n  value: string\n): string {\n  return sha256Hex(`${uid}|${fingerprint}|${field}|${value}`);\n}\n```\n\nThe EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION constant:\n```ts\n/** Current execution-record schema (v2: identifiers stored as keyed refs). */\nexport const EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2;\n```\n\nThe module-level decideRecord (moved from claimExecution):\n```ts\nfunction decideRecord(\n  record: CopilotActionExecution | null\n):\n  | { kind: 'fresh' }\n  | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'reclaim'; record: CopilotActionExecution } {\n  if (!record) return { kind: 'fresh' };\n  if (isTerminal(record)) {\n    return { kind: 'replay', result: replayResult(record) };\n  }\n  if (isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n    return {\n      kind: 'interrupted',\n      result: {\n        code: 'interrupted',\n        message:\n          'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n      },\n    };\n  }\n  return { kind: 'reclaim', record };\n}\n```\n\nAddition to the header — extend the last bullet with a crash-boundary note. The current end of the header:\n\n```\n *     non-terminal record that a later retry reclaims and reconciles\n *     (safe because every domain seam is idempotent/CAS-keyed).\n */\n```\n\nAdd before the closing `*/`:\n\n```\n *\n *   Crash boundary (documented, non-atomic by design): the domain\n *   mutation (county enqueue / task CAS / mail send) and the terminal\n *   audit transition live in different collections — and the\n *   owner-request seams in other modules — so they cannot be one\n *   transaction. A crash after the mutation but before the terminal\n *   write leaves a non-terminal record; the next confirmation of the\n *   same fingerprint reclaims it and re-dispatches through the same\n *   idempotent/CAS-keyed seam, where the second attempt is a\n *   deterministic no-op (duplicate enqueue → stale; duplicate\n *   cancel/retry → revision conflict; duplicate send → the mail\n *   idempotency key). The audit always catches up; the domain never\n *   double-applies.\n```\n\nAlso update the recordGateOutcome doc comment to mention the transaction.\n\nOne more check: the `CopilotExecuteRequest` interface has an `idempotencyKey` field — keep it (it's input, not storage).\n\nRegarding the interface edit, the current text is:\n\n```ts\nexport interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  actionType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  fingerprint: string;\n  idempotencyKey: string;\n  state: CopilotActionState;\n  /** Terminal outcome code (null until the record is terminal). */\n  code: CopilotActionCode | null;\n  /** Redacted outcome message (empty until the record is terminal). */\n  message: string;\n  /** Which domain action ran (null until executed). */\n  action: string | null;\n  acceptedAt: string;\n  updatedAt: string;\n  /** How many times this confirmation has been (re)claimed. */\n  attempts: number;\n}\n```\n\nNew version:\n\n```ts\nexport interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  /** 2 (current): caller identifiers persist only as keyed refs\n   *  (targetRef/keyRef). Absent on legacy v1 records, which carry the\n  *  raw targetId/idempotencyKey and remain readable (the replay and\n   *  in-flight checks depend only on state and timestamps). */\n  schemaVersion?: number;\n  actionType: string;\n  /** v2: keyed hash of the caller's targetId (keyedIdentifierRef) —\n   *  never the raw value. */\n  targetRef?: string;\n  /** v2: keyed hash of the caller's idempotency key. */\n  keyRef?: string;\n  /** v1 (legacy): raw caller-controlled values — read-only for\n   *  backward compatibility; current code never writes them. */\n  targetId?: string;\n  idempotencyKey?: string;\n  fingerprint: string;\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nNow let's write the edits. I have the exact original text from the Read in this session. Be careful with exact whitespace matching.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll now implement WU3 in `copilot-actions.ts` with five targeted edits covering the header note, Transaction import, interface, helpers, and rewriting the two racy functions.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8b6bcbc8c47c115","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":" *     non-terminal record that a later retry reclaims and reconciles\n *     (safe because every domain seam is idempotent/CAS-keyed).\n *\n *   Crash boundary (documented, non-atomic by design): the domain\n *   mutation (county enqueue / task CAS / mail send) and the terminal\n *   audit transition live in different collections — and the\n *   owner-request seams in other modules entirely — so they cannot be\n *   one transaction. A crash after the mutation but before the terminal\n *   write leaves a non-terminal record; the next confirmation of the\n *   same fingerprint reclaims it and re-dispatches through the same\n *   idempotent/CAS-keyed seam, where the second attempt is a\n *   deterministic no-op (duplicate enqueue → stale; duplicate\n *   cancel/retry → revision conflict; duplicate send → the mail\n *   idempotency key). The audit always catches up; the domain never\n *   double-applies.\n */\nimport { createHash } from 'crypto';","oldText":" *     non-terminal record that a later retry reclaims and reconciles\n *     (safe because every domain seam is idempotent/CAS-keyed).\n */\nimport { createHash } from 'crypto';"},{"newText":"import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';\nimport type { DocumentReference, Transaction } from 'firebase-admin/firestore';","oldText":"import { getFirestoreDb } from '@/lib/firebase/admin';"},{"newText":"export interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  /** 2 (current): caller identifiers persist only as keyed refs\n   *  (targetRef/keyRef). Absent on legacy v1 records, which carry the\n   *  raw targetId/idempotencyKey and remain readable — the replay and\n   *  in-flight checks depend only on state and timestamps. */\n  schemaVersion?: number;\n  actionType: string;\n  /** v2: keyed hash of the caller's targetId (keyedIdentifierRef) —\n   *  never the raw value. */\n  targetRef?: string;\n  /** v2: keyed hash of the caller's idempotency key. */\n  keyRef?: string;\n  /** v1 (legacy): raw caller-controlled values — read for backward\n   *  compatibility; current code never writes them. */\n  targetId?: string;\n  idempotencyKey?: string;\n  fingerprint: string;","oldText":"export interface CopilotActionExecution {\n  actionType: string;\n  targetId: string;\n  fingerprint: string;\n  idempotencyKey: string;"},{"newText":"const EXECUTIONS_COLLECTION = 'copilotActionExecutions';\n\n/** Current execution-record schema (v2: identifiers stored as keyed refs). */\nexport const EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2;\n\n/**\n * A keyed, irreversibly transformed reference to caller-supplied\n * identifier material. The hash is keyed by (owner, proposal\n * fingerprint, field), so the same input always maps to the same\n * reference for the same owner and proposal — the record stays\n * correlatable for traceability and idempotency — while the raw value\n * cannot be recovered from the audit store. A hostile or\n * model-generated input can no longer smuggle PII or secrets into a\n * durable record.\n */\nexport function keyedIdentifierRef(\n  uid: string,\n  fingerprint: string,\n  field: 'target' | 'key',\n  value: string\n): string {\n  return sha256Hex(`${uid}|${fingerprint}|${field}|${value}`);\n}\n\n/**\n * Build the durable record as CURRENT code writes it (schema v2):\n * caller-controlled identifiers persist only as keyed refs (see\n * keyedIdentifierRef) — never verbatim.\n */\nfunction buildExecutionRecord(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  fields: {\n    state: CopilotActionState;\n    code: CopilotActionCode | null;\n    message: string;\n    action: string | null;\n    attempts: number;\n  }\n) {\n  const t = nowIso();\n  return {\n    schemaVersion: EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n    actionType: req.proposal.actionType,\n    targetRef: keyedIdentifierRef(\n      uid,\n      req.fingerprint,\n      'target',\n      req.proposal.targetId\n    ),\n    keyRef: keyedIdentifierRef(uid, req.fingerprint, 'key', req.idempotencyKey),\n    fingerprint: req.fingerprint,\n    ...fields,\n    acceptedAt: t,\n    updatedAt: t,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Run a read-decide-write cycle against the execution record under a\n * Firestore transaction. The snapshot read inside the transaction is\n * what serializes concurrent writers: if the commit conflicts (the doc\n * changed after this transaction's snapshot), the SDK re-runs the\n * closure against the new state and re-decides. Replay/interrupted\n * outcomes stage no write, so an empty transaction commits as a no-op.\n * A failure that exhausts the SDK's retries resolves to `ok: false` —\n * the caller MUST treat that as \"nothing was durably recorded\".\n */\nasync function withExecutionRecord<T>(\n  docRef: DocumentReference,\n  fn: (\n    tx: Transaction,\n    record: CopilotActionExecution | null\n  ) => T | Promise<T>\n): Promise<{ ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: unknown }> {\n  try {\n    const value = await getFirestoreDb().runTransaction(async (tx) => {\n      const got = await tx.get(docRef);\n      const record = got.exists ? (got.data() as CopilotActionExecution) : null;\n      return await fn(tx, record);\n    });\n    return { ok: true, value };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return { ok: false, error };\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * The claim decision table (pure): no record → fresh; terminal →\n * replay; fresh non-terminal → interrupted; stale non-terminal (crash)\n * → reclaim.\n */\nfunction decideRecord(\n  record: CopilotActionExecution | null\n):\n  | { kind: 'fresh' }\n  | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'reclaim'; record: CopilotActionExecution } {\n  if (!record) return { kind: 'fresh' };\n  if (isTerminal(record)) {\n    return { kind: 'replay', result: replayResult(record) };\n  }\n  if (isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n    return {\n      kind: 'interrupted',\n      result: {\n        code: 'interrupted',\n        message:\n          'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n      },\n    };\n  }\n  return { kind: 'reclaim', record };\n}","oldText":"const EXECUTIONS_COLLECTION = 'copilotActionExecutions';"},{"newText":"/**\n * Persist a TERMINAL execution record for a gate-level rejection\n * (allowlist / tamper). The read-decide-write runs inside one\n * transaction: an existing terminal record is replayed, a fresh\n * in-flight one yields interrupted, and a stale non-terminal (or\n * missing) record is settled with this gate's outcome. Two concurrent\n * settler race only through the transaction — the loser re-decides\n * against the winner's committed record (and replays it) instead of\n * double-writing.\n */\nasync function recordGateOutcome(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  code: CopilotActionCode,\n  message: string\n): Promise<CopilotExecuteResult> {\n  const result: CopilotExecuteResult = { code, message };\n  const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, req.fingerprint);\n  const outcome = await withExecutionRecord(docRef, (tx, record) => {\n    if (record && isTerminal(record)) {\n      return { kind: 'replay', result: replayResult(record) } as const;\n    }\n    if (record && isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n      return {\n        kind: 'interrupted',\n        result: {\n          code: 'interrupted' as const,\n          message:\n            'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n        },\n      } as const;\n    }\n    // Stale non-terminal, or no record yet: settle it with this gate's\n    // outcome inside the transaction.\n    if (record) {\n      tx.update(docRef, {\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        updatedAt: nowIso(),\n      });\n    } else {\n      tx.create(\n        docRef,\n        buildExecutionRecord(uid, req, {\n          state: 'failed',\n          code,\n          message: redactSensitive(message),\n          action: null,\n          attempts: 1,\n        })\n      );\n    }\n    return { kind: 'settled' } as const;\n  });\n\n  if (!outcome.ok) {\n    // A gate rejection executed nothing, so nothing is lost by a failed\n    // audit write — but the caller must not be told a clean rejection.\n    console.error(\n      'Failed to record copilot action gate outcome:',\n      outcome.error\n    );\n    return {\n      code: 'audit_unavailable',\n      message:\n        'The confirmation could not be durably recorded, so no outcome was applied; retry the confirmation.',\n    };\n  }\n  if (outcome.value.kind === 'replay') return outcome.value.result;\n  if (outcome.value.kind === 'interrupted') return outcome.value.result;\n  return result;\n}","oldText":"/**\n * Persist a TERMINAL execution record for a gate-level rejection\n * (allowlist / tamper). Uses the same idempotent claim semantics as\n * the execution path: an existing terminal record is replayed, a fresh\n * in-flight one yields interrupted, everything else becomes terminal\n * with this gate's outcome.\n */\nasync function recordGateOutcome(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest,\n  code: CopilotActionCode,\n  message: string\n): Promise<CopilotExecuteResult> {\n  const { proposal, fingerprint, idempotencyKey } = req;\n  const result: CopilotExecuteResult = { code, message };\n  try {\n    const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, fingerprint);\n    const got = await docRef.get();\n    if (got.exists) {\n      const record = got.data() as CopilotActionExecution;\n      if (isTerminal(record)) return replayResult(record);\n      if (isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n        return {\n          code: 'interrupted',\n          message:\n            'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n        };\n      }\n      // Stale non-terminal: settle it with this gate's outcome.\n      await docRef.update({\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        updatedAt: nowIso(),\n      });\n    } else {\n      const t = nowIso();\n      await docRef.create({\n        actionType: proposal.actionType,\n        targetId: proposal.targetId,\n        fingerprint,\n        idempotencyKey,\n        state: 'failed',\n        code,\n        message: redactSensitive(message),\n        action: null,\n        acceptedAt: t,\n        updatedAt: t,\n        attempts: 1,\n      });\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    // A gate rejection executed nothing, so nothing is lost by a failed\n    // audit write — but the caller must not be told a clean rejection.\n    console.error('Failed to record copilot action gate outcome:', error);\n    return {\n      code: 'audit_unavailable',\n      message:\n        'The confirmation could not be durably recorded, so no outcome was applied; retry the confirmation.',\n    };\n  }\n  return result;\n}"},{"newText":"/**\n * Claim the durable execution record for a confirmation, idempotently\n * keyed by the proposal fingerprint:\n *\n *   - no record yet            → create it as `accepted` (the claim is\n *                                what makes every later domain action\n *                                traceable to exactly one confirmation);\n *   - terminal record          → replay it (duplicate confirmation);\n *   - fresh non-terminal       → interrupted (concurrent in-flight);\n *   - stale non-terminal       → reclaim it (crash recovery) and count\n *                                the attempt.\n *\n * The create and reclaim transitions run inside ONE transaction each.\n * Firestore's snapshot-isolated read plus the commit-conflict retry is\n * what makes EXACTLY ONE concurrent caller win: two racing creates\n * cannot both land (the loser re-runs and sees the fresh in-flight\n * record), and two racing reclaims of a crashed record cannot both\n * proceed (the winner's commit stamps a fresh `updatedAt`, which the\n * loser's re-run classifies as in-flight). Losers return\n * interrupted/replay and never dispatch. A claim that cannot be\n * persisted at all returns `null` semantics — the caller MUST refuse\n * to execute (no durable record ⇒ no unrecorded mutation).\n */\nasync function claimExecution(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest\n): Promise<\n  | { kind: 'proceed' }\n  | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'unavailable' }\n> {\n  const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, req.fingerprint);\n\n  // Fast path outside the transaction: a terminal duplicate and a\n  // fresh in-flight confirmation both end here with no write, and\n  // neither needs isolation.\n  const first = await docRef.get();\n  const firstDecision = decideRecord(\n    first.exists ? (first.data() as CopilotActionExecution) : null\n  );\n  if (firstDecision.kind === 'replay')\n    return { kind: 'replay', result: firstDecision.result };\n  if (firstDecision.kind === 'interrupted')\n    return { kind: 'interrupted', result: firstDecision.result };\n\n  // The racing paths (fresh create, stale reclaim) decide and write in\n  // one transaction; the re-run-on-conflict semantics make the second\n  // caller re-decide against the winner's committed state.\n  const outcome = await withExecutionRecord(docRef, (tx, record) => {\n    const decision = decideRecord(record);\n    switch (decision.kind) {\n      case 'fresh':\n        tx.create(\n          docRef,\n          buildExecutionRecord(uid, req, {\n            state: 'accepted',\n            code: null,\n            message: '',\n            action: null,\n            attempts: 1,\n          })\n        );\n        return { kind: 'proceed' } as const;\n      case 'replay':\n        return { kind: 'replay', result: decision.result } as const;\n      case 'interrupted':\n        return { kind: 'interrupted', result: decision.result } as const;\n      case 'reclaim':\n        tx.update(docRef, {\n          state: 'executing',\n          updatedAt: nowIso(),\n          attempts: (decision.record.attempts ?? 1) + 1,\n        });\n        return { kind: 'proceed' } as const;\n    }\n  });\n\n  if (!outcome.ok) {\n    console.error('Failed to claim copilot action execution record:', outcome.error);\n    return { kind: 'unavailable' };\n  }\n  return outcome.value;\n}","oldText":"/**\n * Claim the durable execution record for a confirmation, idempotently\n * keyed by the proposal fingerprint:\n *\n *   - no record yet            → create it as `accepted` (the claim is\n *                                what makes every later domain action\n *                                traceable to exactly one confirmation);\n *   - terminal record          → replay it (duplicate confirmation);\n *   - fresh non-terminal       → interrupted (concurrent in-flight);\n *   - stale non-terminal       → reclaim it (crash recovery) and count\n *                                the attempt.\n *\n * If the create races with a concurrent claim (the doc appears in the\n * meantime) the result is re-read and re-decided. A claim that cannot\n * be persisted at all returns `null` — the caller MUST refuse to\n * execute (no durable record ⇒ no unrecorded mutation).\n */\nasync function claimExecution(\n  uid: string,\n  req: CopilotExecuteRequest\n): Promise<\n  | { kind: 'proceed' }\n  | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n  | { kind: 'unavailable' }\n> {\n  const { proposal, fingerprint, idempotencyKey } = req;\n  const docRef = executionDocRef(getFirestoreDb(), uid, fingerprint);\n\n  const decide = (\n    record: CopilotActionExecution | null\n  ):\n    | { kind: 'fresh' }\n    | { kind: 'replay'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n    | { kind: 'interrupted'; result: CopilotExecuteResult }\n    | { kind: 'reclaim'; record: CopilotActionExecution } => {\n    if (!record) return { kind: 'fresh' };\n    if (isTerminal(record)) {\n      return { kind: 'replay', result: replayResult(record) };\n    }\n    if (isFreshInFlight(record)) {\n      return {\n        kind: 'interrupted',\n        result: {\n          code: 'interrupted',\n          message:\n            'The same confirmation is already in flight; nothing new was started.',\n        },\n      };\n    }\n    return { kind: 'reclaim', record };\n  };\n\n  const got = await docRef.get();\n  let decision = decide(\n    got.exists ? (got.data() as CopilotActionExecution) : null\n  );\n\n  if (decision.kind === 'fresh') {\n    try {\n      const t = nowIso();\n      await docRef.create({\n        actionType: proposal.actionType,\n        targetId: proposal.targetId,\n        fingerprint,\n        idempotencyKey,\n        state: 'accepted',\n        code: null,\n        message: '',\n        action: null,\n        acceptedAt: t,\n        updatedAt: t,\n        attempts: 1,\n      });\n      return { kind: 'proceed' };\n    } catch (error) {\n      // Either we lost the create race (a concurrent claim landed) or\n      // persistence is genuinely down. Re-read and re-decide; if there\n      // is still no record, persistence failed and execution is refused.\n      const again = await docRef.get();\n      decision = decide(\n        again.exists ? (again.data() as CopilotActionExecution) : null\n      );\n      if (decision.kind === 'fresh') {\n        console.error(\n          'Failed to claim copilot action execution record:',\n          error\n        );\n        return { kind: 'unavailable' };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (decision.kind === 'replay')\n    return { kind: 'replay', result: decision.result };\n  if (decision.kind === 'interrupted') {\n    return { kind: 'interrupted', result: decision.result };\n  }\n  if (decision.kind === 'reclaim') {\n    await docRef.update({\n      state: 'executing',\n      updatedAt: nowIso(),\n      attempts: (decision.record.attempts ?? 1) + 1,\n    });\n    return { kind: 'proceed' };\n  }\n  return { kind: 'unavailable' };\n}"}],"path":"/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/copilot-actions.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen38-main","model":"qwen3.8-27b","usage":{"input":115943,"output":8643,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3825,