Refresh, expectedRevision }, options?)` (L352) → r+1, event `county_record_resolved`; preserves last-known-good `snapshot`.\n  - `confirmCountyParcel(uid, propertyId, { objectId, parcelId, parcelIdFormatted, resolvedAddress, snapshot, expectedRevision }, options?)` (L437) → confirmed r+1 (idempotent on same objectId); candidate must exist in the `confirmation_required` record; requires the watchlist item to exist.\n  - `saveCountySnapshot` (L516) — refresh write.\n  - `recordResolutionFailure` (L580), `recordCountyRefreshFailure` (L666), `clearCountyRecords` (L715).\n  - `CasOptions` (county-records.ts L76): `{ delayBeforeCommitMs?, actor?, taskRef? }`.\n  - `upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, snapshot)` — seed seam; `updateWatchlistItemCounty(uid, propertyId, county)` — real PATCH seam.\n  - `processOneTask(task, { workerId })` in `src/lib/agent-worker.ts`.\n  - `getTaskForOwner(uid, taskId)` in `src/lib/firestore/agent-tasks.ts` (L249) — the task reader.\n  - Worker failure classification: `classifyWorkerFailure` (L230) — `CountyRecordChangedError` → `cas_conflict`; `WorkerBlockedError` → ALWAYS `blocking`; `CountyRecordsError` → blocking iff code in `BLOCKING_WORKER_CODES`, else transient; unknown → transient `internal_error`. `blockTask` (agent-tasks.ts L573) — writes NO domain event. `failTask` → status 'failed'.\n  - `AgentTask`: `status: AgentTaskStatus`, `error: AgentTaskPublicError | null` (`{ code, message }`).\n  - `CountyRefreshInput`: `{ expectedRevision, county? }`; refresh route builds `{ expectedRevision, county: item.county }`.\n  - `CountyResolveInput`: `{ expectedRevision, address, county? }`.\n  - `CountyConfirmInput`: `{ expectedRevision, objectId, address?, county? }`.\n  - `WatchlistSnapshot`: `{address, city, state, zipCode, county, propertyType, title, crexiId, listingUrl, thumbnailUrl, price, sizeSqFt, pricePerSqFt}` (no capturedAt/verdict — those are on `WatchlistItem`).\n  - Fixture source: `sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` (fixtures.ts L185–188); live source `cuyahoga-arcgis` (cuyahoga-arcgis.ts L500). `CuyahogaFixtureProvider` (fixtures.ts L195) — `resolveCandidates` gated by `requireOwnCounty(options)`; `fetchParcelSnapshot` not gated.\n  - `requireLiveCounty(item, record, expectedCounty)` (agent-worker.ts L314) — coverage from `resolveCountyCoverage(item.county ?? null, record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null)`; `review` → `WorkerBlockedError('county_review')`; non-live → `WorkerBlockedError('unsupported_county')`; expectedCounty mismatch → `WorkerBlockedError('county_changed')`.\n  - User subcollections for zero-write counting: `properties` (+ nested `countyRecords` per property), `agentTasks`, `domainEvents`, `feedItems`, `actionItems`.\n  - Fake-firestore harness pattern: `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/agent-tasks-retry.test.ts` (state map + `runTransaction` closure); also used in `owner-requests.test.ts` and `src/lib/screening/__tests__/runs.test.ts`. `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts` has a fake harness special-casing `copilotActionExecutions` (will need `runTransaction` support for WU3).\n  - `recordedReadGuard(user, propertyId)` in `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`; `guardNotice(payload)` in `recorded-documents-section.tsx`; `PropertyCoverageNote` in `src/app/properties/page.tsx`.\n- Important semantic invariants:\n  - Explicit county is the only routing input except provenance backfill for missing county identity.\n  - Provenance backfill applies only when the explicit county is absent.\n  - Contradiction between explicit county and provenance is fail-closed `review`, not a routing note.\n  - County identity is never inferred from state/address; bare slug and registry slug are compared after stripping the two-letter state token.\n  - Non-live coverage states block county work with zero writes.\n  - Recorded-document reads may return stale stored results, but only with `authoritative: false` when coverage is no longer live.\n  - **All county mutation routes (resolve, confirm, refresh) must pass the snapshot provenance to `resolveCountyCoverage`** — verified all three are correct.\n- Seed data context:\n  - `scripts/seed-records-demo.ts` does **not** seed a county-less property with a confirmed county snapshot — the WU1 emulator test creates that legacy state itself via `saveResolution` + `confirmCountyParcel`.\n- Error/diagnostic events this session:\n  - `checkpoint_notes` validation failed 6× total: \"current: must not have more than 2048 characters\" (4×) and \"blockers: must have required properties blockers\" (1×). Learned to keep `current` under 2048 by trimming file lists; `blockers` must always be present (even as `[]`).\n  - Edit rejected once (earlier): \"RETRYABLE — Edit without read\" — read-before-edit guard requires a Read-tool read.\n  - First integration-test draft (resolve auto-confirm on county-less property) — unreachable: audited `requireLiveCounty` blocks `unknown` before any provider call.\n  - Second integration-test draft — all 3 failed during seeding with `CountyRecordsError: 'County records are not available for this property's area yet.'` — cause: `CuyahogaFixtureProvider.resolveCandidates` selection gate (missing `{ county }` option). Fixed by passing `{ county: CUYAHOGA }`.\n  - Test A (after gate fix) — `item.county` null: `runCountyRefresh` has no reconcile call; switched Test A to the `county_resolve` auto-confirm path.\n  - Test A — expected `countyReconciledFrom: 'cuyahoga-fixture'`, got `'cuyahoga-arcgis'`: reconcile uses registry canonical source id; fixed the test expectation (kept implementation).\n  - Test A — expected revision 3, got 4: worker auto-confirm = 2 CAS transitions (resolve r3 + confirm r4); fixed expectations to r4 + 2 events.\n  - Test C — `countUserDocs` before=4 received=5: the enqueue creates the task document; switched to domain-scoped `countSubcol` assertions.\n  - `coverage/route.ts` — `continue` inside `items.forEach` callback (syntax error) made the whole coverage test suite fail to run; converted to a `for` loop.\n  - Coverage test suite — route now imports `getCountyRecord` (real module breaks unit env); added `jest.mock('@/lib/firestore/county-records')`.\n  - Coverage test edit batch 1 — rejected: non-unique trailing `});` anchor (13 occurrences); re-anchored on the full last-test block (all-or-nothing, no partial state).\n  - Jest pattern with `[id]` unescaped matched only the coverage suite (bracket treated as character class); must escape as `\\[id\\]`.\n  - **RESOLVED**: refresh route review test — `expect(body.reason).toBe('review')` got `'planned'`. Root cause: test mock's `SNAPSHOT` constant had no `sourceId` in provenance; fix = inject `sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` into the mock. Not a route bug.\n  - Recorded-documents GET test — LSP error `Cannot find name 'getCountyRecord'`: the file had `jest.mock` but the named import was missing (dropped in a prior edit). Fixed by adding the import.\n  - `grep -F -f` with `comm -12` on sorted lists is more reliable for intersecting prettier warnings with git-changed files than raw `grep -F -f` (which can fail on whitespace).\n- Diagnostics status: all WU1-edited implementation + test files report clean JavaScript/TypeScript diagnostics.\n- Test status snapshot (current — all green):\n  - `src/lib/county-records/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts` — PASS\n  - `src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts` — PASS (incl. new review note test)\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts` — 15/15 (incl. new GET review test)\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts` — PASS (incl. new review case)\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/__tests__/route.test.ts` — 5/5\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/resolve/__tests__/route.test.ts` — 10/10\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/confirm/__tests__/route.test.ts` — 7/7 (incl. review zero-write)\n  - `src/app/api/pro