c/lib/firestore/domain-events.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/firestore/recorded-documents.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/firestore/__tests__/agent-tasks-retry.test.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/lib/screening/inputs.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/types/agent-tasks.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/types/records-dashboard.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/src/types/county-records.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/jest.setup.integration.js`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/docker-compose.yml`\n  - `/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/scripts/records-local-stack.sh`\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\n- Prior closeout commits referenced in `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`:\n  - `346765c`, `ae7c143`, `3b273a6`, `760710c`, `7654baa`, `ae6f77a`, `1484465`, `1b2976e`, `1a4301f`\n- WU3 implementation context still relevant:\n  - `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts` currently has read-then-unconditional-update races in `claimExecution` and `recordGateOutcome`.\n  - `CopilotActionExecution` currently persists caller-controlled `targetId` and `idempotencyKey` verbatim.\n  - Existing test harness `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts` has a fake-Firestore harness special-casing `copilotActionExecutions`; it will need `runTransaction` support for concurrent-reclaim tests.\n  - `firestore/county-records.ts` already uses a `CasOptions.delayBeforeCommitMs`-style pattern for transaction-barrier testing.\n- `verifier.requiredValidation`: \"Re-run the focused checks required by the acceptance criteria.\"\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n\n\n## Original Request\nThe user asked (after an automatic context compaction) to continue the previous task from the saved summary, complete its next concrete action, and not repeat completed work. The overarching task is a multi-work-unit (WU) audit gap-closure for a \"records-agent-launch\" feature. The immediate concrete actions were: finish WU1 (format flagged files, re-verify, commit) and then implement WU3 (make Copilot stale reclaim atomic and redact caller-controlled identifiers in `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts`).\n\n## Early Progress\n- Recovered state from NOTES.md: WU1 in progress on worktree `.worktrees/records-agent-launch` (base `a9eeff9`, branch `feat/records-agent-launch`, emulator UP :8095), all WU1 tests green (unit 1233/1233; county-reconcile integration 3/3; recorded-documents integration 8/8); 6 WU1 files needed `prettier --write`.\n- Confirmed prettier clean + capabilities/reconcile suites green; `git status` showed exactly the 23 WU1 files (21 modified + 2 new test files) plus one untracked plans doc to exclude.\n- Staged exactly the 23 WU1 files and committed → SHA `ac6ee29` (23 files, +1370/-95, pre-commit hooks clean, human-style message, no AI attribution); verified with `git log -1` and `git diff --stat`.\n- Started WU3: read all of `copilot-actions.ts` (found the read-then-unconditional-update race in `claimExecution`/`recordGateOutcome`, verbatim persistence of `targetId`/`idempotencyKey`, and no schema version); read the WU3 plan section (L63-84) and the test harness (`src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts`, 1021 lines; `createFakeDb` at L63 with `failCreate`/`failFinalize`, fixtures L168-305, record-shape assertions at L688/L860/L903/L935).\n- Requested and enabled deeper reasoning; confirmed only the execute route references the `copilotActionExecutions` collection (a comment) and that the import pattern is `import type { DocumentReference, Transaction } from 'firebase-admin/firestore'`.\n- Made 6 edits to `copilot-actions.ts` (all applied, TypeScript clean): (1) crash-boundary note in the module header (domain mutation + terminal audit transition non-atomic by design, reconciled via idempotent/CAS seams); (2) `Transaction`/`DocumentReference` import; (3) schema-v2 `CopilotActionExecution` interface (`schemaVersion?`, `targetRef?`, `keyRef?`; `targetId?`/`idempotencyKey?` made optional for v1 read-compat); (4) new helpers `EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION=2`, `keyedIdentifierRef` (sha256 of `uid|fingerprint|field|value`), `buildExecutionRecord`, `withExecutionRecord` (wraps `runTransaction`: tx.get snapshot → decide → create/update; empty commit = no-op; catch → `{ok:false}`), and module-level `decideRecord`; (5) rewrote `recordGateOutcome` to run through the transaction (terminal→replay, fresh→interrupted, stale/absent→terminal-failed); (6) rewrote `claimExecution` (fast out-of-tx read for replay/interrupted, then tx path where fresh→`tx.create` accepted and stale→`tx.update` executing/attempts+1; commit-conflict re-run gives exactly-one-winner).\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- Environment: worktree `.worktrees/records-agent-launch` on `feat/records-agent-launch` (WU1 now at `ac6ee29`; base `a9eeff9`); Firestore emulator UP on :8095; `IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS=5min`.\n- Just-completed action: the 6-block edit to `copilot-actions.ts` succeeded (TypeScript clean). **Immediate next step is the test side**, which the suffix continues:\n  - Extend the fake harness in `copilot-actions.test.ts` with `runTransaction` (per-db serialization queue; honor `failCreate`/`failFinalize` at commit time on staged create/update ops; fresh snapshot per run).\n  - Update the L688 \"successful action leaves exactly one terminal record\" test: it currently asserts raw `idempotencyKey === 'ui:message-1'` → must assert `keyRef` (64-hex), `schemaVersion===2`, and that the serialized record contains no raw identifiers.\n  - `seedExecution` seeds v1-shaped records (raw `targetId`/`idempotencyKey`) — reuse as the backward-compat (v1 replay) fixture.\n  - Add new unit tests: concurrent reclaim (seed crashed record `executing`, `updatedAt` −10min, `attempts`1; `Promise.all` two `executeCopilotAction` → one `executed` + one `interrupted`, domain seam called once, `attempts`2, terminal), concurrent fresh claim, identifier redaction (PII in `targetId` absent from serialization), v1 legacy replay, gate-settle-on-crashed.\n  - Add an emulator-backed concurrent-reclaim integration test at `__tests__/integration/firestore/copilot-reclaim.integration.test.ts` (seed county record via `saveResolution`; raw-seed a crashed execution record; two concurrent real POSTs to `/api/copilot/proposals/execute` → one `executed` + one `interrupted`; assert `agentTasks`=1, record `succeeded`/`attempts`2, domainEvents +1).\n- After WU3 (run tests, commit) the remaining units per the plan doc are: WU2 (provenance presentation on feed/task surfaces), WU4-6 (viewport/theme, screening columns, `scripts/records-local-stack.sh`), WU7 (`test-routes.md` + closeout reports + seed-twice test), WU8 (missing browser/integration evidence), WU9 (full verification at one exact commit + both closeout reports, then stop for GoalJudge/GoalVerifier).\n- Constraint: WU3 must stay in the parent/high-reasoning session (plan L207; subagents are local 9B only).\n\n<read-files>\n/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/dev/pi-subagents-local/README.md\n/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/notes/9b3f771d-b43a-45a1-a4e6-1cad29d7d7c4/NOTES.md\n/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts\n/Users/evanhuang/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch/docs/superpowe