{"type":"compaction","id":"3f889c0c","parentId":"8c4f4587","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:07:52.358Z","summary":"\n\n## Goal\n- Implement the immutable plan **Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan** from `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md` / untracked `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`.\n- Close the nine verified audit gaps, reconcile closeout evidence against one exact commit, then stop for `GoalJudge` and independent read-only `GoalVerifier` evaluation.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use the main session's currently selected PLAN / ORCHESTRATOR / YOLO mode and available tools; do not assume unavailable capabilities.\n- `GoalJudge` cannot mutate the goal; `GoalVerifier` is read-only acceptance verification.\n- Preserve all user changes and never disable/bypass pre-commit hooks, tests, authorization checks, provider gates, CAS, or idempotency controls.\n- Preserve county fail-closed behavior, explicit Copilot confirmation, durable audits, fixture honesty, product deferrals, and all existing checks.\n- Never infer Cuyahoga from Ohio/state/address, fabricate provenance, or turn external deferrals into fake functionality.\n- Work in `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch` on branch `feat/records-agent-launch`, audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` / short `a9eeff9`.\n- Deterministic suites must remain network-free; local-9B validation is opt-in, serial, and uses `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`.\n- WU1 county-coverage changes must keep all surfaces canonical: explicit county plus confirmed-snapshot provenance are the same resolver inputs everywhere; non-live/review states must fail closed with zero writes.\n- Tooling constraints learned this session: the read-before-edit guard requires a **Read-tool** read of each file (sed/bash views do not count); `checkpoint_notes.current` must be ≤2048 chars (trim before committing; `blockers` is a required field — omitting it fails validation); Jest patterns with bracketed paths like `[id]` must be escaped (`\\[id\\]`) or they match zero/wrong files; curl with visible stdout is blocked by a hook (use `-o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\"`).\n- **New**: `checkpoint_notes.current` 2048-char limit required aggressive compression (two failed attempts before the third succeeded at generation 44); keep file lists terse and use abbreviations (e.g., `Promise.all`, `→`, `=`) when filling it.\n- **New**: TypeScript closure-narrowing pitfall — `let x: T | null = null` declared *after* a closure that assigns it gets narrowed to `null`/`never` at later check sites (CFA doesn't track closure assignments). Fix: use a single `const obj = { prop: null as T | null }` declared *before* the closure; property access is not aggressively narrowed.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Ran `git status --short --branch`, `git worktree list --porcelain`, `git branch --show-current`, `git remote -v`.\n- [x] Confirmed repo state:\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard 450773f [main]`\n  - `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch a9eeff9 [feat/records-agent-launch]`\n  - Untracked: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-final-audit-gap-closure.md`\n  - Remote: `origin git@github.com:Brickspect/dashboard.git`\n- [x] Read prior material:\n  - `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-23-records-agent-post-audit-completion.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-post-audit-closeout-2026-08-23.md`\n  - `docs/records-agent-launch-final-report.md`\n- [x] Checked `todo` list: **No tasks**.\n- [x] Requested deeper reasoning (`request_deeper_reasoning`) for WU1 core because the fail-closed contradiction design ripples through route surfaces, worker, UI, and tests.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts`**\n  - Added a fifth `CountyCoverage` status: `review`.\n  - `review` is returned when explicit county and confirmed-snapshot provenance prove different counties after slug/base comparison.\n  - `review` is fail-closed: it is never `live`, even if one side is a covered county.\n  - `review` displays the explicit county and carries non-null `contradiction: { explicit, provenance }`.\n  - Updated `notCoveredPayload` so `reason` includes `'review'` and the message names both counties and says county work is paused. Exact review message: \"This property's county needs review: it is set to {explicit.name}, but a confirmed parcel proves it is in {provenance.name}. County work is paused until the county is resolved.\"\n  - Added `coverageNote(coverage)` helper returning client-safe `{ status, county, message, contradiction? }`; `contradiction` is set only for `review`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/county-records/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts`**\n  - Rewrote old permissive contradiction tests to fail-closed `review` semantics.\n  - Added tests for `notCoveredPayload(review)` and `coverageNote` behavior.\n  - Fixed import by adding `coverageNote`.\n  - Fixed stale test expecting old permissive note language.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/types/screening.ts`**\n  - Extended `ScreeningCoverage.status` to include `'review'`.\n  - No change needed in `src/lib/screening/inputs.ts` because `coverageForScreening` already forwards county-record snapshot provenance to `resolveCountyCoverage`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`.\n  - GET detail now resolves coverage with `property.county ?? null` plus `countyRecord?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null`.\n  - PATCH now resolves post-update coverage with the same provenance input so a contradictory county lands in `review` immediately.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/coverage/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`.\n  - Replaced explicit-only \"light projection\" with per-item county-record reads via `Promise.all(items.map((item) => getCountyRecord(user.id, item.id)))`.\n  - Each row resolves with `resolveCountyCoverage(identity, record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null)`.\n  - Added `review` to the deterministic `ORDER` map: `live: 0, planned: 1, not_covered: 2, review: 3`.\n  - **BUG FIXED**: the per-item loop was written as `items.forEach((item, index) => { ... continue; ... })` — a syntax error (`continue` outside an iteration statement) that made the entire coverage test suite fail to run under jest's parser. Converted to a proper `for (let index = 0; index < items.length; index += 1)` loop.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `getCountyRecord`, `coverageNote`, `resolveCountyCoverage`.\n  - GET now returns additive `coverage: Record<string, ReturnType<typeof coverageNote>>` keyed by property id.\n  - Uses `countyIdentityForProperty(item.county ?? undefined, item.state)` plus per-item county-record provenance.\n  - Updated `src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts` to mock `@/lib/firestore/county-records` and assert additive coverage behavior.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/properties/page.tsx`**\n  - Added exported `PropertyCoverageNote` type with optional `contradiction`.\n  - `fetchWatchlist` now parses and returns the server-provided `coverage` map.\n  - Added `coverageByProperty` state.\n  - Both watchlist load paths set `coverageByProperty`; error path clears it.\n  - List pill now uses `coverageByProperty[p.id] ?? resolveCountyCoverage(p.county ?? null, null)`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/components/records-dashboard/county-coverage-banner.tsx`**\n  - Widened `CoveragePill` `coverage` prop from full `CountyCoverage` to `{ status: CountyCoverage['status'] }` so both full deep-dive coverage and list notes are accepted.\n  - Added amber `review` pill variant with `data-testid=\"coverage-pill-review\"`.\n  - Added `CountyCoverageBanner` `review` case naming both counties and explaining county work is paused.\n  - `showForm` now includes `review`; chip label renders `'Needs review'`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/types/recorded-documents.ts`**\n  - Added `RecordedCoverageNote`:\n    - `status: 'live' | 'planned' | 'not_covered' | 'unknown' | 'review'`\n    - `county: { code: string; name: string } | null`\n    - `message: string | null`\n  - Added `RecordedSearchGuardedResponse = RecordedSearchResponse & { authoritative: boolean; coverage: RecordedCoverageNote }`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`**\n  - Added `recordedReadGuard(user, propertyId)`.\n  - It reads `getWatchlistItem` and `getCountyRecord` in parallel.\n  - It resolves canonical coverage using the same inputs as the search POST gate:\n    - `property.county ?? null`\n    - `record?.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null`\n  - Returns `{ authoritative: coverage.status === 'live', coverage: coverageNote(coverage) }`.\n  - Restored `requireRecordedProperty` after an accidental placeholder clobber.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `recordedReadGuard`.\n  - GET root spreads `{ ...guard }` into both the inline `not_started` payload and the latest search response.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/route.ts`**\n  - Imported `recordedReadGuard`.\n  - GET search poll spreads `{ ...search, ...guard }` into the response.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/components/records-dashboard/recorded-documents-section.tsx`**\n  - Added `guardNotice(payload)` helper.\n  - Added `coverageNotice` state.\n  - `loadState` and poll path call `setCoverageNotice(guardNotice(payload))`.\n  - Renders amber notice when `authoritative === false` and `coverage.message` exists.\n  - Added `data-testid=\"recorded-coverage-notice\"`.\n  - Additive guard fields keep existing `isSearchResponse` checks passing.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/firestore/properties.ts` — transactional reconcile (replaces non-atomic backfill)**\n  - REMOVED `backfillWatchlistCounty` (non-atomic read-then-set, line ~94). Only caller was the worker; no test referenced it (grep-verified).\n  - Added `CountyReconcileOutcome` union type: `{ status: 'reconciled'; county } | { status: 'already_reconciled'; county } | { status: 'explicit_conflict'; county; stored } | { status: 'property_gone' }`.\n  - Added `reconcileWatchlistCounty(uid, propertyId, county, sourceId)` using `getFirestoreDb().runTransaction`:\n    - property absent → `property_gone` (no write)\n    - existing county, same base (after `countyBase(normalizeCountyCode(...))` on both) → `already_reconciled` (NO write; returns the STORED identity, not the derived one; no normalization)\n    - existing county, different base → `explicit_conflict` (NO write — explicit assertion never overwritten)\n    - county absent → `tx.set(ref, { county, countyReconciledFrom: sourceId, countyReconciledAt: new Date().toISOString() }, { merge: true })` → `reconciled`\n  - Errors PROPAGATE (never swallowed inside the function).\n  - Imports `countyBase, normalizeCountyCode` from `@/lib/county-records/capabilities`.\n  - Diagnostics clean.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/agent-worker.ts` — worker wiring**\n  - Import swapped: `backfillWatchlistCounty` → `reconcileWatchlistCounty` (L69).\n  - `requireLiveCounty` (L314): added explicit review branch BEFORE the generic `!== 'live'` check: `if (coverage.status === 'review') throw new WorkerBlockedError('county_review', notCoveredPayload(coverage).message)` — distinct code, since this is a human-only contradiction, not \"county unsupported\".\n  - Local helper `backfillCountyBestEffort` (L343, old numbering) replaced by `reconcileCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage)` (L364): early-returns if `item.county` (explicit never touched); calls `reconcileWatchlistCounty(uid, item.id, coverage.county, coverage.source.id)`; `explicit_conflict` → `console.info` (review state surfaces on read surfaces, no write); thrown error → `console.error` with property/county/source ids — NEVER rethrows (the CAS parcel confirm is already durable; failing/retrying the task would CAS-conflict on stale revision; idempotent re-attempt happens on next county work).\n  - Both call sites updated to `await reconcileCountyBestEffort(uid, item, coverage)`: L578 (auto-confirm branch inside `runCountyResolve` — unique match auto-confirms and now reconciles; comment updated to \"same transactional reconcile the explicit confirm lane uses\") and L666 (`runCountyConfirm`). Verified `runCountyRefresh` (L674) has NO backfill/reconcile call (refresh doesn't change identity) — nothing to do. Line numbers shifted +34 from pre-edit (544→578, 632→666).\n  - File diagnostics clean.\n- [x] **WU1 test fixes — all existing WU1-affected unit suites green**:\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added `jest.mock('@/lib/firestore/county-records', ...)`; added PATCH review test. **14/14 PASS**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added county-records mock + guard assertions + non-authoritative test. **Green**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/searches/[searchId]/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added mock + guard assertions + contradictory non-authoritative test. **5/5 PASS**.\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/resolve/__tests__/route.test.ts`: updated stale test to new fail-closed review payload (`reason: 'review'`, `eta: null`, `/needs review/i` + `/paused/i`). **10/10 PASS**.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts` (NEW) — reconcile unit matrix, 6/6 PASS** (fake-DB harness; reconciled / idempotent / same-base / explicit_conflict / property_gone / error propagation).\n- [x] **Emulator environment restored**: started `docker compose up -d firestore-emulator` (container `records-agent-launch-firestore-emulator-1`, `localhost:8095`, project `demo-brickspect-dashboard`). Recorded-documents integration **8/8 PASS**.\n- [x] **WU1: `__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` (NEW) — 3/3 PASS against emulator**:\n  - Seeding strategy (all real seams, no raw record writes): `upsertWatchlistItem` (`county: null`) → `saveResolution` (`status: 'confirmation_required'`, fixture candidates, `expectedRevision: 0`) → `confirmCountyParcel` (`expectedRevision: 1`) → confirmed r2 with a genuine fixture snapshot. `ADDR = { street: '5180 broadview road', unit: null, city: 'cleveland', state: 'OH', zip: '44143' }`; fixture provider `CuyahogaFixtureProvider` (imported from `@/lib/county-records/fixtures`).\n  - Test A (\"a re-resolution with a unique match auto-confirms and reconciles a legacy county-less property\"): enqueue `county_resolve` (`{ expectedRevision: 2, address: ADDR }`) → `processOneTask` → task `succeeded`; county = `CUYAHOGA`; raw doc has `countyReconciledFrom: 'cuyahoga-arcgis'` (registry canonical source id — see Key Decisions) + string `countyReconciledAt`; record revision **4**; domainEvents = eventsBefore + **2** (worker auto-confirm = `saveResolution` r3 `county_record_resolved` + `confirmCountyParcel` r4 `county_record_confirmed`).\n  - Test B (\"a direct reconciliation is idempotent: a re-attempt writes nothing\"): first `reconcileWatchlistCounty` → `reconciled`; second → `already_reconciled`; `countUserDocs` unchanged; county unchanged.\n  - Test C (\"a review contradiction blocks worker county work with zero domain writes\"): after seeding, `updateWatchlistItemCounty(uid, propertyId, SUMMIT)` (real PATCH seam creates the contradiction) → enqueue `county_refresh` (`{ expectedRevision: 2, county: CUYAHOGA }`) → `processOneTask` → task `blocked` with `error.code: 'county_review'`; **zero domain writes**: `agentTasks` = 1 (only the enqueued task doc; `blockTask` writes no domain event), `domainEvents` unchanged, county record revision + snapshot unchanged, county still Summit.\n  - Helpers: `seedLegacyConfirmed`, `rawPropertyDoc`, `countUserDocs`, `countSubcol`, `runRefresh`, `runResolve`.\n  - Key diagnosis during authoring: the first draft (resolve auto-confirm on a county-less property) was **unreachable** — the audited-baseline `requireLiveCounty` blocks county work for county-less properties (coverage `unknown` → `unsupported_county`) BEFORE any provider call; the only path to a county for a county-less property is a legacy confirmed snapshot (provenance → live coverage). The second draft failed on the fixture provider's selection gate (`CuyahogaFixtureProvider.resolveCandidates` requires `{ county }` options or it throws `unsupported_county`; `fetchParcelSnapshot` does not). Also: the worker in the emulator environment runs the ArcGIS provider variant with a local/no-network data path (auto-confirm succeeded offline in ~327ms).\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/coverage/__tests__/route.test.ts` — 7/7 PASS**:\n  - Added `jest.mock('@/lib/firestore/county-records', () => ({ getCountyRecord: jest.fn() }))` (route now imports `getCountyRecord`; unmocked real module breaks the unit env) + stubs in all 5 pre-existing tests.\n  - Added NEW review-agreement test: item with explicit `summit-oh` + `getCountyRecord` mock `{ status: 'confirmed', revision: 4, snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture', ... } } }` → row `{ code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County', state: 'OH', status: 'review', eta: null, sourceLabel: null, propertyCount: 1 }`, `unknownCount: 0`.\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/confirm/__tests__/route.test.ts`** — added review 422 zero-write test (Summit item + record snapshot provenance `cuyahoga-fixture` → 422 `not_covered`/`review`, message matches `/Summit County/` + `/Cuyahoga County/` + `/paused/i`, `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent` NOT called, no-store). **7/7 PASS** (suite green).\n- [x] **WU1: `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/refresh/__tests__/route.test.ts`** — added the same review 422 zero-write test. **Initially FAILED** (`reason` got `'planned'` instead of `'review'`): the test's `storedRecord()` mock used the default `SNAPSHOT` constant whose provenance has no `sourceId` (only `sourceUpdateAt`, `taxBillUpdateAt`, `retrievedAt`), so `resolveCountyCoverage(Summit, null)` → `planned` (Summit is a planned county). **FIXED** by overriding the record's snapshot provenance with `sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` in the mock, mirroring the confirm test. **6/6 PASS**.\n- [x] **WU1: Detail GET review test** — `src/app/api/properties/[id]/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added test \"reports the fail-closed review state (explicit county vs confirmed parcel) on GET\" after the last GET test (L333-345). The `watched` fixture (L195) has NO county field (undefined); spread it and add `county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' }`. Mock `getCountyRecord` with `{ status: 'confirmed', revision: 4, snapshot: { provenance: { sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture', ... } } }`. Asserts `body.coverage` deep-equals the RAW `CountyCoverage` review union: `{status:'review', county:{code:'summit-oh',name:'Summit County'}, eta:null, source:null, contradiction:{explicit:{code:'summit-oh',name:'Summit County'}, provenance:{code:'cuyahoga-oh',name:'Cuyahoga County'}}}`. NO `message` field on this surface. **PASS** (suite 15/15 with new test).\n- [x] **WU1: List review note test** — `src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added test \"flags a contradictory property with the review note (explicit county vs confirmed parcel)\" after the \"includes the latest screening run projection\" test. Item: `{ ...watched, county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' } }` (the `watched` fixture in this file has `county: null`). Mock `getCountyRecord` with snapshot provenance `cuyahoga-fixture`. Asserts `body.coverage['prop-001']` equals `{status:'review', county:{code:'summit-oh',name:'Summit County'}, message: expect.stringMatching(/needs review/), contradiction:{explicit:{code:'summit-oh',name:'Summit County'}, provenance:{code:'cuyahoga-oh',name:'Cuyahoga County'}}}`. Also asserts `message` matches `/Cuyahoga County/`. **PASS** (suite green).\n- [x] **WU1: Recorded-documents GET review test** — `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts`: added test \"flags stored results as non-authoritative when the county is in review\" after the unknown non-authoritative test. Item: `{ ...WATCH_ITEM, county: { code: 'summit-oh', name: 'Summit County' } }`. Mock `getCountyRecord` with snapshot provenance `cuyahoga-fixture`; `getLatestRecordedSearch` → `SEARCH`. Asserts: `body.authoritative` false, `body.coverage.status` 'review', `body.coverage.county?.code` 'summit-oh', message matches `/Summit County/` and `/Cuyahoga County/`. **LSP error**: `getCountyRecord` name not found — the file had a `jest.mock` for `@/lib/firestore/county-records` but the named import was missing (it had been dropped; the earlier unknown test didn't need it). **FIXED** by adding `import { getCountyRecord } from '@/lib/firestore/county-records'`. **PASS** (suite green).\n- [x] **All three extended route-agreement suites re-run**: `npx jest \"src/app/api/properties/\\[id\\]/__tests__/route.test.ts\" \"src/app/api/properties/__tests__/route.test.ts\" \"src/app/api/properties/\\[id\\]/recorded-documents/__tests__/route.test.ts\"` → **3 suites, 34 tests, ALL PASS**.\n- [x] **FULL unit suite**: `npx jest --selectProjects unit` → **97/97 suites passed (1 skipped suite, 2 skipped tests — pre-existing), 1233/1233 tests PASS**. Time: 2.854s.\n- [x] **Prettier audit**: `npx prettier --check \"src/**/*.{ts,tsx}\"` → 37 repo-wide warnings. Cross-referenced with `git status --porcelain` via `comm -12` on sorted lists → exactly **6 WU1 files** need `prettier --write`: `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts`, `src/lib/county-records/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts`, `src/lib/firestore/properties.ts`, `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts`, `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`, `src/components/records-dashboard/county-coverage-banner.tsx`. The other ~31 warnings are pre-existing drift in files not touched this session (excluded from WU1 commit; deferred to WU9's repo-wide Prettier step).\n- [x] **Prettier --write applied** to the 6 flagged WU1 files. LSP clean on all 6.\n- [x] **Post-Prettier re-run**: `npx jest \"src/lib/county-records\" \"src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile\"` → 6 suites, 219/220 tests pass (1 skipped), Prettier check on all 6 files → \"All matched files use Prettier code style!\".\n- [x] Committed checkpoint notes through generation **40** (sha256 `c57a80fe3a25`) at `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/notes/9b3f771d-b43a-45a1-a4e6-1cad29d7d7c4/NOTES.md`.\n- [x] **WU1 COMMITTED**: Staged exactly the 23 WU1 files, committed as **`ac6ee29`** (23 files, +1370/-95, pre-commit hooks clean, human-style message, no AI attribution). Verified with `git log -1` and `git diff --stat`. Tree clean except untracked plans doc.\n- [x] **WU3 implementation APPLIED to `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts`** (LSP clean, 1666ms check). Six edits:\n  1. Crash-boundary note in module header (domain mutation + terminal audit transition non-atomic by design, reconciled via idempotent/CAS seams).\n  2. `import type { DocumentReference, Transaction } from 'firebase-admin/firestore'`.\n  3. `CopilotActionExecution` interface: added `schemaVersion?`, `targetRef?`, `keyRef?`; made `targetId?` and `idempotencyKey?` optional (v1 read-compat).\n  4. New helpers: `EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`; `keyedIdentifierRef(uid, fp, field, value)` = `sha256Hex(uid + '|' + fp + '|' + field + '|' + value)`; `buildExecutionRecord` (v2 writes, never raw identifiers); `withExecutionRecord` (wraps `db.runTransaction`: tx.get → decide → fresh→tx.create / reclaim→tx.update executing+attempts+1 / replay|interrupted→no write; catch→`{ok:false, code:'audit_unavailable'}`); `decideRecord` moved to module scope.\n  5. `claimExecution` rewritten: fast out-of-tx read (replay/interrupted fast path), then tx path for claim.\n  6. `recordGateOutcome` rewritten: runs through `withExecutionRecord` (terminal→replay result, fresh→interrupted, stale/absent→stage terminal failed/tampered; does NOT touch `attempts`).\n- [x] **WU3 test harness extended** in `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts`: replaced `createFakeDb` (L63) with a version that adds `db.runTransaction(fn)` — per-db `txQueue` (Promise chain) serializes runs; each run snapshots the store at its turn; `tx.get/create/update/set` stage writes; commit applies staged atomically; retry up to 3 runs on throw (models Firestore commit-conflict retry). `makeDoc` gains `__key` property so tx ops map to the store. `failCreate`/`failFinalize` honored at **commit time** on staged tx ops (keeps existing L718/L781 failure-injection tests working). **TS fix applied**: initial draft declared `let stagedCreate/Update/Set` after the tx closure → CFA narrowed to `null`/`never` (10 property errors); fixed by using a single `const staged = { create: null as ...|null, update: ..., set: ... }` object declared before `tx`. LSP clean (973ms).\n- [x] Committed checkpoint notes through generation **44** (sha256 `c5db95bf5906`).\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] **WU3 — tests in `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts`** (harness extended; LSP clean):\n  - **Immediate**: run the copilot-actions suite to get the current pass/fail count after the harness fix (previous run showed expected `failCreate`/`failFinalize` console.error output but the final test summary was truncated at 100 chars — need full output).\n  - Update L688 test: replace raw `idempotencyKey` assertion → assert `schemaVersion === 2`, `targetRef`/`keyRef` match `/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/`, `JSON.stringify(record)` contains no raw `'task-1'`/`'ui:message-1'`; keep `attempts === 1`.\n  - Add 5 new unit tests:\n    1. **Concurrent reclaim**: seed crashed record (`state: 'executing'`, `updatedAt: Date.now()-10min`, `attempts: 1`) via `seedExecution`; `Promise.all` two `executeCopilotAction` (same request, `county_confirm`, live county, one candidate) → codes `{executed, interrupted}`, `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent` called ONCE, record `succeeded`/`attempts: 2`/`schemaVersion: 2`.\n    2. **Concurrent fresh claim**: no seed; `Promise.all` two calls → one `executed` + one `interrupted`, store size 1, `attempts: 1`.\n    3. **Identifier redaction**: `targetId: 'victim@example.com'` → no raw value in `JSON.stringify(record)`, `targetRef` 64-hex, no `targetId`/`idempotencyKey` properties.\n    4. **v1 legacy replay**: `seedExecution` base is v1-shape (raw fields, no `schemaVersion`) → terminal `succeeded` seed replays `executed` without dispatch.\n    5. **Concurrent gate settle on crashed**: two concurrent TAMPERED confirmations on a stale seeded record → both return `'tampered'`, record `failed`/`tampered`, `attempts` unchanged (1).\n  - **NEW emulator integration test** `__tests__/integration/firestore/copilot-reclaim.integration.test.ts` (mirror `county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` pattern): real POSTs to `/api/copilot/proposals/execute`; seed watchlist item + county record via `upsertWatchlistItem`+`saveResolution` (confirmation_required, 1 candidate, resolvedAddress, revision N); raw-seed a crashed execution record into `users/{uid}/copilotActionExecutions/{fingerprint}` (fingerprint via imported `proposalFingerprint`, state `executing`, `updatedAt` now-10min, `attempts` 1); two concurrent fetches → one `executed` + one `interrupted`; assert `agentTasks`=1, record `succeeded`/`attempts: 2`, `domainEvents` +1, no second task.\n  - Run copilot-actions unit suite + full unit suite, `prettier --write` touched files, commit WU3 (3 files: `copilot-actions.ts` + test file + new integration test; no AI attribution).\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Work in the existing records-agent worktree**: Continue on `feat/records-agent-launch` rather than starting a new branch, because the audit plan explicitly anchors to audited commit `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be` and existing closeout docs.\n- **Follow the plan's execution order**: county resolver/reconciliation first, then Copilot atomic reclaim/redaction, provenance rollout, theme/screening/local-stack lanes, documentation/seed evidence, missing browser/integration evidence, and full verification.\n- **Treat prior closeout as context, not proof**: New claims must come from newly executed checks against a single recorded commit; unavailable evidence must be reported as unavailable.\n- **WU1 contradiction is fail-closed `review`, not permissive annotation**: If explicit county and confirmed-snapshot provenance prove different counties, the result is `status: 'review'`; no county work runs until a human resolves it, even if one county is live.\n- **Review displays the explicit county**: The explicit county is the user assertion and is displayed; the provenance county is named in the message.\n- **Canonical inputs are explicit county + confirmed-snapshot provenance**: Property detail, `/api/coverage`, `/api/properties` list, screening, county mutation routes, worker selection, and recorded-document reads all resolve from `resolveCountyCoverage(explicitCounty, confirmedSourceId)` (or equivalent normalized county identity plus the same provenance source id).\n- **Provenance is only a migration/backfill signal, never inferred from state/address**: A county-less legacy property with a confirmed Cuyahoga snapshot can resolve live through provenance; a county-less property without provenance stays unknown.\n- **Recorded-document reads get additive guard fields**: Stored search documents remain retrievable, but non-live coverage reads return `authoritative: false` plus a typed `coverage` note so stale county-specific results are not presented as current authoritative data.\n- **Additive recorded-read fields are backward-compatible**: The UI's `isSearchResponse` checks only `status` membership in `SEARCH_STATUSES`.\n- **`CoveragePill` accepts a minimal status shape**: prop widened to `{ status: CountyCoverage['status'] }`.\n- **`coverageNote` carries optional contradiction only for `review`**.\n- **Worker `county_review` blocked code is safe**: `WorkerBlockedError` → ALWAYS `blocking` → `blockTask` → task `blocked` with `error: { code, message }`.\n- **Transactional county reconciliation must never overwrite explicit county**: outcomes `already_reconciled` (same base) or `explicit_conflict` (different base); explicit assertions never silently overwritten.\n- **Reconcile failure after a durable confirm must not fail the task or roll back**: worker catches + logs, never rethrows.\n- **Same-base idempotency does not normalize**: stored `'cuyahoga'` vs derived `'cuyahoga-oh'` → `already_reconciled`, returns the STORED identity.\n- **Only Cuyahoga can be proven by snapshot provenance**: `countyForSourceId(sourceId)` matches ONLY registry entries with non-null `source` — currently only Cuyahoga. The only producible review contradiction is explicit non-Cuyahoga + Cuyahoga-confirmed parcel; `'lorain-fixture'` is not a producible source. Test fixtures must use `cuyahoga-fixture`/`cuyahoga-arcgis` provenance with a non-Cuyahoga explicit county.\n- **Two distinct response contracts — tests must match each surface**: detail/PATCH routes return the RAW `CountyCoverage` union (no `message` field); recorded-read routes and list notes use `coverageNote`/`notCoveredPayload` shapes (which carry `message`).\n- **Auto-confirm lives inside `runCountyResolve`**: worker handlers `runCountyResolve` (L423; auto-confirm branch), `runCountyConfirm` (L586), `runCountyRefresh` (L674, NO reconcile call). Reconcile call sites at L578 + L666.\n- **Deeper reasoning was justified for WU1** (xhigh pass requested).\n- **Check the emulator FIRST for integration-suite timeouts**: the recorded-documents 8/8 timeout was environmental (emulator down).\n- **The emulator stays running for the rest of the session** (WU1 emulator test, WU8, WU9).\n- **Reconcile metadata uses the registry's canonical source id, not the per-run snapshot provenance**: `reconcileCountyBestEffort` passes `coverage.source.id` (registry canonical `'cuyahoga-arcgis'`), not `snapshot.provenance.sourceId` (which could be `'cuyahoga-fixture'` in dev). Rationale: the registry source id is the stable, environment-independent identity of the county's source (both fixture and ArcGIS variants resolve to the same provenance county via `countyForSourceId`); in production the worker's live provider provenance equals it anyway. The test expectation was changed to `'cuyahoga-arcgis'` rather than the implementation.\n- **Fixture provider `resolveCandidates` requires an explicit county selection**: `CuyahogaFixtureProvider.resolveCandidates(addr, options)` calls `requireOwnCounty(options)` and throws `'unsupported_county'` (\"County records are not available for this property's area yet.\") when `options.county` is absent or not Cuyahoga — mirroring the live provider's selection gate. `fetchParcelSnapshot(objectId, options)` has NO such gate (reads only `options.scenario`, default `'exact'`). `CountyProviderOptions` is defined in `src/lib/county-records/provider.ts:22`. Tests must pass `{ county: CUYAHOGA }` to `resolveCandidates`.\n- **Worker auto-confirm = 2 CAS transitions**: `runCountyResolve`'s unique-match branch commits `saveResolution` (r+1, event `county_record_resolved`, `lastRefresh: null`, `candidates: [selected]`) then `confirmCountyParcel` against `pending.revision` (r+2, event `county_record_confirmed`), then `reconcileCountyBestEffort`. A re-resolution from r2 therefore lands at r4 with 2 new domain events.\n- **`blockTask` writes no domain event**: only the task document itself changes (status → `blocked`, error set). Zero-write assertions must be **domain-scoped** (events/record/county), not total document count — the enqueue itself legitimately creates the task document.\n- **The refresh route review test failure was a test-mock issue, not a route bug**: the refresh route's gate was correct (it passed `record.snapshot?.provenance?.sourceId ?? null`); the test's `storedRecord()` mock used the default `SNAPSHOT` constant whose provenance lacks `sourceId`, so `resolveCountyCoverage(Summit, null)` → `planned`. Fix: inject `sourceId: 'cuyahoga-fixture'` into the mock's snapshot provenance, mirroring the confirm test.\n- **All route-agreement WU1 tests share the same fixture pair**: explicit `summit-oh` + confirmed snapshot provenance `'cuyahoga-fixture'` → `review`.\n- **`coverageNote(review)` reuses `notCoveredPayload`'s message and adds the contradiction** — one wording, three surfaces (detail = raw union without message; list + recorded = `coverageNote` with message + contradiction).\n- **`comm -12` on sorted lists** is the clean way to intersect Prettier warnings with git-changed files (avoids `grep -F -f` whitespace issues).\n- **Prettier --write only on the 6 flagged WU1 files**; pre-existing drift in other files is out of WU1 scope (deferred to WU9's repo-wide Prettier step).\n- **Full unit suite runs in ~3s** (fast, deterministic, network-free) — safe to re-run often.\n- **WU3 advisory findings are all consistent with existing module patterns** (no action needed): (1) `keyedIdentifierRef`/`EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION` exported but unused in-module — the test file will import both, making them used; Knip flags on pre-existing re-exported allowlist consts (`COPILOT_PROPOSAL_ONLY` etc.) are the established import surface. (2) `switch-without-default` in the tx closure — all four union members of `decision.kind` are covered; TS exhaustiveness check guarantees the default is unreachable; the existing `dispatchAction` switch also has no default. (3) `no-console-except-error ×2` — matches the pre-existing `console.error` pattern in the finalize catch. (4) `pass-through-wrapper` on `withExecutionRecord` — intentional isolation boundary between the transaction wrapper and the domain logic.\n- **Fake Firestore `runTransaction` models serialization, not true concurrency**: per-db Promise queue makes runs exclusive; each run snapshots the store at its turn (sees everything prior runs committed); the real Firestore SDK's snapshot-read + commit-conflict-retry is modeled by re-snapshotting on each retry run. True concurrent-winner semantics are proven by the emulator integration test, not the unit fake.\n- **`failCreate`/`failFinalize` are honored at commit time for staged tx ops** (not at stage time): `tx.create` stages `{doc, d}`; the commit phase checks `failCreate` (throws before `store.has`/`store.set`) and `failFinalize` (throws if `d.state` is terminal). This keeps the pre-existing L718 (audit-persistence-failure → `audit_unavailable`, store empty) and L781 (finalize-failure-after-successful-mutation → `audit_unavailable`) tests working unchanged.\n- **Gate-settle on a stale record does NOT touch `attempts`** (matches pre-WU3 behavior where the gate path never incremented attempts; only the claim path does).\n- **TS closure-narrowing fix for staged writes**: `let x: T | null = null` declared after a closure that assigns it gets CFA-narrowed to `null`/`never` at later check sites. The fix is a single `const staged = { prop: null as T | null }` object declared before the closure; property access retains its declared type through CFA.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. **WU3 tests** (continue in `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts`, harness already extended and LSP-clean):\n   - Run `npx jest \"src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts\"` to get the full pass/fail summary after the harness fix (previous run output was truncated; expect the 27/32 `db.runTransaction is not a function` failures to be resolved).\n   - Update the L688 \"successful action leaves exactly one terminal record\" test: replace the raw `idempotencyKey` assertion with `schemaVersion === 2`, `targetRef`/`keyRef` 64-hex, and `JSON.stringify(record)` free of raw identifiers.\n   - Add the five new unit tests (concurrent reclaim, concurrent fresh claim, identifier redaction, v1 legacy replay, concurrent gate settle on crashed).\n   - Create `__tests__/integration/firestore/copilot-reclaim.integration.test.ts` (emulator-backed concurrent reclaim).\n   - Run copilot-actions unit suite + full unit suite; `prettier --write` on all three WU3 files; commit WU3 (3 files, no AI attribution).\n2. **WU2** (provenance presentation on feed/task surfaces).\n3. **WU4-6** (viewport/theme, screening columns, `scripts/records-local-stack.sh`).\n4. **WU7** (`test-routes.md` + closeout reports + seed-twice test).\n5. **WU8** (missing browser/integration evidence).\n6. **WU9** (full verification at one exact commit + both closeout reports, then stop for GoalJudge/GoalVerifier).\n\n## Critical Context\n- `loopId`: `7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866`\n- `originalPlan` path: `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/goal-loops/7ba885b3-76f1-4ab1-89ca-6a3d84043866/original-plan.md`\n- `originalPlan` hash: `b1642915c461fd2e2b379dd15404f144542a94533bea65b33b1b9e0fd0a1637a`\n- Audited commit: `a9eeff99715775a7392e8cc8ab367e5ee3f5a4be`\n- Current branch/worktree:\n  - branch `feat/records-agent-launch`\n  - worktree `~/brickspect/dashboard/.worktrees/records-agent-launch`\n  - main checkout `~/brickspect/dashboard` on `main` at `450773f`\n- **Commit history this session**: `ac6ee29` (WU1, 23 files, +1370/-95, committed). WU3 changes (`copilot-actions.ts` + test harness) are uncommitted working-tree edits.\n- Latest checkpoint notes:\n  - path: `/Users/evanhuang/.pi/agent/notes/9b3f771d-b43a-45a1-a4e6-1cad29d7d7c4/NOTES.md`\n  - latest generation committed: `44` (sha256 `c5db95bf5906`).\n- **Firestore emulator: RUNNING**: `docker compose up -d firestore-emulator` → container `records-agent-launch-firestore-emulator-1`, `localhost:8095`, project `demo-brickspect-dashboard`. `jest.setup.integration.js` sets `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST`, `FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=demo-brickspect-dashboard`, `ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=true`, deletes `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID`, `NODE_ENV=test`. Keep it up for all remaining integration/E2E work.\n- Original user input was `icontinue` (typo for \"continue\"), asking the assistant to proceed with executing the Records Agent Final Audit-Gap Closure Plan.\n- Environment/local-mode context:\n  - Main model: `qwen38-main/qwen3.8-27b` via vLLM `192.168.93.107:18020`.\n  - Subagents must use local 9B `qwopus-subagent/qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp` via gateway `192.168.93.107:8082`, serialized only.\n  - 9B context: 98k ctx, 16k max output.\n  - Local 9B provider contract:\n    - `AI_PROVIDER=local`\n    - `AI_PROVIDER_FALLBACKS=`\n    - `LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://192.168.93.107:8082/v1`\n    - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=none`\n    - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwopus3.5-9b-coder-mtp`\n    - `LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=300000`\n    - Probe only `GET http://192.168.93.107:8082/v1/models`; never probe `/health`.\n- Key WU1 files (all committed in `ac6ee29`):\n  - `src/lib/county-records/capabilities.ts` + `__tests__/capabilities.test.ts`\n  - `src/types/screening.ts`, `src/types/recorded-documents.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/route.ts` + `__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/coverage/route.ts` + `__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/route.ts` + `__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `src/app/properties/page.tsx`, `src/components/records-dashboard/county-coverage-banner.tsx`, `src/components/records-dashboard/recorded-documents-section.tsx`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/recorded-documents/shared.ts`, `route.ts`, `searches/[searchId]/route.ts` + their test files\n  - `src/lib/firestore/properties.ts` + `src/lib/firestore/__tests__/properties-reconcile.test.ts` (NEW)\n  - `src/lib/agent-worker.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/resolve/__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/confirm/__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `src/app/api/properties/[id]/county-records/refresh/__tests__/route.test.ts`\n  - `__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` (NEW — 3/3 PASS)\n- Key WU3 files (uncommitted working-tree edits):\n  - `src/lib/copilot-actions.ts` — implementation (6 edits, LSP clean)\n  - `src/lib/__tests__/copilot-actions.test.ts` — harness extended with `runTransaction` (LSP clean, 973ms); tests not yet updated\n- Key existing functions/types relevant to WU3:\n  - `executeCopilotAction(uid, request)` — entry point; calls `claimExecution` → `dispatchAction` → finalize.\n  - `claimExecution(uid, record, fingerprint)` — fast read outside tx (replay/interrupted), then `withExecutionRecord` tx path.\n  - `recordGateOutcome(uid, record, gateResult, fingerprint)` — tx-based settle for gate failures (tampered etc.).\n  - `withExecutionRecord(uid, fingerprint, fn)` — wraps `getFirestoreDb().runTransaction`; returns `{ok:true, record}` or `{ok:false, code:'audit_unavailable'}`.\n  - `decideRecord(record, fingerprint, now)` — module-scope classifier: `replay` / `interrupted` / `fresh` / `stale` / `absent`.\n  - `buildExecutionRecord(record, targetId, idempotencyKey)` — produces v2 shape with `targetRef`/`keyRef` (sha256) instead of raw values.\n  - `keyedIdentifierRef(uid, fp, field, value)` — `sha256Hex(uid + '|' + fp + '|' + field + '|' + value)`.\n  - `EXECUTION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`.\n  - `IN_FLIGHT_GRACE_MS` = 5 min (stale threshold for reclaim).\n  - `proposalFingerprint` — exported from the module; used to compute the fingerprint for raw-seeding in the integration test.\n  - Existing test harness structure (post-extension):\n    - `createFakeDb(over: FakeOptions)` → `{ db, store }`\n    - `FakeOptions`: `{ failCreate?: boolean; failFinalize?: boolean }`\n    - `store`: `Map<string, StoredRecord>` keyed by `uid:fp`\n    - `makeDoc(uid, fp)` → `{ __key, get, create, update, set }` (plain doc ops)\n    - `db.collection('users').doc(uid).collection('copilotActionExecutions').doc(fp)` → `makeDoc(uid, fp)`\n    - `db.runTransaction(fn)` → serialized via per-db `txQueue`; `fn(tx)` receives `{get, create, update, set}` that stage writes; commit applies staged atomically; retry ≤3 runs on throw.\n    - `seedExecution(uid, fp, overrides)` — writes a v1-shaped record (raw `targetId`/`idempotencyKey`, no `schemaVersion`) as the backward-compat fixture.\n    - `stored(uid, fp)` — reads from `store`.\n    - Test fixtures at L168-305 (old numbering): `proposal()`, `makeRequest()`, `watchItem`, `SNAPSHOT`, etc.\n    - `beforeEach` (L296, old numbering) recreates the fake db + all jest stubs.\n    - Record-shape assertions at L688/L860/L903/L935 (old numbering).\n- WU3 test plan details:\n  - **L688 update**: The test \"a successful action leaves exactly one terminal record\" currently asserts `record.idempotencyKey` toBe `'ui:message-1'`. Replace with: `record.schemaVersion` toBe `2`, `record.targetRef` toMatch `/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/`, `record.keyRef` toMatch `/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/`, `JSON.stringify(record)` NOT to contain `'task-1'` or `'ui:message-1'`. Keep `attempts` toBe `1`.\n  - **Concurrent reclaim test**: `seedExecution('u1', fp, { state: 'executing', updatedAt: new Date(Date.now() - 10*60*1000).toISOString(), attempts: 1 })` (v1 base provides raw fields). `Promise.all([executeCopilotAction('u1', req), executeCopilotAction('u1', req)])` where req is a `county_confirm` proposal (live county, single candidate). Expect: one result `code: 'executed'`, one `code: 'interrupted'`; `enqueueCountyTaskIfCurrent` mock called exactly once; stored record: `state: 'succeeded'`, `attempts: 2`, `schemaVersion: 2`, `code: 'executed'`.\n  - **Concurrent fresh claim test**: no seed. Same `Promise.all` pattern. Expect: one `executed`, one `interrupted`; `store.size === 1`; record `attempts: 1`, `state: 'succeeded'`.\n  - **Identifier redaction test**: `proposal({ actionType: 'task_retry', targetId: 'victim@example.com', revision: 2 })`; `makeRequest(p)` gives `idempotencyKey: 'ui:message-1'`. Execute → `code: 'executed'`. Stored record: `schemaVersion: 2`, `targetRef` 64-hex, `keyRef` 64-hex, NO `targetId`/`idempotencyKey` property, `JSON.stringify(record)` does not contain `'victim@example.com'` or `'ui:message-1'`.\n  - **v1 legacy replay test**: `seedExecution('u1', fp, { state: 'succeeded', code: 'executed', message: 'Task task-1 retried.', action: 'task_retry' })` (v1 shape — raw fields, no schemaVersion). `executeCopilotAction` → `code: 'executed'` (replayed); `retryTask` mock NOT called.\n  - **Concurrent gate settle on crashed test**: seed a crashed record (stale `executing`). Two concurrent TAMPERED confirmations (fingerprint mismatch in request vs record). Both hit `recordGateOutcome`: A's tx sees stale → stages terminal `failed`/`tampered` → commits; B's tx sees terminal → replays the tampered result. Both return `code: 'tampered'`. Record: `state: 'failed'`, `code: 'tampered'`, `attempts: 1` (unchanged).\n  - **Emulator integration test** (`__tests__/integration/firestore/copilot-reclaim.integration.test.ts`):\n    - Mirror the `county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` pattern (emulator env, real POSTs).\n    - Seed: `upsertWatchlistItem(uid, propertyId, snapshot)` → `saveResolution(uid, propertyId, { status: 'confirmation_required', resolvedAddress, candidates: [oneCandidate], expectedRevision: 0 })`.\n    - Raw-seed a crashed execution record: compute fingerprint via imported `proposalFingerprint`; write to `users/{uid}/copilotActionExecutions/{fingerprint}` with `{ state: 'executing', updatedAt: new Date(Date.now()-10*60*1000).toISOString(), attempts: 1, ... }` using the admin SDK's `doc().set()`.\n    - Two concurrent `fetch` POSTs to `/api/copilot/proposals/execute` with the same proposal.\n    - Assert: one response `executed`, one `interrupted`; `agentTasks` count = 1 (only the enqueued county_confirm task); execution record: `state: 'succeeded'`, `attempts: 2`, `schemaVersion: 2`; `domainEvents` count incremented by 1.\n- Error/diagnostic events this session (carried forward + new):\n  - `checkpoint_notes` validation failed 6× total: \"current: must not have more than 2048 characters\" (4×) and \"blockers: must have required properties blockers\" (1×). **New**: two more failures at generation 43/44 before the compressed version at generation 44 succeeded. Learned to compress aggressively with abbreviations.\n  - Edit rejected once (earlier): \"RETRYABLE — Edit without read\" — read-before-edit guard requires a Read-tool read.\n  - **New (this turn)**: First `createFakeDb` rewrite had a TS error — `let stagedCreate/Update/Set: T | null = null` declared AFTER the `tx` object that assigns them in closures → TS CFA narrowed to `null`/`never` → 10 \"Property does not exist on type 'never'\" errors at the commit-time checks. **Fixed** by replacing with `const staged = { create: null as T | null, update: null as T | null, set: null as T | null }` declared BEFORE `tx`. LSP clean.\n  - **New (this turn)**: First jest run after harness fix — `grep -E \"Tests:|Suites:|...\"` returned no output (pattern may not have matched the jest output format in this environment); `tail -30` showed expected `failCreate`/`failFinalize` `console.error` output from the failure-injection tests but the final pass/fail summary was truncated. Need a full re-run to confirm the suite is now green.\n- Diagnostics status: `copilot-actions.ts` LSP clean (1666ms); `copilot-actions.test.ts` LSP clean (973ms) after the staged-object fix.\n- Test status snapshot (current):\n  - All WU1 suites: **green** (see Done section for exact counts).\n  - FULL unit suite (pre-WU3): **97/97 suites, 1233/1233 tests PASS**.\n  - `copilot-actions.test.ts` (post-harness-fix, pre-test-update): **unknown** — previous run showed 27/32 failing due to missing `runTransaction`; harness now has `runTransaction`; full re-run needed. The `tail -30` output showed expected failure-injection console errors but was truncated before the final summary.\n  - `__tests__/integration/firestore/recorded-documents.integration.test.ts` — 8/8 (emulator)\n  - `__tests__/integration/firestore/county-reconcile.integration.test.ts` — 3/3 (emulator)\n- Prettier status:\n  - 6 WU1 files: **PASS** (committed in `ac6ee29`)\n  - 31 other files: pre-existing drift, NOT touched this session, deferred to WU9